// Multilevel Master Listening — Part 2 (kitob + audio transkripti)
window.LISTENING_L2=[{"n":1,"title":"Video game review","dur":259.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Action takes place in: a {1}"},{"k":"p","t":"Players answer questions about: {2}"},{"k":"p","t":"Name of most difficult level of game: the {3}"},{"k":"p","t":"Best thing about the game: the {4}"},{"k":"p","t":"Maximum number of players: {5}"},{"k":"p","t":"Website for more details: www.{6}.com"}],"items":[{"a":["rainforest"],"ps":27.99,"en":33.85,"si":3,"ev":"Instead of streets and huge buildings though, you'll find yourself living in a rainforest in this game.","hl":"rainforest","uz":"Ko'chalar va ulkan binolar o'rniga, bu o'yinda o'zingizni tropik o'rmonda yashayotgandek his qilasiz.","why":"\"City\" (shahar) — oldingi o'yin Road Jam haqida, tuzoq. Sky Jam'da voqealar \"rainforest\"da kechadi."},{"a":["insects"],"ps":43.7,"en":52.83,"si":5,"ev":"You'll be asked all sorts of things regarding insects, which you have to learn on the way from the many helpful creatures you meet, such as butterflies and bats.","hl":"insects","uz":"Yo'lda sizga savollar hasharotlar haqida beriladi; ularni kapalaklar va ko'rshapalaklar kabi yordamchi jonzotlardan o'rganasiz.","why":"\"Regarding insects\" — hasharotlar haqida. Butterflies va bats — yordam beradigan jonzotlar, savol mavzusi emas."},{"a":["(the) monkey"],"ps":61.91,"en":71.77,"si":7,"ev":"I found the one called the monkey almost impossible, even though it comes well before the last level called the frog, which didn't seem so difficult.","hl":"monkey","uz":"Men \"Maymun\" deb nomlangan darajani deyarli imkonsiz deb topdim, garchi u oxirgi \"Qurbaqa\" darajasidan ancha oldin kelsa ham, qurbaqa unchalik qiyin tuyulmadi.","why":"Eng qiyin daraja — \"the monkey\". \"The frog\" oxirgi daraja, lekin u qiyin tuyulmagan."},{"a":["characters"],"ps":75.77,"en":85.25,"si":9,"ev":"The story you learn about as you continue through the game is fantastic, second only to the characters you can play who are lovely and extremely interesting too.","hl":"characters","uz":"O'yin davomida bilib boradigan hikoyangiz ajoyib, undan faqat o'ynash mumkin bo'lgan personajlar ustun — ular yoqimli va juda qiziqarli.","why":"\"Second only to the characters\" — personajlar hikoyadan ham yaxshiroq, demak eng yaxshi tomoni characters."},{"a":["six","6"],"ps":89.72,"en":98.65,"si":11,"ev":"Unfortunately, unlike the eight players who could play against each other in Road Jam, six people at the most can join in this game at any one time.","hl":"six","uz":"Afsuski, Road Jam'da sakkiz kishi bir-biriga qarshi o'ynay olgan bo'lsa, bu o'yinda bir vaqtda ko'pi bilan olti kishi qatnasha oladi.","why":"Road Jam'da 8 kishi o'ynagan (tuzoq). Bu o'yinda ko'pi bilan 6 kishi; 4 kishi esa gapiruvchiga yoqqan son."},{"a":["Lombardio"],"ps":108.02,"en":124.13,"si":14,"ev":"If you're interested, visit the company's website www.lombardio.com. I'll spell that for you. It's L-O-M-B-A-R-D-I-O.","hl":"lombardio","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, kompaniya saytiga kiring: www.lombardio.com. Harflab aytaman: L-O-M-B-A-R-D-I-O.","why":"Sayt nomi harflab aytiladi. Harflab aytilgan so'zni aynan shunday yozing."}],"segs":[{"s":5.27,"e":9.85,"t":"You will hear a student giving a review of a new video game to his class."},{"s":13.46,"e":20.0,"t":"Hi everyone! I'm going to tell you about a new video game that I've played a lot recently called Sky Jam."},{"s":20.89,"e":27.26,"t":"Produced by the same company that made Road Jam a few years ago, which was set in a city of course."},{"s":27.99,"e":33.85,"t":"Instead of streets and huge buildings though, you'll find yourself living in a rainforest in this game.","uz":"Ko'chalar va ulkan binolar o'rniga, bu o'yinda o'zingizni tropik o'rmonda yashayotgandek his qilasiz."},{"s":34.9,"e":42.91,"t":"It's an unusual game because you have to answer questions in order to make progress as well as by moving through the environment."},{"s":43.7,"e":52.83,"t":"You'll be asked all sorts of things regarding insects, which you have to learn on the way from the many helpful creatures you meet, such as butterflies and bats.","uz":"Yo'lda sizga savollar hasharotlar haqida beriladi; ularni kapalaklar va ko'rshapalaklar kabi yordamchi jonzotlardan o'rganasiz."},{"s":55.51,"e":61.18,"t":"There are 30 levels in the whole game, which are supposed to become more and more challenging as you go on."},{"s":61.91,"e":71.77,"t":"I found the one called the monkey almost impossible, even though it comes well before the last level called the frog, which didn't seem so difficult.","uz":"Men \"Maymun\" deb nomlangan darajani deyarli imkonsiz deb topdim, garchi u oxirgi \"Qurbaqa\" darajasidan ancha oldin kelsa ham, qurbaqa unchalik qiyin tuyulmadi."},{"s":72.76,"e":75.26,"t":"There are lots of things to love about this game."},{"s":75.77,"e":85.25,"t":"The story you learn about as you continue through the game is fantastic, second only to the characters you can play who are lovely and extremely interesting too.","uz":"O'yin davomida bilib boradigan hikoyangiz ajoyib, undan faqat o'ynash mumkin bo'lgan personajlar ustun — ular yoqimli va juda qiziqarli."},{"s":86.01,"e":88.86,"t":"Learning to play the game is easy and fun too."},{"s":89.72,"e":98.65,"t":"Unfortunately, unlike the eight players who could play against each other in Road Jam, six people at the most can join in this game at any one time.","uz":"Afsuski, Road Jam'da sakkiz kishi bir-biriga qarshi o'ynay olgan bo'lsa, bu o'yinda bir vaqtda ko'pi bilan olti kishi qatnasha oladi."},{"s":99.64,"e":104.03,"t":"I found this to be a few too many though, and preferred playing in a group of four."},{"s":105.05,"e":107.55,"t":"You can find out more about the game online."},{"s":108.02,"e":124.13,"t":"If you're interested, visit the company's website www.lombardio.com. I'll spell that for you. It's L-O-M-B-A-R-D-I-O.","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, kompaniya saytiga kiring: www.lombardio.com. Harflab aytaman: L-O-M-B-A-R-D-I-O."},{"s":125.11,"e":127.23,"t":"I hope you enjoyed my presentation."},{"s":127.7,"e":128.77,"t":"Thank you for listening."}]},{"n":2,"title":"School photography competition","dur":282.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The subject of this year's competition is {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Photos must show some {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"A local {3} will judge the competition."},{"k":"p","t":"First prize is a photography {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Send your entries in by 15th {5} at the latest."},{"k":"p","t":"School secretary's email address is k.{6}@school.com"}],"items":[{"a":["(the) environment"],"ps":27.42,"en":31.17,"si":4,"ev":"As you'll probably remember, last year's competition asked you to focus on the topic of travel, but photos should have something to do with the environment this time.","hl":"environment","uz":"Eslasangiz, o'tgan yilgi tanlov sayohat mavzusida edi, lekin bu safar suratlar atrof-muhitga oid bo'lishi kerak.","why":"\"Travel\" — o'tgan yilgi mavzu, tuzoq. Bu yil — environment."},{"a":["wildlife"],"ps":38.84,"en":41.63,"si":6,"ev":"We want all the pictures to have wildlife in them.","hl":"wildlife","uz":"Barcha suratlarda yovvoyi tabiat (hayvonlar, qushlar) bo'lishini xohlaymiz.","why":"Landscapes (manzaralar) yoki odamlar yetarli emas — suratda wildlife bo'lishi shart."},{"a":["writer"],"ps":64.57,"en":67.74,"si":10,"ev":"Writer James McKay has agreed to help us instead.","hl":"Writer","uz":"Uning o'rniga yozuvchi Jeyms Makkey yordam berishga rozi bo'ldi.","why":"Rassom Sally Graves kela olmaydi (tuzoq) — o'rniga writer (yozuvchi) baholaydi."},{"a":["course"],"ps":83.42,"en":89.57,"si":14,"ev":"So the organizers have decided that the winner will receive a photography course run by Central College instead.","hl":"course","uz":"Shuning uchun tashkilotchilar g'olib Central College o'tkazadigan fotografiya kursini olishiga qaror qilishdi.","why":"Kitob yoki jihozlar emas — \"photography course\"."},{"a":["February"],"ps":106.94,"en":115.65,"si":18,"ev":"If you wish to enter, please make sure we receive your photos by the 15th of February, as the judging will take place on the 19th of February.","hl":"February","uz":"Qatnashmoqchi bo'lsangiz, suratlaringiz bizga 15-fevralgacha yetib kelsin, chunki baholash 19-fevralda bo'ladi.","why":"11-mart — g'olib e'lon qilinadigan sana, 19-fevral — baholash kuni. Topshirish muddati: 15-fevral."},{"a":["Mitchell"],"ps":117.43,"en":124.41,"si":19,"ev":"If you're interested, send your entry to the school secretary, Mrs Mitchell, not to me or the head teacher.","hl":"Mitchell","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, ishingizni menga yoki direktorga emas, maktab kotibi Missis Mitchellga yuboring.","why":"Email manzili kotibning familiyasi bilan: k.mitchell@school.com. Ism harflab aytiladi — M-I-T-C-H-E-L-L."}],"segs":[{"s":5.37,"e":9.69,"t":"You will hear a teacher giving some information about a school photography competition."},{"s":13.18,"e":14.33,"t":"Listen, everyone."},{"s":15.32,"e":19.39,"t":"I've got some information about this year's school photography competition."},{"s":20.5,"e":26.72,"t":"As you'll probably remember, last year's competition asked you to focus on the topic of travel."},{"s":27.42,"e":31.17,"t":"As you'll probably remember, last year's competition asked you to focus on the topic of travel, but photos should have something to do with the environment this time.","uz":"Eslasangiz, o'tgan yilgi tanlov sayohat mavzusida edi, lekin bu safar suratlar atrof-muhitga oid bo'lishi kerak."},{"s":33.02,"e":38.05,"t":"As in previous years, there are certain things that we want the photographs to include."},{"s":38.84,"e":41.63,"t":"We want all the pictures to have wildlife in them.","uz":"Barcha suratlarda yovvoyi tabiat (hayvonlar, qushlar) bo'lishini xohlaymiz."},{"s":42.23,"e":46.4,"t":"So we're not looking for photos that only show landscapes or people."},{"s":48.92,"e":55.17,"t":"The head teacher has decided to ask someone from outside the school to judge the competition this year."},{"s":56.15,"e":63.36,"t":"She was hoping that local artist Sally Graves would be able to judge the entries, but she's actually away at that time."},{"s":64.57,"e":67.74,"t":"Writer James McKay has agreed to help us instead.","uz":"Uning o'rniga yozuvchi Jeyms Makkey yordam berishga rozi bo'ldi."},{"s":68.73,"e":71.84,"t":"I'm sure many of you have heard of him as he's quite famous"},{"s":72.28,"e":74.56,"t":"and was born not far away from here too."},{"s":76.7,"e":82.91,"t":"It was felt that most keen photographers already have the photography books or equipment they need."},{"s":83.42,"e":89.57,"t":"So the organizers have decided that the winner will receive a photography course run by Central College instead.","uz":"Shuning uchun tashkilotchilar g'olib Central College o'tkazadigan fotografiya kursini olishiga qaror qilishdi."},{"s":90.3,"e":96.89,"t":"College was also hoping to have a small photography exhibition for winners of all the school photography competitions in the area."},{"s":97.75,"e":100.8,"t":"but their gallery is too busy putting on other shows, I'm afraid."},{"s":102.65,"e":106.3,"t":"The winner of the competition will be announced on the 11th of March."},{"s":106.94,"e":115.65,"t":"If you wish to enter, please make sure we receive your photos by the 15th of February, as the judging will take place on the 19th of February.","uz":"Qatnashmoqchi bo'lsangiz, suratlaringiz bizga 15-fevralgacha yetib kelsin, chunki baholash 19-fevralda bo'ladi."},{"s":117.43,"e":124.41,"t":"If you're interested, send your entry to the school secretary, Mrs Mitchell, not to me or the head teacher.","uz":"Qiziqsangiz, ishingizni menga yoki direktorga emas, maktab kotibi Missis Mitchellga yuboring."},{"s":125.37,"e":126.91,"t":"I'll give you her email address."},{"s":127.35,"e":129.85,"t":"It's K.Mitchell."},{"s":130.58,"e":132.19,"t":"that spelt, M."},{"s":132.63,"e":136.67,"t":"I T C H E double L."},{"s":137.3,"e":139.04,"t":"school.com"},{"s":139.93,"e":140.32,"t":"Good luck"}]},{"n":3,"title":"My acting club","dur":245.4,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Teacher:"},{"k":"p","t":"Appeared on TV as a {1}"},{"k":"p","t":"Has mostly appeared in {2} shows"},{"k":"h","t":"Sessions:"},{"k":"p","t":"First part – using your {3} well"},{"k":"p","t":"Second part – practising performance skills"},{"k":"p","t":"Take place at the {4}"},{"k":"h","t":"Acting Club play:"},{"k":"p","t":"Called {5}"},{"k":"p","t":"First performance – on 20th {6}"}],"items":[{"a":["farmer"],"ps":33.46,"en":41.5,"si":5,"ev":"She plays a policewoman in that, but you'll probably know her better as the farmer in the series Green Valley that was on last year.","hl":"farmer","uz":"U o'sha spektaklda politsiyachi ayolni o'ynaydi, lekin uni ko'proq o'tgan yili efirga uzatilgan Green Valley serialidagi fermer rolidan bilsangiz kerak.","why":"\"Policewoman\" — teatrdagi roli. Televizorda esa \"farmer\" bo'lib chiqqan."},{"a":["comedy"],"ps":46.65,"en":57.31,"si":7,"ev":"…as well as having three years' experience of appearing in serious drama, she's also spent 7 years working in comedy productions, so she has lots of different talents.","hl":"comedy","uz":"Jiddiy dramada uch yillik tajribasidan tashqari, u yana 7 yil komediya spektakllarida ishlagan, shuning uchun turli iste'dodlarga ega.","why":"Jiddiy dramada 3 yil, komediyada 7 yil — demak, asosan comedy."},{"a":["voice"],"ps":67.83,"en":71.77,"si":10,"ev":"In the first part, rather than practicing anything to do with movement of the body, we focus instead on improving how to control the voice as an actor.","hl":"voice","uz":"Birinchi qismda tana harakatlarini emas, aktyor sifatida ovozni boshqarishni yaxshilashga e'tibor beramiz.","why":"\"Movement of the body\" — rad etilgan variant. Birinchi qism — voice (ovoz)."},{"a":["university"],"ps":82.78,"en":86.21,"si":13,"ev":"The club actually hires a room from the university to run the classes.","hl":"university","uz":"Klub darslar uchun aslida universitetdan xona ijaraga oladi.","why":"College va acting school — tilga olinadi, lekin darslar universitetda."},{"a":["(the) passenger"],"ps":99.74,"en":101.79,"si":17,"ev":"Its name is The Passenger.","hl":"Passenger","uz":"Uning nomi — \"The Passenger\" (Yo'lovchi).","why":"\"Reality\" — klubning oldingi spektakli, tuzoq."},{"a":["July"],"ps":112.73,"en":121.21,"si":20,"ev":"We've got our last practice for the new play on the 13th of July, with audiences able to come and see it from the 20th of July for one week.","hl":"July","uz":"Yangi spektakl bo'yicha oxirgi mashg'ulotimiz 13-iyulda, tomoshabinlar esa uni 20-iyuldan boshlab bir hafta davomida ko'rishlari mumkin.","why":"13-iyul — oxirgi mashg'ulot (tuzoq). Birinchi tomosha — 20-iyul."}],"segs":[{"s":6.42,"e":12.32,"t":"You will hear a student giving some information to his class about an acting club he's a member of."},{"s":15.19,"e":20.13,"t":"Hello everyone, I'd like to tell you about this wonderful acting club I joined recently"},{"s":21.02,"e":22.88,"t":"Best thing about it is the teacher."},{"s":23.48,"e":27.04,"t":"We're really lucky to have someone who's actually quite famous."},{"s":27.54,"e":32.8,"t":"Her name's Alice Fisher and she's appearing in a play at the big theatre in town at the moment."},{"s":33.46,"e":41.5,"t":"She plays a policewoman in that, but you'll probably know her better as the farmer in the series Green Valley that was on last year.","uz":"U o'sha spektaklda politsiyachi ayolni o'ynaydi, lekin uni ko'proq o'tgan yili efirga uzatilgan Green Valley serialidagi fermer rolidan bilsangiz kerak."},{"s":42.33,"e":45.98,"t":"She's worked as a professional theatre actor for about 10 years."},{"s":46.65,"e":57.31,"t":"…as well as having three years' experience of appearing in serious drama, she's also spent 7 years working in comedy productions, so she has lots of different talents.","uz":"Jiddiy dramada uch yillik tajribasidan tashqari, u yana 7 yil komediya spektakllarida ishlagan, shuning uchun turli iste'dodlarga ega."},{"s":58.2,"e":61.82,"t":"The sessions are always fun and are split into two sections."},{"s":62.42,"e":66.85,"t":"In the first part, rather than practicing anything to do with movement of the body,"},{"s":67.83,"e":71.77,"t":"In the first part, rather than practicing anything to do with movement of the body, we focus instead on improving how to control the voice as an actor.","uz":"Birinchi qismda tana harakatlarini emas, aktyor sifatida ovozni boshqarishni yaxshilashga e'tibor beramiz."},{"s":72.66,"e":76.03,"t":"And the second part, we practice our performance skills."},{"s":76.89,"e":81.5,"t":"If you're interested in coming to the drama club, you'll need to know where to come of course."},{"s":82.78,"e":86.21,"t":"The club actually hires a room from the university to run the classes.","uz":"Klub darslar uchun aslida universitetdan xona ijaraga oladi."},{"s":86.71,"e":90.85,"t":"It's much cheaper to do it there than at the college or the acting school."},{"s":91.35,"e":93.44,"t":"The sessions are on Wednesday evenings."},{"s":94.3,"e":99.07,"t":"At the moment we're practicing for a play which will be on at the Town Theatre soon."},{"s":99.74,"e":101.79,"t":"Its name is The Passenger.","uz":"Uning nomi — \"The Passenger\" (Yo'lovchi)."},{"s":102.23,"e":108.83,"t":"And we're hoping that this latest one will be as popular as the last production the club did, which was called 'Reality'."},{"s":109.53,"e":111.49,"t":"It was a big success apparently."},{"s":112.73,"e":121.21,"t":"We've got our last practice for the new play on the 13th of July, with audiences able to come and see it from the 20th of July for one week.","uz":"Yangi spektakl bo'yicha oxirgi mashg'ulotimiz 13-iyulda, tomoshabinlar esa uni 20-iyuldan boshlab bir hafta davomida ko'rishlari mumkin."},{"s":121.88,"e":122.78,"t":"Thanks for listening."}]},{"n":4,"title":"Science museum visit","dur":270.1,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Matilde's favourite room contained displays about {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The {2} exhibition is currently closed."},{"k":"p","t":"Matilde made a {3} at the museum."},{"k":"p","t":"The shop had a really good range of {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"The guided tour lasts for {5} minutes."},{"k":"p","t":"Visitors must use the entrance on {6} Road."}],"items":[{"a":["energy"],"ps":31.64,"en":41.21,"si":4,"ev":"We spent ages looking around the room that was all about space, and even longer in the one with loads of stuff on energy, which I thought was the best bit.","hl":"energy","uz":"Kosmosga bag'ishlangan xonani uzoq aylandik, energiyaga oid narsalar ko'p bo'lgan xonada esa undan ham ko'proq vaqt o'tkazdik — menimcha, eng zo'r joyi shu edi.","why":"\"Space\" xonasi ham yoqqan, lekin \"the best bit\" — energy xonasi."},{"a":["health"],"ps":44.92,"en":54.94,"si":6,"ev":"But there are also two special exhibitions that you have to pay for. You can't go into the one on health yet because it doesn't open for another couple of weeks.","hl":"health","uz":"Pullik ikkita maxsus ko'rgazma ham bor. Sog'liqqa oid ko'rgazmaga hozircha kira olmaysiz, chunki u yana ikki haftadan keyin ochiladi.","why":"\"Doesn't open for another couple of weeks\" — hozir yopiq. Demak, health ko'rgazmasi."},{"a":["rocket"],"ps":69.66,"en":79.77,"si":10,"ev":"My brother made this fantastic car that went quite fast, using only power from the sun. I created a rocket that used gas to fly.","hl":"rocket","uz":"Akam faqat quyosh energiyasida ancha tez yuradigan ajoyib mashina yasadi. Men esa gaz yordamida uchadigan raketa yasadim.","why":"Car — akasi yasagan (tuzoq). Matilde o'zi — rocket."},{"a":["chemistry"],"ps":93.69,"en":99.45,"si":14,"ev":"There were so many chemistry sets to choose from. It took me ages to decide which one I wanted.","hl":"chemistry","uz":"Juda ko'p kimyo to'plamlari bor edi, qaysi birini tanlashga ancha vaqt ketdi.","why":"\"So many chemistry sets\" — tanlov katta. Oddiy o'yinchoqlar ham bor, lekin \"good range\" — chemistry."},{"a":["80","eighty"],"ps":110.07,"en":119.2,"si":18,"ev":"When we arrived, they said we'd have to wait for at least 60 minutes for the 80-minute tour because it was so popular. So we decided against it.","hl":"80","uz":"Kelganimizda, juda mashhur bo'lgani uchun 80 daqiqalik ekskursiyaga kamida 60 daqiqa kutishimiz kerakligini aytishdi, shuning uchun bormaslikka qaror qildik.","why":"60 daqiqa — kutish vaqti (tuzoq). Ekskursiya davomiyligi — 80 daqiqa."},{"a":["Lockhart"],"ps":120.76,"en":133.53,"si":19,"ev":"If you want to go, the entrance is on Lockhart Road. Spelled out for you, it's L-O-C-K-H-A-R-T Road.","hl":"Lockhart","uz":"Bormoqchi bo'lsangiz, kirish Lockhart ko'chasida. Harflab aytaman: L-O-C-K-H-A-R-T.","why":"Harflab aytilgan nom — har bir harfni diqqat bilan yozing."}],"segs":[{"s":5.11,"e":11.71,"t":"You will hear a student called Mathilde giving a presentation to her class about a science museum she visited."},{"s":14.42,"e":19.9,"t":"Hi everyone! I'm going to tell you about my trip to the new science museum last week."},{"s":20.63,"e":24.29,"t":"I went with my family and we looked around the whole museum."},{"s":25.21,"e":30.69,"t":"There are loads of different rooms and each one contains displays about a particular topic."},{"s":31.64,"e":41.21,"t":"We spent ages looking around the room that was all about space, and even longer in the one with loads of stuff on energy, which I thought was the best bit.","uz":"Kosmosga bag'ishlangan xonani uzoq aylandik, energiyaga oid narsalar ko'p bo'lgan xonada esa undan ham ko'proq vaqt o'tkazdik — menimcha, eng zo'r joyi shu edi."},{"s":43.0,"e":44.35,"t":"The museum's free!"},{"s":44.92,"e":54.94,"t":"But there are also two special exhibitions that you have to pay for. You can't go into the one on health yet because it doesn't open for another couple of weeks.","uz":"Pullik ikkita maxsus ko'rgazma ham bor. Sog'liqqa oid ko'rgazmaga hozircha kira olmaysiz, chunki u yana ikki haftadan keyin ochiladi."},{"s":55.8,"e":57.73,"t":"I'd like to go back and see that."},{"s":59.1,"e":62.3,"t":"The other exhibition on computers was good though."},{"s":64.22,"e":68.73,"t":"As well as the displays, there are lots of things you can actually do there too."},{"s":69.66,"e":79.77,"t":"My brother made this fantastic car that went quite fast, using only power from the sun. I created a rocket that used gas to fly.","uz":"Akam faqat quyosh energiyasida ancha tez yuradigan ajoyib mashina yasadi. Men esa gaz yordamida uchadigan raketa yasadim."},{"s":80.47,"e":82.05,"t":"It went really high."},{"s":83.67,"e":87.52,"t":"As well as the interesting things to see and do, there's a nice shot."},{"s":88.66,"e":91.9,"t":"My mum and dad let me get something because it was my birthday."},{"s":93.69,"e":99.45,"t":"There were so many chemistry sets to choose from. It took me ages to decide which one I wanted.","uz":"Juda ko'p kimyo to'plamlari bor edi, qaysi birini tanlashga ancha vaqt ketdi."},{"s":100.47,"e":102.37,"t":"They have the usual toys and games."},{"s":102.9,"e":104.7,"t":"and a few nice books there too."},{"s":106.49,"e":109.5,"t":"You can also take a tour of the museum with a guide."},{"s":110.07,"e":119.2,"t":"When we arrived, they said we'd have to wait for at least 60 minutes for the 80-minute tour because it was so popular. So we decided against it.","uz":"Kelganimizda, juda mashhur bo'lgani uchun 80 daqiqalik ekskursiyaga kamida 60 daqiqa kutishimiz kerakligini aytishdi, shuning uchun bormaslikka qaror qildik."},{"s":120.76,"e":133.53,"t":"If you want to go, the entrance is on Lockhart Road. Spelled out for you, it's L-O-C-K-H-A-R-T Road.","uz":"Bormoqchi bo'lsangiz, kirish Lockhart ko'chasida. Harflab aytaman: L-O-C-K-H-A-R-T."},{"s":134.62,"e":135.71,"t":"Thanks for listening!"}]},{"n":5,"title":"School trip to farm","dur":268.1,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Meeting place","t":"8 a.m. next to the school {1}"},{"k":"row","l":"Need to bring","t":"a {2}"},{"k":"row","l":"Morning activity","t":"feeding the {3}"},{"k":"row","l":"Afternoon activity","t":"{4} wall"},{"k":"row","l":"Return to school at","t":"{5}"},{"k":"row","l":"For more information","t":"www.{6}.farm.com"}],"items":[{"a":["gate"],"ps":20.76,"en":30.53,"si":3,"ev":"As I told you last week, you need to wait for the bus by the school gate. Don't go to the bus stop or come straight into the playground like you usually do.","hl":"gate","uz":"O'tgan hafta aytganimdek, avtobusni maktab darvozasi oldida kutishingiz kerak. Bekatga bormang va odatdagidek to'g'ri hovliga kirmang.","why":"Bus stop va playground — rad etilgan joylar. To'g'ri javob — gate."},{"a":["drink"],"ps":32.15,"en":45.09,"si":4,"ev":"The farm is providing us all with a nice packed lunch, so there's no need to bring one yourself. It'd be great if you could make sure you've got a drink though, as it can get quite hot on the bus.","hl":"drink","uz":"Ferma hammamizga tushlik beradi, shuning uchun o'zingiz olib kelishingiz shart emas. Lekin ichimlik olishni unutmang, avtobusda ancha issiq bo'lishi mumkin.","why":"Lunch olib kelish shart emas (tuzoq). Olib kelish kerak — a drink."},{"a":["lambs"],"ps":49.59,"en":62.75,"si":6,"ev":"You're all going to have a go at brushing the horses just after we arrive there at about 9am. Shortly after this, you'll learn what farmers give lambs to eat, and you'll be able to give them their breakfast too.","hl":"lambs","uz":"Soat 9 larda yetib borgach, otlarni tarab ko'rasiz. Shundan keyin fermerlar qo'zichoqlarga nima berishini o'rganasiz va ularga nonushta ham berasiz.","why":"Otlarni faqat tarashadi (brushing). Ovqatlantirish — lambs (qo'zichoqlar)."},{"a":["climbing"],"ps":70.55,"en":81.6,"si":9,"ev":"We're going to do some climbing on the special wall they have there after lunch. And maybe next time we can try one of the other activities like fishing or playing baseball.","hl":"climbing","uz":"Tushlikdan keyin maxsus devorda toqqa chiqish mashg'ulotini qilamiz. Keyingi safar baliq ovlash yoki beysbol kabi boshqa mashg'ulotlarni sinab ko'rarmiz.","why":"Fishing va baseball — \"next time\". Tushdan keyin — climbing wall."},{"a":["4.15"],"ps":83.22,"en":94.75,"si":10,"ev":"We'll be setting off back to school at about 3.30pm and we'll be back here at 4.15. So, 45 minutes after the usual school finish time of 3.30.","hl":"4.15","uz":"Maktabga soat 15:30 da yo'lga chiqamiz va bu yerga 16:15 da qaytamiz — ya'ni odatdagi dars tugash vaqti 15:30 dan 45 daqiqa keyin.","why":"3.30 — jo'nash vaqti (tuzoq). Maktabga qaytish — 4.15."},{"a":["Caffertys","Cafferty's"],"ps":116.31,"en":132.06,"si":14,"ev":"It's www.caffertys.farm.com. I'll spell that for you. It's C-A-F-F-E-R-T-Y-S.","hl":"caffertys","uz":"Manzil: www.caffertys.farm.com. Harflab aytaman: C-A-F-F-E-R-T-Y-S.","why":"\"Double F\" — ikkita F. Harflab aytilgan so'zni harfma-harf yozing."}],"segs":[{"s":5.88,"e":11.1,"t":"You will hear a teacher giving his students information about a school trip to a farm."},{"s":14.42,"e":15.55,"t":"Good morning everyone."},{"s":16.7,"e":19.77,"t":"I'm going to tell you about the school trip to the farm tomorrow."},{"s":20.76,"e":30.53,"t":"As I told you last week, you need to wait for the bus by the school gate. Don't go to the bus stop or come straight into the playground like you usually do.","uz":"O'tgan hafta aytganimdek, avtobusni maktab darvozasi oldida kutishingiz kerak. Bekatga bormang va odatdagidek to'g'ri hovliga kirmang."},{"s":32.15,"e":45.09,"t":"The farm is providing us all with a nice packed lunch, so there's no need to bring one yourself. It'd be great if you could make sure you've got a drink though, as it can get quite hot on the bus.","uz":"Ferma hammamizga tushlik beradi, shuning uchun o'zingiz olib kelishingiz shart emas. Lekin ichimlik olishni unutmang, avtobusda ancha issiq bo'lishi mumkin."},{"s":46.58,"e":48.8,"t":"There are lots of different animals on the farm."},{"s":49.59,"e":62.75,"t":"You're all going to have a go at brushing the horses just after we arrive there at about 9am. Shortly after this, you'll learn what farmers give lambs to eat, and you'll be able to give them their breakfast too.","uz":"Soat 9 larda yetib borgach, otlarni tarab ko'rasiz. Shundan keyin fermerlar qo'zichoqlarga nima berishini o'rganasiz va ularga nonushta ham berasiz."},{"s":64.15,"e":65.44,"t":"as well as the animals."},{"s":65.88,"e":69.37,"t":"The farm has lots of activities students can take part in."},{"s":70.55,"e":81.6,"t":"We're going to do some climbing on the special wall they have there after lunch. And maybe next time we can try one of the other activities like fishing or playing baseball.","uz":"Tushlikdan keyin maxsus devorda toqqa chiqish mashg'ulotini qilamiz. Keyingi safar baliq ovlash yoki beysbol kabi boshqa mashg'ulotlarni sinab ko'rarmiz."},{"s":83.22,"e":94.75,"t":"We'll be setting off back to school at about 3.30pm and we'll be back here at 4.15. So, 45 minutes after the usual school finish time of 3.30.","uz":"Maktabga soat 15:30 da yo'lga chiqamiz va bu yerga 16:15 da qaytamiz — ya'ni odatdagi dars tugash vaqti 15:30 dan 45 daqiqa keyin."},{"s":96.06,"e":101.34,"t":"Please could you let your parents know, especially if they usually come to the school to pick you up."},{"s":103.19,"e":112.8,"t":"If you or your parents want to find out more about the farm before we go, you can visit their website and there's loads of information about it on there."},{"s":113.75,"e":115.52,"t":"I'll give you the website address."},{"s":116.31,"e":132.06,"t":"It's www.caffertys.farm.com. I'll spell that for you. It's C-A-F-F-E-R-T-Y-S.","uz":"Manzil: www.caffertys.farm.com. Harflab aytaman: C-A-F-F-E-R-T-Y-S."},{"s":133.02,"e":133.6,"t":"Okay."},{"s":134.14,"e":135.07,"t":"See you all tomorrow."}]},{"n":6,"title":"Saturday music classes","dur":297.0,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Classes available"},{"k":"li","t":"drums"},{"k":"li","t":"{1}"},{"k":"li","t":"guitar"},{"k":"h","t":"On arrival"},{"k":"li","t":"go to the {2} room to pick up your instrument"},{"k":"h","t":"Cost"},{"k":"li","t":"£{3} per class"},{"k":"h","t":"End-of-term concert"},{"k":"li","t":"on {4}"},{"k":"li","t":"play alone or with the {5}"},{"k":"li","t":"friends and family welcome"},{"k":"h","t":"For more information"},{"k":"li","t":"contact music teacher on {6}@school.net"}],"items":[{"a":["flute"],"ps":36.15,"en":45.41,"si":6,"ev":"The violin teacher the school usually uses can't make it on Saturdays, but why not have a go at the flute if you prefer classical music.","hl":"flute","uz":"Maktabning skripka o'qituvchisi shanba kunlari kela olmaydi, lekin klassik musiqani yoqtirsangiz, nay chalib ko'ring.","why":"Violin darsi bo'lmaydi (tuzoq). Mavjud dars — flute."},{"a":["drama"],"ps":51.8,"en":63.13,"si":8,"ev":"You probably know that these are normally kept in the large cupboard next to the technology room. But we'll make sure they're all ready for you in the drama room. So go straight there, please.","hl":"drama","uz":"Bilsangiz kerak, ular odatda texnologiya xonasi yonidagi katta shkafda turadi. Lekin hammasini siz uchun drama xonasida tayyorlab qo'yamiz, to'g'ri o'sha yerga boring.","why":"Technology room — odatdagi joy (tuzoq). Shanba kuni — drama room."},{"a":["7.75"],"ps":71.29,"en":83.71,"si":11,"ev":"If they decide to pay for each individual class, it'll be £7.75, or they can pay per term, in which case it works out a little cheaper at 72 pounds.","hl":"7.75","uz":"Har bir dars uchun alohida to'lasa — 7,75 funt, yoki chorak uchun to'lasa, biroz arzonroq — 72 funt bo'ladi.","why":"\"Per class\" — har bir dars uchun: 7.75. 72 funt — butun chorak uchun."},{"a":["24th June","June 24th","24 June"],"ps":85.34,"en":95.87,"si":12,"ev":"There'll be an end of term concert for all students, which will take place on the 24th of June and not on the 7th of July as it says on the school website.","hl":"24th of June","uz":"Barcha o'quvchilar uchun chorak oxiri konserti bo'ladi — u maktab saytida yozilganidek 7-iyulda emas, 24-iyunda o'tadi.","why":"7-iyul — saytdagi xato sana (tuzoq). Konsert — 24-iyun."},{"a":["orchestra"],"ps":102.39,"en":115.87,"si":15,"ev":"Last year, there were several students who joined together in a band and they played together at the concert. This year though, we'd like to include more people and have an orchestra that students can play in.","hl":"orchestra","uz":"O'tgan yili bir necha o'quvchi guruh tuzib, konsertda birga chalishgan. Bu yil esa ko'proq odamni qamrab olib, orkestr tuzmoqchimiz.","why":"Band — o'tgan yili (tuzoq). Bu yil — orchestra."},{"a":["Driscoll"],"ps":120.5,"en":135.97,"si":17,"ev":"If you or your parents want more information, you'll need to email Mr Driscoll, the music teacher, on driscoll@school.net. I'll spell that for you. It's D-R-I-S-C-O-L-L.","hl":"Driscoll","uz":"Ko'proq ma'lumot kerak bo'lsa, musiqa o'qituvchisi janob Driskollga driscoll@school.net manziliga yozing. Harflab: D-R-I-S-C-O-L-L.","why":"Ikkita L bilan tugaydi — harflab aytilganiga e'tibor bering."}],"segs":[{"s":5.53,"e":11.29,"t":"You will hear a music teacher giving some information to students about Saturday music classes."},{"s":14.14,"e":15.29,"t":"Listen, everyone."},{"s":15.93,"e":20.29,"t":"I know some of you are interested in learning to play a musical instrument"},{"s":20.76,"e":26.33,"t":"So I have some information about Saturday morning music classes that are starting this week."},{"s":27.51,"e":31.65,"t":"There are many classes to choose from for a range of different instruments."},{"s":32.41,"e":35.13,"t":"You can learn anything from the drums to the guitar."},{"s":36.15,"e":45.41,"t":"The violin teacher the school usually uses can't make it on Saturdays, but why not have a go at the flute if you prefer classical music.","uz":"Maktabning skripka o'qituvchisi shanba kunlari kela olmaydi, lekin klassik musiqani yoqtirsangiz, nay chalib ko'ring."},{"s":46.97,"e":50.88,"t":"When you arrive at the school, you'll need to collect your instruments."},{"s":51.8,"e":63.13,"t":"You probably know that these are normally kept in the large cupboard next to the technology room. But we'll make sure they're all ready for you in the drama room. So go straight there, please.","uz":"Bilsangiz kerak, ular odatda texnologiya xonasi yonidagi katta shkafda turadi. Lekin hammasini siz uchun drama xonasida tayyorlab qo'yamiz, to'g'ri o'sha yerga boring."},{"s":65.02,"e":68.0,"t":"You'll need to tell your parents about the cost, of course."},{"s":68.57,"e":70.62,"t":"They can pay in two different ways."},{"s":71.29,"e":83.71,"t":"If they decide to pay for each individual class, it'll be £7.75, or they can pay per term, in which case it works out a little cheaper at 72 pounds.","uz":"Har bir dars uchun alohida to'lasa — 7,75 funt, yoki chorak uchun to'lasa, biroz arzonroq — 72 funt bo'ladi."},{"s":85.34,"e":95.87,"t":"There'll be an end of term concert for all students, which will take place on the 24th of June and not on the 7th of July as it says on the school website.","uz":"Barcha o'quvchilar uchun chorak oxiri konserti bo'ladi — u maktab saytida yozilganidek 7-iyulda emas, 24-iyunda o'tadi."},{"s":96.79,"e":98.62,"t":"you'll be able to play solo."},{"s":99.06,"e":101.44,"t":"That's by yourself, all with others."},{"s":102.39,"e":115.87,"t":"Last year, there were several students who joined together in a band and they played together at the concert. This year though, we'd like to include more people and have an orchestra that students can play in.","uz":"O'tgan yili bir necha o'quvchi guruh tuzib, konsertda birga chalishgan. Bu yil esa ko'proq odamni qamrab olib, orkestr tuzmoqchimiz."},{"s":116.82,"e":119.23,"t":"Family and friends are welcome to come and listen."},{"s":120.5,"e":135.97,"t":"If you or your parents want more information, you'll need to email Mr Driscoll, the music teacher, on driscoll@school.net. I'll spell that for you. It's D-R-I-S-C-O-L-L.","uz":"Ko'proq ma'lumot kerak bo'lsa, musiqa o'qituvchisi janob Driskollga driscoll@school.net manziliga yozing. Harflab: D-R-I-S-C-O-L-L."},{"s":137.02,"e":137.66,"t":"I"},{"s":138.68,"e":139.39,"t":"S"},{"s":140.95,"e":141.47,"t":"C"},{"s":142.87,"e":143.39,"t":"Oh?"},{"s":144.92,"e":145.89,"t":"Double L."},{"s":147.45,"e":148.99,"t":"school.net"}]},{"n":7,"title":"How to help the environment","dur":259.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Remember that when we're {1} we always have the choice to buy something somewhere else."},{"k":"p","t":"Take plastic {2} with you the next time you go shopping."},{"k":"p","t":"Recycle unwanted things by giving them to {3} shops."},{"k":"p","t":"See how you might be able to help with {4} problems where you live."},{"k":"p","t":"Ask your friends to help you clear rubbish and litter from {5} and streets in your area."},{"k":"p","t":"Try car-sharing with your {6} if you work in the same area."}],"items":[{"a":["shopping"],"ps":22.23,"en":32.54,"si":3,"ev":"We often forget that as people who go shopping, we have a lot of power. If one company does something we don't like, we can always shop somewhere else.","hl":"shopping","uz":"Xarid qiluvchilar sifatida katta kuchga ega ekanimizni ko'pincha unutamiz. Biror kompaniya yoqmaydigan ish qilsa, doim boshqa joydan xarid qilishimiz mumkin.","why":"\"People who go shopping\" — xarid qilayotganimizda (when we're shopping)."},{"a":["bags"],"ps":41.85,"en":56.51,"si":6,"ev":"And if you're offered a bag and you don't need one, just say no thanks. And any plastic bags you have at home, don't throw them away. Put them away somewhere until your next shopping trip and use them then.","hl":"bags","uz":"Sizga paket taklif qilinsa va kerak bo'lmasa, shunchaki \"yo'q, rahmat\" deng. Uydagi plastik paketlarni esa tashlamang — keyingi xaridgacha olib qo'yib, o'shanda ishlating.","why":"Plastic bags — keyingi xaridga olib boring."},{"a":["charity"],"ps":63.96,"en":70.85,"si":8,"ev":"There are always charity shops which are very happy to help you recycle your old clothes or things in the house.","hl":"charity","uz":"Har doim xayriya do'konlari bor — ular eski kiyim yoki uy-ro'zg'or buyumlaringizni qayta ishlatishga bajonidil yordam beradi.","why":"\"Charity shops\" — xayriya do'konlari."},{"a":["environmental"],"ps":88.86,"en":94.05,"si":12,"ev":"Find out what some of the local environmental problems are and see how you can help.","hl":"environmental","uz":"Mahallangizdagi ekologik muammolar nimaligini bilib oling va qanday yordam bera olishingizni ko'ring.","why":"\"Local environmental problems\" — yashash joyingizdagi ekologik muammolar."},{"a":["rivers"],"ps":94.81,"en":104.8,"si":13,"ev":"Get together with friends and help to clear the rubbish from local rivers or collect litter from the streets around your home to keep the area looking tidy.","hl":"rivers","uz":"Do'stlar bilan birga mahalliy daryolardagi axlatni tozalang yoki uyingiz atrofidagi ko'chalardan chiqindilarni yig'ing.","why":"\"Rivers and streets\" — daryolar va ko'chalar."},{"a":["neighbour"],"ps":116.25,"en":129.6,"si":16,"ev":"But we should all try to avoid making unnecessary car journeys. Go by bike or public transport sometimes, or if you work in the same area as your neighbour, try car sharing!","hl":"neighbour","uz":"Keraksiz avtomobil safarlaridan qochishga harakat qilishimiz kerak. Ba'zan velosiped yoki jamoat transportida yuring, qo'shningiz bilan bir hududda ishlasangiz — bitta mashinada boring!","why":"Car-sharing — qo'shni (neighbour) bilan."}],"segs":[{"s":3.83,"e":10.46,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter called Erica talking about how we can help the environment."},{"s":12.18,"e":18.01,"t":"This morning we're continuing to look at environmental problems to see what we can do to help."},{"s":18.52,"e":21.6,"t":"and we can make a difference if we try."},{"s":22.23,"e":32.54,"t":"We often forget that as people who go shopping, we have a lot of power. If one company does something we don't like, we can always shop somewhere else.","uz":"Xarid qiluvchilar sifatida katta kuchga ega ekanimizni ko'pincha unutamiz. Biror kompaniya yoqmaydigan ish qilsa, doim boshqa joydan xarid qilishimiz mumkin."},{"s":33.66,"e":37.95,"t":"Then there's the amount of plastic that comes with the goods we buy."},{"s":38.9,"e":41.31,"t":"Try buying things that aren't wrapped in it."},{"s":41.85,"e":56.51,"t":"And if you're offered a bag and you don't need one, just say no thanks. And any plastic bags you have at home, don't throw them away. Put them away somewhere until your next shopping trip and use them then.","uz":"Sizga paket taklif qilinsa va kerak bo'lmasa, shunchaki \"yo'q, rahmat\" deng. Uydagi plastik paketlarni esa tashlamang — keyingi xaridgacha olib qo'yib, o'shanda ishlating."},{"s":57.78,"e":63.39,"t":"On the subject of throwing stuff away, I try to keep things that other people might be able to use."},{"s":63.96,"e":70.85,"t":"There are always charity shops which are very happy to help you recycle your old clothes or things in the house.","uz":"Har doim xayriya do'konlari bor — ular eski kiyim yoki uy-ro'zg'or buyumlaringizni qayta ishlatishga bajonidil yordam beradi."},{"s":71.67,"e":77.15,"t":"Knowing that someone else is getting pleasure from something you no longer need is a lovely feeling."},{"s":78.39,"e":86.27,"t":"Evolution is of course a big problem and we often feel that as individuals we have no power to make any difference."},{"s":87.06,"e":88.13,"t":"It's not true."},{"s":88.86,"e":94.05,"t":"Find out what some of the local environmental problems are and see how you can help.","uz":"Mahallangizdagi ekologik muammolar nimaligini bilib oling va qanday yordam bera olishingizni ko'ring."},{"s":94.81,"e":104.8,"t":"Get together with friends and help to clear the rubbish from local rivers or collect litter from the streets around your home to keep the area looking tidy.","uz":"Do'stlar bilan birga mahalliy daryolardagi axlatni tozalang yoki uyingiz atrofidagi ko'chalardan chiqindilarni yig'ing."},{"s":106.26,"e":108.51,"t":"Finally, let's turn to energy."},{"s":109.34,"e":115.65,"t":"Cars are here to stay for the moment and it would be difficult to ask people not to use them at all."},{"s":116.25,"e":129.6,"t":"But we should all try to avoid making unnecessary car journeys. Go by bike or public transport sometimes, or if you work in the same area as your neighbour, try car sharing!","uz":"Keraksiz avtomobil safarlaridan qochishga harakat qilishimiz kerak. Ba'zan velosiped yoki jamoat transportida yuring, qo'shningiz bilan bir hududda ishlasangiz — bitta mashinada boring!"},{"s":130.17,"e":132.64,"t":"Take it in turns to drive to work."}]},{"n":8,"title":"Radio Programmes","dur":308.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"There are {1} to some of our programmes this week."},{"k":"p","t":"The wildlife documentary looks at wild {2} and how to identify them."},{"k":"p","t":"In Writers' World, discover how to get your work {3} by using the web."},{"k":"p","t":"On Sports Night, there will be no discussions on last week's matches as they were {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Join Sally at the new time of {5} to ask questions on Money Matters."},{"k":"p","t":"You'll find Sally at the entrance to the {6} on Friday."}],"items":[{"a":["changes"],"ps":25.43,"en":34.62,"si":2,"ev":"There are a few changes to our regular programs, so listen carefully to make sure you don't miss any of your favourites.","hl":"changes","uz":"Doimiy dasturlarimizda bir nechta o'zgarishlar bor, shuning uchun sevimli ko'rsatuvlaringizni o'tkazib yubormaslik uchun diqqat bilan tinglang.","why":"\"A few changes to our regular programmes\" — dasturlarga o'zgarishlar."},{"a":["flowers"],"ps":42.87,"en":59.71,"si":4,"ev":"John entertained us all previously with his trip to the safari park when he went along to meet the elephants. This time John will be telling us about how we can recognize the wild flowers in our gardens.","hl":"flowers","uz":"Jon avval safari parkiga borib, fillar bilan tanishgani haqida so'zlab bergan edi. Bu safar u bog'larimizdagi yovvoyi gullarni qanday tanib olishni aytib beradi.","why":"Elephants — oldingi ko'rsatuv (tuzoq). Bu hafta — wild flowers."},{"a":["published"],"ps":74.71,"en":90.21,"si":7,"ev":"We've had to rearrange this interview for next week as Francis is attending a conference. Instead, we'll be talking with an expert about how you can make use of the internet to get your next book published.","hl":"published","uz":"Frensis konferensiyada bo'lgani uchun bu intervyuni keyingi haftaga ko'chirdik. Uning o'rniga mutaxassis bilan keyingi kitobingizni internet orqali qanday nashr ettirish haqida suhbatlashamiz.","why":"\"Using the web\" = \"make use of the internet\". Bo'shliqqa fe'lning 3-shakli kerak: published."},{"a":["cancelled"],"ps":100.02,"en":109.41,"si":9,"ev":"Most of the games from last Saturday were cancelled due to the terrible weather, so there are no reports on those matches.","hl":"cancelled","uz":"O'tgan shanbadagi o'yinlarning aksariyati dahshatli ob-havo tufayli bekor qilindi, shuning uchun o'sha o'yinlar haqida hisobot bo'lmaydi.","why":"\"As they were ___\" — sabab: o'yinlar bekor qilingan (cancelled)."},{"a":["10.00","10 am","10"],"ps":130.23,"en":139.13,"si":13,"ev":"She'll be interviewing people for our weekly programme Money Matters, starting from 10, not the usual 9.","hl":"10","uz":"U har haftalik \"Money Matters\" dasturi uchun odamlardan intervyu oladi — odatdagidek soat 9 dan emas, 10 dan boshlab.","why":"\"The new time\" — yangi vaqt: 10. Soat 9 — odatdagi (eski) vaqt."},{"a":["library"],"ps":139.93,"en":158.43,"si":14,"ev":"If you'd like the chance to speak to her and share your views of your experiences and any problems you may have, meet Sally at the main door of the library, not the normal meeting place at the town hall, which is closed due to building work.","hl":"library","uz":"U bilan gaplashmoqchi bo'lsangiz, Sallini kutubxonaning asosiy eshigi oldida kuting — odatdagi joy bo'lgan shahar hokimiyati qurilish ishlari tufayli yopiq.","why":"Town hall — odatdagi joy, hozir yopiq (tuzoq). Bu safar — library."}],"segs":[{"s":6.84,"e":13.44,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter called Jonathan talking about the programmes during the week."},{"s":15.22,"e":24.64,"t":"Before tonight's news, let me tell you about some of the shows we have for you this week so you can make a note of them in your diary."},{"s":25.43,"e":34.62,"t":"There are a few changes to our regular programs, so listen carefully to make sure you don't miss any of your favourites.","uz":"Doimiy dasturlarimizda bir nechta o'zgarishlar bor, shuning uchun sevimli ko'rsatuvlaringizni o'tkazib yubormaslik uchun diqqat bilan tinglang."},{"s":35.42,"e":42.11,"t":"Tonight at 8.30, John Seymour will present this week's wildlife documentary."},{"s":42.87,"e":59.71,"t":"John entertained us all previously with his trip to the safari park when he went along to meet the elephants. This time John will be telling us about how we can recognize the wild flowers in our gardens.","uz":"Jon avval safari parkiga borib, fillar bilan tanishgani haqida so'zlab bergan edi. Bu safar u bog'larimizdagi yovvoyi gullarni qanday tanib olishni aytib beradi."},{"s":60.66,"e":63.26,"t":"Then, our first change of schedule."},{"s":63.8,"e":74.27,"t":"Apologies to listeners looking forward to writer's world and our interview with Francis Selhurst on how to get ideas for your next novel."},{"s":74.71,"e":90.21,"t":"We've had to rearrange this interview for next week as Francis is attending a conference. Instead, we'll be talking with an expert about how you can make use of the internet to get your next book published.","uz":"Frensis konferensiyada bo'lgani uchun bu intervyuni keyingi haftaga ko'chirdik. Uning o'rniga mutaxassis bilan keyingi kitobingizni internet orqali qanday nashr ettirish haqida suhbatlashamiz."},{"s":91.45,"e":99.1,"t":"On Thursday at 8, we have sports night as usual with a look at next weekend's football."},{"s":100.02,"e":109.41,"t":"Most of the games from last Saturday were cancelled due to the terrible weather, so there are no reports on those matches.","uz":"O'tgan shanbadagi o'yinlarning aksariyati dahshatli ob-havo tufayli bekor qilindi, shuning uchun o'sha o'yinlar haqida hisobot bo'lmaydi."},{"s":110.33,"e":119.49,"t":"Our experts will be looking forward to seeing some action this Saturday and will be trying to predict results as usual."},{"s":119.96,"e":122.01,"t":"Join our team at eight."},{"s":122.87,"e":129.6,"t":"And finally, our reporter Sally Williams will be in town next Friday morning."},{"s":130.23,"e":139.13,"t":"She'll be interviewing people for our weekly programme Money Matters, starting from 10, not the usual 9.","uz":"U har haftalik \"Money Matters\" dasturi uchun odamlardan intervyu oladi — odatdagidek soat 9 dan emas, 10 dan boshlab."},{"s":139.93,"e":158.43,"t":"If you'd like the chance to speak to her and share your views of your experiences and any problems you may have, meet Sally at the main door of the library, not the normal meeting place at the town hall, which is closed due to building work.","uz":"U bilan gaplashmoqchi bo'lsangiz, Sallini kutubxonaning asosiy eshigi oldida kuting — odatdagi joy bo'lgan shahar hokimiyati qurilish ishlari tufayli yopiq."}]},{"n":9,"title":"Company Training Day","dur":273.4,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Some of the training sessions may take place in a different {1} to the one in the programme."},{"k":"p","t":"Your training sessions will be confirmed by email on 13 {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Please complete the {3} in the materials before you come to the training event."},{"k":"p","t":"Please give your completed questionnaire to the {4} manager after the training day."},{"k":"p","t":"The {5} will be closed on the training day."},{"k":"p","t":"Remember to check the noticeboard outside room {6} for any last-minute changes."}],"items":[{"a":["building"],"ps":19.16,"en":34.3,"si":2,"ev":"You should all receive your program by email shortly. We've had to make changes to rooms, and even now, some of the training sessions may have to be held in a different building, but we'll let you know if this happens.","hl":"building","uz":"Dasturingizni tez orada email orqali olasiz. Xonalarni o'zgartirishga to'g'ri keldi, hatto ayrim mashg'ulotlar boshqa binoda o'tishi mumkin — bunday bo'lsa, xabar beramiz.","why":"\"Different rooms\" ham aytiladi, lekin mashg'ulotlar boshqa building (bino)da bo'lishi mumkin."},{"a":["September"],"ps":49.78,"en":56.96,"si":4,"ev":"We will let you know by email on the 13th of September, the full list of names of people going to each session.","hl":"September","uz":"Har bir mashg'ulotga boradiganlarning to'liq ro'yxatini 13-sentabrda email orqali yuboramiz.","why":"\"On the 13th of September\" — sana: 13 September."},{"a":["exercises"],"ps":66.23,"en":77.76,"si":6,"ev":"There are some tasks for you to complete in preparation for your session. Please make sure you print out these materials and complete the exercises before you attend.","hl":"exercises","uz":"Mashg'ulotga tayyorgarlik uchun bajarishingiz kerak bo'lgan topshiriqlar bor. Bu materiallarni chop etib, kelishdan oldin mashqlarni bajaring.","why":"\"Complete the exercises\" — bo'shliq: exercises. \"Tasks\" sinonim, lekin kalit so'z — exercises."},{"a":["training"],"ps":78.81,"en":90.59,"si":7,"ev":"At the end of the training day, you will all be given a questionnaire for your comments on each of the sessions you attended. Could you please make sure you complete this and give it to the training manager?","hl":"training","uz":"Trening kuni oxirida har bir mashg'ulot haqida fikringizni yozish uchun so'rovnoma beriladi. Uni to'ldirib, trening menejeriga topshiring.","why":"Restaurant manager ham tilga olinadi (tuzoq) — so'rovnoma training managerga beriladi."},{"a":["restaurant"],"ps":98.1,"en":105.05,"si":9,"ev":"Because staff in the company restaurant will also be attending training sessions, the restaurant will not be open.","hl":"restaurant","uz":"Kompaniya restorani xodimlari ham trening mashg'ulotlarida qatnashgani uchun restoran ochiq bo'lmaydi.","why":"\"Will not be open\" = will be closed. Javob — restaurant."},{"a":["134"],"ps":119.74,"en":127.13,"si":12,"ev":"Finally, can I remind you to check the notice board outside room 134 for any last minute changes?","hl":"134","uz":"Va nihoyat, so'nggi daqiqadagi o'zgarishlar uchun 134-xona tashqarisidagi e'lonlar taxtasini tekshirishni unutmang.","why":"Son: 134. Email ham bor, lekin ishonchli joy — e'lonlar taxtasi."}],"segs":[{"s":7.48,"e":13.21,"t":"You will hear a manager called Sandra talking about a company training day."},{"s":15.03,"e":18.72,"t":"Can I just say something about the training day next week?"},{"s":19.16,"e":34.3,"t":"You should all receive your program by email shortly. We've had to make changes to rooms, and even now, some of the training sessions may have to be held in a different building, but we'll let you know if this happens.","uz":"Dasturingizni tez orada email orqali olasiz. Xonalarni o'zgartirishga to'g'ri keldi, hatto ayrim mashg'ulotlar boshqa binoda o'tishi mumkin — bunday bo'lsa, xabar beramiz."},{"s":35.19,"e":49.15,"t":"And some of you have asked about changing to a different session than the one you signed up for. We've tried to do this when it's been possible, but as some training sessions are full, it will sometimes not be possible."},{"s":49.78,"e":56.96,"t":"We will let you know by email on the 13th of September, the full list of names of people going to each session.","uz":"Har bir mashg'ulotga boradiganlarning to'liq ro'yxatini 13-sentabrda email orqali yuboramiz."},{"s":58.39,"e":65.69,"t":"The trainers will email you the materials they'll be using during the sessions for you to have a look at before the training day."},{"s":66.23,"e":77.76,"t":"There are some tasks for you to complete in preparation for your session. Please make sure you print out these materials and complete the exercises before you attend.","uz":"Mashg'ulotga tayyorgarlik uchun bajarishingiz kerak bo'lgan topshiriqlar bor. Bu materiallarni chop etib, kelishdan oldin mashqlarni bajaring."},{"s":78.81,"e":90.59,"t":"At the end of the training day, you will all be given a questionnaire for your comments on each of the sessions you attended. Could you please make sure you complete this and give it to the training manager?","uz":"Trening kuni oxirida har bir mashg'ulot haqida fikringizni yozish uchun so'rovnoma beriladi. Uni to'ldirib, trening menejeriga topshiring."},{"s":91.22,"e":96.64,"t":"We are using a new company for this event and are keen to see how well the day goes."},{"s":98.1,"e":105.05,"t":"Because staff in the company restaurant will also be attending training sessions, the restaurant will not be open.","uz":"Kompaniya restorani xodimlari ham trening mashg'ulotlarida qatnashgani uchun restoran ochiq bo'lmaydi."},{"s":105.53,"e":110.01,"t":"We are arranging cold food, teas, and coffee for everyone."},{"s":110.87,"e":118.72,"t":"Could you email the restaurant manager before the end of this week and let him know if you have any special dietary requirements?"},{"s":119.74,"e":127.13,"t":"Finally, can I remind you to check the notice board outside room 134 for any last minute changes?","uz":"Va nihoyat, so'nggi daqiqadagi o'zgarishlar uchun 134-xona tashqarisidagi e'lonlar taxtasini tekshirishni unutmang."},{"s":127.58,"e":140.61,"t":"Yes, we'll email you all important information, but several of you have complained that you haven't received our messages. So, to be absolutely sure you're up to date, check the notice board."}]},{"n":10,"title":"The Speakers' Club","dur":282.6,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"For business presentations to colleagues or to get ready for an {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Workshop leaders have a background in business or {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Sessions start at {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Members are invited to try one of our {4} once a year."},{"k":"p","t":"The first meeting is speech {5} but remember to reserve a place."},{"k":"p","t":"Membership costs {6} per year or payment can be made each month."}],"items":[{"a":["interview"],"ps":29.53,"en":38.17,"si":3,"ev":"Perhaps you have to give talks to colleagues at work or need to practice a presentation you have prepared for a job interview.","hl":"interview","uz":"Balki ishda hamkasblarga ma'ruza qilishingiz yoki ish suhbati uchun tayyorlagan taqdimotingizni mashq qilishingiz kerakdir.","why":"\"Job interview\" — ish suhbati. Bo'shliqqa bitta so'z: interview."},{"a":["entertainment"],"ps":39.35,"en":54.3,"si":4,"ev":"The Speakers Club offers a weekly meeting in the main hall where members can learn from each other as well as through talks given by highly experienced speakers from the world of business or entertainment.","hl":"entertainment","uz":"Klub har hafta asosiy zalda yig'ilish o'tkazadi: a'zolar bir-biridan va biznes yoki ko'ngilochar sohadan kelgan tajribali notiqlardan o'rganadi.","why":"\"From the world of business or entertainment\" — biznes yoki ko'ngilochar soha."},{"a":["7.00","7pm","7 o'clock","7"],"ps":62.58,"en":73.31,"si":6,"ev":"A typical session starts at 7 with tea, coffee and biscuits before we listen to the speaker and start looking at a particular topic.","hl":"7","uz":"Odatiy mashg'ulot soat 7 da choy, qahva va pechenye bilan boshlanadi, keyin notiqni tinglaymiz.","why":"\"Starts at 7\" — 7.00 / 7 pm."},{"a":["competitions"],"ps":85.62,"en":90.75,"si":8,"ev":"We also invite you to enter one of our speech competitions each year.","hl":"competitions","uz":"Shuningdek, sizni har yili nutq tanlovlarimizdan birida qatnashishga taklif qilamiz.","why":"\"Speech competitions each year\" — yiliga bir marta tanlov."},{"a":["free"],"ps":103.1,"en":107.9,"si":10,"ev":"So, we invite anyone to attend their first session for free.","hl":"free","uz":"Shuning uchun birinchi mashg'ulotga istalgan kishini bepul taklif qilamiz.","why":"\"For free\" — bepul: free."},{"a":["£170","170"],"ps":120.63,"en":132.48,"si":12,"ev":"If you do decide to join us, annual membership is £170 per year. Arrangements can be made to pay the membership fee once a month.","hl":"£170","uz":"Qo'shilishga qaror qilsangiz, yillik a'zolik 170 funt. A'zolik to'lovini oyma-oy to'lash ham mumkin.","why":"Son va valyuta: £170 (170 deb yozsangiz ham bo'ladi)."}],"segs":[{"s":6.58,"e":12.8,"t":"You will hear a man called Russell talking about a new club in the community centre."},{"s":14.68,"e":21.98,"t":"And finally, news of an interesting club that started recently and meets here every week."},{"s":22.55,"e":28.93,"t":"The Speakers Club is aimed at anyone who needs to develop their public speaking skills."},{"s":29.53,"e":38.17,"t":"Perhaps you have to give talks to colleagues at work or need to practice a presentation you have prepared for a job interview.","uz":"Balki ishda hamkasblarga ma'ruza qilishingiz yoki ish suhbati uchun tayyorlagan taqdimotingizni mashq qilishingiz kerakdir."},{"s":39.35,"e":54.3,"t":"The Speakers Club offers a weekly meeting in the main hall where members can learn from each other as well as through talks given by highly experienced speakers from the world of business or entertainment.","uz":"Klub har hafta asosiy zalda yig'ilish o'tkazadi: a'zolar bir-biridan va biznes yoki ko'ngilochar sohadan kelgan tajribali notiqlardan o'rganadi."},{"s":54.97,"e":61.57,"t":"We look at everything from body language and eye contact to storytelling and delivery."},{"s":62.58,"e":73.31,"t":"A typical session starts at 7 with tea, coffee and biscuits before we listen to the speaker and start looking at a particular topic.","uz":"Odatiy mashg'ulot soat 7 da choy, qahva va pechenye bilan boshlanadi, keyin notiqni tinglaymiz."},{"s":74.14,"e":85.02,"t":"Members are then given the chance to change a presentation they've prepared before the session so that it includes the ideas presented by the speaker."},{"s":85.62,"e":90.75,"t":"We also invite you to enter one of our speech competitions each year.","uz":"Shuningdek, sizni har yili nutq tanlovlarimizdan birida qatnashishga taklif qilamiz."},{"s":91.74,"e":102.49,"t":"We understand that clubs like ours might not suit everyone, and we like to give you the chance to see for yourself how we operate before you join."},{"s":103.1,"e":107.9,"t":"So, we invite anyone to attend their first session for free.","uz":"Shuning uchun birinchi mashg'ulotga istalgan kishini bepul taklif qilamiz."},{"s":108.5,"e":119.49,"t":"However, in order for us to manage the numbers of people attending, please make sure you reserve a place first or you may not be able to attend."},{"s":120.63,"e":132.48,"t":"If you do decide to join us, annual membership is £170 per year. Arrangements can be made to pay the membership fee once a month.","uz":"Qo'shilishga qaror qilsangiz, yillik a'zolik 170 funt. A'zolik to'lovini oyma-oy to'lash ham mumkin."},{"s":133.18,"e":145.41,"t":"Membership allows you to attend all sessions during the year and gives you access to private areas of the website and the chance to take part in our social events."}]},{"n":11,"title":"How to Take a Great Photo","dur":241.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The photography course lasted two {1} and was for beginners."},{"k":"h","t":"Useful tips:"},{"k":"p","t":"Make sure the camera is at the same {2} as the person."},{"k":"p","t":"Stand the person in front of a {3} background."},{"k":"p","t":"Taking photos in daylight can help make sure colours are {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Take a photo of your subject when they are {5} or looking out of the window."},{"k":"p","t":"Try to take at least three {6} of people every day."}],"items":[{"a":["days"],"ps":13.88,"en":29.95,"si":1,"ev":"I had a great time away on holiday and one of the things I did was go on a two-day photography course about taking photos of people. It was for beginners and I was given quite a few tips.","hl":"day","uz":"Ta'tilda zo'r dam oldim; qilgan ishlarimdan biri — odamlarni suratga olish bo'yicha ikki kunlik fotografiya kursi edi. U boshlovchilar uchun bo'lib, menga bir qancha maslahatlar berildi.","why":"\"A two-day course\" — kurs ikki kun davom etgan: two days. Bo'shliqqa ko'plik shakli kerak: days."},{"a":["height"],"ps":47.13,"en":54.78,"si":5,"ev":"It's also important to make sure the camera is at the same height as the person, especially if you're taking one of a child.","hl":"height","uz":"Kamera odam bilan bir xil balandlikda bo'lishi ham muhim, ayniqsa bolani suratga olayotgan bo'lsangiz.","why":"\"Same height\" — bir xil balandlik."},{"a":["plain"],"ps":60.5,"en":65.25,"si":7,"ev":"The person will stand out much more if the background is as plain as possible.","hl":"plain","uz":"Fon iloji boricha oddiy (bir xil rangda) bo'lsa, odam ancha ajralib turadi.","why":"\"Plain background\" — oddiy, naqshsiz fon."},{"a":["accurate"],"ps":79.96,"en":85.09,"si":10,"ev":"Doing this will make the colors more accurate and the photo will appear more natural.","hl":"accurate","uz":"Bu ranglarni aniqroq qiladi va surat tabiiyroq ko'rinadi.","why":"\"Make the colours more accurate\" — ranglar aniq chiqadi. Natural — suratning o'zi haqida."},{"a":["reading"],"ps":101.18,"en":104.7,"si":13,"ev":"Perhaps they're reading or looking out of the window.","hl":"reading","uz":"Ehtimol, ular kitob o'qiyotgan yoki derazadan qarab turgan bo'ladi.","why":"\"Reading or looking out of the window\" — kitobdagi gap bilan bir xil tuzilma."},{"a":["photos"],"ps":105.98,"en":117.6,"si":14,"ev":"Finally, they told us to take plenty of photos so we can practice our skills. They said we should aim to take at least three photos of people every day.","hl":"photos","uz":"Nihoyat, ko'nikmalarimizni mashq qilish uchun ko'p suratga olishni aytishdi: har kuni odamlarning kamida uchta suratini olishni maqsad qilishimiz kerak.","why":"\"At least three photos of people every day\" — javob: photos."}],"segs":[{"s":5.88,"e":12.06,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter called William talking about a photography course he did."},{"s":13.88,"e":29.95,"t":"I had a great time away on holiday and one of the things I did was go on a two-day photography course about taking photos of people. It was for beginners and I was given quite a few tips.","uz":"Ta'tilda zo'r dam oldim; qilgan ishlarimdan biri — odamlarni suratga olish bo'yicha ikki kunlik fotografiya kursi edi. U boshlovchilar uchun bo'lib, menga bir qancha maslahatlar berildi."},{"s":30.81,"e":35.01,"t":"For example, getting your position correct is really important."},{"s":35.51,"e":40.22,"t":"They said a common mistake is to stand too far away from the person."},{"s":40.73,"e":46.01,"t":"You get a much better result if you get close to them as they take up more of the photo."},{"s":47.13,"e":54.78,"t":"It's also important to make sure the camera is at the same height as the person, especially if you're taking one of a child.","uz":"Kamera odam bilan bir xil balandlikda bo'lishi ham muhim, ayniqsa bolani suratga olayotgan bo'lsangiz."},{"s":55.83,"e":59.81,"t":"A really useful tip was to pay attention to the background."},{"s":60.5,"e":65.25,"t":"The person will stand out much more if the background is as plain as possible.","uz":"Fon iloji boricha oddiy (bir xil rangda) bo'lsa, odam ancha ajralib turadi."},{"s":66.1,"e":69.18,"t":"This will help you to focus on the subject of your photo."},{"s":70.52,"e":79.33,"t":"Although most smartphones come with a flash to provide extra light, they suggested we try to make as much use as possible of daylight."},{"s":79.96,"e":85.09,"t":"Doing this will make the colors more accurate and the photo will appear more natural.","uz":"Bu ranglarni aniqroq qiladi va surat tabiiyroq ko'rinadi."},{"s":86.49,"e":91.68,"t":"We're all used to asking someone to say cheese when we're about to take their photo."},{"s":92.57,"e":100.54,"t":"To get a more interesting picture, they recommended taking a photo of the person when they don't know you're about to do it."},{"s":101.18,"e":104.7,"t":"Perhaps they're reading or looking out of the window.","uz":"Ehtimol, ular kitob o'qiyotgan yoki derazadan qarab turgan bo'ladi."},{"s":105.98,"e":117.6,"t":"Finally, they told us to take plenty of photos so we can practice our skills. They said we should aim to take at least three photos of people every day.","uz":"Nihoyat, ko'nikmalarimizni mashq qilish uchun ko'p suratga olishni aytishdi: har kuni odamlarning kamida uchta suratini olishni maqsad qilishimiz kerak."},{"s":118.39,"e":124.54,"t":"These can be of friends and family or even strangers if you ask their permission."}]},{"n":12,"title":"Summer Activities","dur":249.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"For a full programme of events, text {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The Activity Centre is running indoor {2} sessions for beginners."},{"k":"p","t":"There are also walks along the coast {3} to learn about the local wildlife."},{"k":"p","t":"The Activity Centre is running an open day on {4} June."},{"k":"p","t":"On the History Group walk you can learn about a famous {5} who was born in the area."},{"k":"p","t":"If you're interested in writing {6} don't forget to book a place with the Arts Centre."}],"items":[{"a":["1576"],"ps":20.95,"en":32.8,"si":2,"ev":"I'll give you an idea of what you can do now, but for a full program of events, text 1576 and we'll send you a link to all the information you need.","hl":"1576","uz":"Hozir sizga qanday imkoniyatlar borligi haqida tasavvur beraman, to'liq tadbirlar dasturi uchun esa 1576 raqamiga SMS yuboring — sizga barcha ma'lumotlar havolasini jo'natamiz.","why":"Raqamni aynan yozing: 1576."},{"a":["climbing"],"ps":42.33,"en":49.31,"si":4,"ev":"There's climbing for beginners. This is indoors and will be led by experienced teachers.","hl":"climbing","uz":"Boshlovchilar uchun toqqa chiqish (climbing) mashg'uloti bor. U yopiq binoda bo'lib, tajribali o'qituvchilar olib boradi.","why":"\"Indoors\" — yopiq joyda; \"for beginners\" — boshlovchilar uchun. Mashg'ulot — climbing."},{"a":["path"],"ps":49.94,"en":57.41,"si":5,"ev":"The centre has also organized a walk along the coast path. Have a look at some of the creatures you can find there.","hl":"path","uz":"Markaz qirg'oq yo'lagi bo'ylab sayr ham tashkil qilgan. U yerda uchraydigan jonzotlarni tomosha qiling.","why":"\"Coast path\" — qirg'oq bo'ylab yo'lak."},{"a":["13","13th"],"ps":58.3,"en":67.49,"si":6,"ev":"The center is open seven days a week with a special open day on the 13th of June to give you an idea of what else is on offer.","hl":"13","uz":"Markaz haftada yetti kun ishlaydi, boshqa imkoniyatlar bilan tanishishingiz uchun 13-iyunda maxsus ochiq eshiklar kuni bo'ladi.","why":"\"Seven days a week\" — ish rejimi (tuzoq). Ochiq eshiklar kuni — 13-iyun."},{"a":["celebrity"],"ps":81.24,"en":88.61,"si":8,"ev":"Find out where a very well-known celebrity was born and learn about local industry in the past.","hl":"celebrity","uz":"Juda mashhur bir shaxs qayerda tug'ilganini bilib oling va o'tmishdagi mahalliy sanoat haqida o'rganing.","why":"\"A very well-known celebrity\" — mashhur shaxs: celebrity."},{"a":["poetry"],"ps":114.52,"en":128.96,"si":13,"ev":"This year, they'll be organizing a question and answer session for anyone interested in writing poetry. The Arts Centre expects this to be quite popular, so you should call them first to book a place.","hl":"poetry","uz":"Bu yil she'r yozishga qiziquvchilar uchun savol-javob kechasi tashkil qilinadi. San'at markazi bunga qiziqish katta bo'lishini kutyapti, shuning uchun avval qo'ng'iroq qilib joy band qiling.","why":"\"Writing poetry\" — she'r yozish. Mashhur yozuvchilar — oldingi gapda (tuzoq emas, lekin javob ham emas)."}],"segs":[{"s":5.14,"e":12.99,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter called Ellen talking about local activities taking place over the summer."},{"s":14.81,"e":20.41,"t":"If you're looking for things to do over the summer, there's lots going on in the area."},{"s":20.95,"e":32.8,"t":"I'll give you an idea of what you can do now, but for a full program of events, text 1576 and we'll send you a link to all the information you need.","uz":"Hozir sizga qanday imkoniyatlar borligi haqida tasavvur beraman, to'liq tadbirlar dasturi uchun esa 1576 raqamiga SMS yuboring — sizga barcha ma'lumotlar havolasini jo'natamiz."},{"s":33.94,"e":41.66,"t":"To give you a taste of what's on offer, the Activity Center is running a wide range of activities for all the family."},{"s":42.33,"e":49.31,"t":"There's climbing for beginners. This is indoors and will be led by experienced teachers.","uz":"Boshlovchilar uchun toqqa chiqish (climbing) mashg'uloti bor. U yopiq binoda bo'lib, tajribali o'qituvchilar olib boradi."},{"s":49.94,"e":57.41,"t":"The centre has also organized a walk along the coast path. Have a look at some of the creatures you can find there.","uz":"Markaz qirg'oq yo'lagi bo'ylab sayr ham tashkil qilgan. U yerda uchraydigan jonzotlarni tomosha qiling."},{"s":58.3,"e":67.49,"t":"The center is open seven days a week with a special open day on the 13th of June to give you an idea of what else is on offer.","uz":"Markaz haftada yetti kun ishlaydi, boshqa imkoniyatlar bilan tanishishingiz uchun 13-iyunda maxsus ochiq eshiklar kuni bo'ladi."},{"s":68.66,"e":80.25,"t":"As you know, our town has a very long history, and those with an interest in the past can sign up for one of the guided walks the history group has organized."},{"s":81.24,"e":88.61,"t":"Find out where a very well-known celebrity was born and learn about local industry in the past.","uz":"Juda mashhur bir shaxs qayerda tug'ilganini bilib oling va o'tmishdagi mahalliy sanoat haqida o'rganing."},{"s":89.11,"e":94.72,"t":"You can find out more at the History Center, which is located in the Central Library."},{"s":95.86,"e":102.62,"t":"For film lovers, the Arts Center has a full program of films running throughout the summer months."},{"s":103.06,"e":110.24,"t":"and the Book Festival, which starts on the 14th of August, has several speakers on its program."},{"s":111.16,"e":113.89,"t":"Greetings by some well-known authors."},{"s":114.52,"e":128.96,"t":"This year, they'll be organizing a question and answer session for anyone interested in writing poetry. The Arts Centre expects this to be quite popular, so you should call them first to book a place.","uz":"Bu yil she'r yozishga qiziquvchilar uchun savol-javob kechasi tashkil qilinadi. San'at markazi bunga qiziqish katta bo'lishini kutyapti, shuning uchun avval qo'ng'iroq qilib joy band qiling."}]},{"n":13,"title":"Milburn's Stores","dur":256.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"At this Thursday's 'Special Buy' day you can get something for your {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"There are jobs available for trainee managers and {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Collect a {3} by the exit for information about how to apply."},{"k":"p","t":"On Friday the supermarket will open until {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"This month Milburn's are supporting the local Arts Project and Children's {5} Group."},{"k":"p","t":"You will be given a {6} when you pay to show your support."}],"items":[{"a":["pet"],"ps":28.92,"en":36.96,"si":4,"ev":"This Thursday you'll be able to buy a special gift for your pet with lots of items at low, low prices.","hl":"pet","uz":"Shu payshanba uy hayvoningiz uchun maxsus sovg'a sotib olishingiz mumkin — ko'plab mahsulotlar juda arzon narxlarda.","why":"\"A special gift for your pet\" — uy hayvoni uchun."},{"a":["cleaners"],"ps":49.85,"en":56.77,"si":7,"ev":"There are now opportunities to join our trainee manager program and several jobs for cleaners.","hl":"cleaners","uz":"Endi stajyor menejerlar dasturiga qo'shilish imkoniyati va farroshlar uchun bir nechta ish o'rni bor.","why":"\"Several jobs for cleaners\" — farroshlar (tozalovchilar)."},{"a":["magazine"],"ps":57.43,"en":82.11,"si":8,"ev":"We are proud of our staff and like to think they're proud to be part of the Milburn family. Why not speak to our manager today if you're interested in joining us? Or pick up our magazine at the exit for details about how to apply. As the new year approaches we know you'll need to get your shopping done ready for all the celebrations.","hl":"magazine","uz":"Xodimlarimiz bilan faxrlanamiz va ular ham Milburn oilasining a'zosi bo'lishdan faxrlanadi deb o'ylaymiz. Bizga qo'shilishga qiziqsangiz, bugun menejerimiz bilan gaplashing yoki ariza topshirish tafsilotlari uchun chiqish yonidan jurnalimizni oling.","why":"\"Pick up our magazine at the exit\" — chiqish yonida jurnal."},{"a":["10.30","10.30 pm","22:30","22.30"],"ps":75.77,"en":89.28,"si":null,"ev":"As the new year approaches, we know you'll need to get your shopping done ready for all the celebrations. We'll be opening until 10.30 on Friday evening to give you time to get ready for the big day.","hl":"10.30","uz":"Yangi yil yaqinlashar ekan, bayramga xaridlarni qilib olishingiz kerakligini bilamiz. Juma kuni kechqurun soat 22:30 gacha ochiq bo'lamiz.","why":"\"Until 10.30 on Friday evening\" — 10.30 (pm)."},{"a":["theatre"],"ps":106.26,"en":112.38,"si":12,"ev":"This month we're supporting the Local Arts Project and the Children's Theatre Group.","hl":"Theatre","uz":"Bu oy biz Mahalliy San'at loyihasi va Bolalar teatri guruhini qo'llab-quvvatlayapmiz.","why":"\"Children's Theatre Group\" — bolalar teatri."},{"a":["ticket"],"ps":113.14,"en":124.61,"si":13,"ev":"When you pay for your shopping, you'll be given a ticket. To show your support, choose which of the organisations you would like to give this to by putting it in the box by the exit.","hl":"ticket","uz":"Xarid uchun to'laganingizda sizga chipta beriladi. Qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun uni qaysi tashkilotga bermoqchi bo'lsangiz, chiqishdagi qutiga soling.","why":"\"You'll be given a ticket\" — chipta."}],"segs":[{"s":4.79,"e":8.25,"t":"You will hear an announcement in a supermarket."},{"s":10.01,"e":11.93,"t":"Welcome to Milburn's."},{"s":12.38,"e":22.62,"t":"If you're looking for a sale or for something unusual, don't forget our Thursday Special Buy Day, where you'll find some great offers."},{"s":23.13,"e":28.19,"t":"These change every week and are removed from the shelves at the end of the day."},{"s":28.92,"e":36.96,"t":"This Thursday you'll be able to buy a special gift for your pet with lots of items at low, low prices.","uz":"Shu payshanba uy hayvoningiz uchun maxsus sovg'a sotib olishingiz mumkin — ko'plab mahsulotlar juda arzon narxlarda."},{"s":37.43,"e":40.57,"t":"Come early and don't miss our offers."},{"s":41.94,"e":49.18,"t":"Are you interested in a career with Milburn's? We're looking for new staff in various areas of the business."},{"s":49.85,"e":56.77,"t":"There are now opportunities to join our trainee manager program and several jobs for cleaners.","uz":"Endi stajyor menejerlar dasturiga qo'shilish imkoniyati va farroshlar uchun bir nechta ish o'rni bor."},{"s":57.43,"e":82.11,"t":"We are proud of our staff and like to think they're proud to be part of the Milburn family. Why not speak to our manager today if you're interested in joining us? Or pick up our magazine at the exit for details about how to apply. As the new year approaches we know you'll need to get your shopping done ready for all the celebrations.","uz":"Xodimlarimiz bilan faxrlanamiz va ular ham Milburn oilasining a'zosi bo'lishdan faxrlanadi deb o'ylaymiz. Bizga qo'shilishga qiziqsangiz, bugun menejerimiz bilan gaplashing yoki ariza topshirish tafsilotlari uchun chiqish yonidan jurnalimizni oling."},{"s":82.58,"e":89.28,"t":"We'll be opening until 10.30 on Friday evening to give you time to get ready for the big day."},{"s":90.07,"e":97.82,"t":"Don't forget we'll be closed on the first, but open again on the second when we return to normal opening hours."},{"s":98.9,"e":105.41,"t":"We value our local community and are always looking for the chance to help out where we can."},{"s":106.26,"e":112.38,"t":"This month we're supporting the Local Arts Project and the Children's Theatre Group.","uz":"Bu oy biz Mahalliy San'at loyihasi va Bolalar teatri guruhini qo'llab-quvvatlayapmiz."},{"s":113.14,"e":124.61,"t":"When you pay for your shopping, you'll be given a ticket. To show your support, choose which of the organisations you would like to give this to by putting it in the box by the exit.","uz":"Xarid uchun to'laganingizda sizga chipta beriladi. Qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun uni qaysi tashkilotga bermoqchi bo'lsangiz, chiqishdagi qutiga soling."},{"s":125.3,"e":129.69,"t":"We'll turn these into cash when they are counted up at the end of the month."}]},{"n":14,"title":"Your First Week at University","dur":265.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Make sure you bring information about your course and {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Tell someone if you find anything that is {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The first place to meet new people is the {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Clubs and societies are a great way to meet people who are studying different {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"Avoid signing up for more than {5} groups."},{"k":"p","t":"Register with the local {6} soon after you arrive."}],"items":[{"a":["accommodation"],"ps":34.2,"en":40.54,"si":5,"ev":"You'll certainly need all the documentation the university has sent you about your course or accommodation.","hl":"accommodation","uz":"Universitet kursingiz yoki yotoqxonangiz haqida yuborgan barcha hujjatlar sizga albatta kerak bo'ladi.","why":"\"Course or accommodation\" — kurs va turar joy hujjatlari. Passport — sayohat qilsangiz kerak (tuzoq)."},{"a":["damaged"],"ps":49.24,"en":64.0,"si":8,"ev":"When you arrive and go to your room, check that everything is as it should be and in good condition. Report anything that looks damaged — you don't want to be blamed for this and be asked to pay any costs involved.","hl":"damaged","uz":"Kelib xonangizga kirganingizda hammasi joyida va yaxshi holatda ekanini tekshiring. Shikastlangan narsa bo'lsa, xabar bering — aybdor qilinib, xarajatni to'lashingizni so'rashlarini istamaysiz.","why":"\"Anything that looks damaged\" — shikastlangan."},{"a":["kitchen"],"ps":68.73,"en":77.12,"si":10,"ev":"Don't lock yourself away in your room. Go to the kitchen, as this is always the first place to introduce yourself to other students.","hl":"kitchen","uz":"Xonangizga qamalib olmang. Oshxonaga boring — boshqa talabalar bilan tanishadigan birinchi joy doim shu.","why":"\"The first place to introduce yourself\" — kitchen."},{"a":["subjects"],"ps":90.3,"en":94.27,"si":13,"ev":"These are great ways to get to know students doing different subjects.","hl":"subjects","uz":"Ular boshqa fanlarni o'qiyotgan talabalar bilan tanishishning zo'r usuli.","why":"\"Students doing different subjects\" — turli fanlar."},{"a":["five","5"],"ps":102.71,"en":111.68,"si":15,"ev":"It's sensible to limit yourself to signing up to a maximum of five groups, or you'll be receiving emails for weeks to come.","hl":"five","uz":"Ko'pi bilan beshta guruhga yozilish oqilona, aks holda haftalab email olib yurasiz.","why":"\"A maximum of five groups\" — besh."},{"a":["doctor"],"ps":113.27,"en":122.17,"si":16,"ev":"Don't forget the important things like registering with the local doctor as soon as you can. And think about your weekly shopping list.","hl":"doctor","uz":"Mahalliy shifokorga imkon qadar tezroq ro'yxatdan o'tish kabi muhim ishlarni unutmang.","why":"\"Registering with the local doctor\" — shifokor."}],"segs":[{"s":5.11,"e":10.85,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter telling new students about the first week at university."},{"s":12.7,"e":15.9,"t":"This will be a very exciting time for you."},{"s":17.02,"e":20.45,"t":"the grades you needed and you're off to university."},{"s":21.34,"e":25.21,"t":"For many of you, this will be the first time away from home."},{"s":26.49,"e":33.21,"t":"Write a list of things you should take with you, for example, your passport, if you're planning to go travelling."},{"s":34.2,"e":40.54,"t":"You'll certainly need all the documentation the university has sent you about your course or accommodation.","uz":"Universitet kursingiz yoki yotoqxonangiz haqida yuborgan barcha hujjatlar sizga albatta kerak bo'ladi."},{"s":41.78,"e":44.29,"t":"Bring too many household items with you."},{"s":44.79,"e":47.71,"t":"you'll be able to buy a lot of things at university."},{"s":49.24,"e":64.0,"t":"When you arrive and go to your room, check that everything is as it should be and in good condition. Report anything that looks damaged — you don't want to be blamed for this and be asked to pay any costs involved.","uz":"Kelib xonangizga kirganingizda hammasi joyida va yaxshi holatda ekanini tekshiring. Shikastlangan narsa bo'lsa, xabar bering — aybdor qilinib, xarajatni to'lashingizni so'rashlarini istamaysiz."},{"s":64.92,"e":67.77,"t":"This is also the time to get to meet new people."},{"s":68.73,"e":77.12,"t":"Don't lock yourself away in your room. Go to the kitchen, as this is always the first place to introduce yourself to other students.","uz":"Xonangizga qamalib olmang. Oshxonaga boring — boshqa talabalar bilan tanishadigan birinchi joy doim shu."},{"s":78.62,"e":82.43,"t":"During your first week, you can enjoy Freshers Week."},{"s":83.32,"e":89.47,"t":"This is the time to find out about all the clubs and societies you can join at university."},{"s":90.3,"e":94.27,"t":"These are great ways to get to know students doing different subjects.","uz":"Ular boshqa fanlarni o'qiyotgan talabalar bilan tanishishning zo'r usuli."},{"s":95.03,"e":101.5,"t":"These people will help you forget about your studies when you need to relax and not talk about work."},{"s":102.71,"e":111.68,"t":"It's sensible to limit yourself to signing up to a maximum of five groups, or you'll be receiving emails for weeks to come.","uz":"Ko'pi bilan beshta guruhga yozilish oqilona, aks holda haftalab email olib yurasiz."},{"s":113.27,"e":122.17,"t":"Don't forget the important things like registering with the local doctor as soon as you can. And think about your weekly shopping list.","uz":"Mahalliy shifokorga imkon qadar tezroq ro'yxatdan o'tish kabi muhim ishlarni unutmang."},{"s":122.9,"e":128.16,"t":"Don't spend too much, but at the same time, make sure you don't go hungry."},{"s":128.86,"e":131.58,"t":"and remember to put your name on your food."},{"s":132.09,"e":135.97,"t":"A shared fridge sometimes leads to arguments."}]},{"n":15,"title":"French for Beginners","dur":114.0,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Class numbers:"},{"k":"li","t":"Minimum 8 students"},{"k":"li","t":"Maximum {1} students"},{"k":"row","l":"Day and time","t":"Tuesday, 7.30 p.m. – {2} p.m."},{"k":"row","l":"Place","t":"Room 26, second floor (opposite the {3} room)"},{"k":"row","l":"Coursebook title","t":"{4} French"},{"k":"row","l":"Price","t":"£8 (if you order now, it will arrive on 1st {5})"},{"k":"row","l":"International evening","t":"Each class will provide some {6}"}],"items":[{"a":["15","fifteen"],"ps":9.88,"en":17.79,"si":1,"ev":"But don't worry, there won't be any more of you — there's always a maximum of 15 in the class and a minimum of 8.","hl":"15","uz":"Xavotir olmang, bundan ko'p bo'lmaysiz — sinfda doim ko'pi bilan 15 va kamida 8 kishi bo'ladi.","why":"8 — minimum (kitobda berilgan). Maksimum — 15."},{"a":["9.30"],"ps":28.44,"en":41.05,"si":4,"ev":"The class will still be on Tuesday evenings but it won't start at 7 o'clock. It will start at the later time of 7.30 and will end at 9.30, not 9 o'clock.","hl":"9.30","uz":"Dars hamon seshanba kechqurunlari bo'ladi, lekin soat 7 da emas, kechroq — 7:30 da boshlanib, 9 da emas, 9:30 da tugaydi.","why":"9 o'clock — eski vaqt (tuzoq). Tugash vaqti — 9.30."},{"a":["art"],"ps":52.38,"en":59.52,"si":8,"ev":"Next week we need to move to the second floor — the room opposite the art room. That's room 26.","hl":"art","uz":"Keyingi hafta ikkinchi qavatga, rassomlik xonasi qarshisidagi xonaga ko'chamiz. Bu — 26-xona.","why":"Room 12 — bugungi xona (tuzoq). 26-xona san'at (art) xonasi qarshisida."},{"a":["starting"],"ps":64.92,"en":69.28,"si":10,"ev":"The course book will be the same as before, that is, starting French.","hl":"starting","uz":"Darslik avvalgidek bo'ladi: \"Starting French\".","why":"Kitob nomi: Starting French."},{"a":["October"],"ps":73.62,"en":84.48,"si":12,"ev":"However, if you want to buy it from us, it costs £8. You can order it today, but it takes two weeks, so you won't have it until the first of October.","hl":"October","uz":"Bizdan sotib olsangiz, narxi 8 funt. Bugun buyurtma bersangiz bo'ladi, lekin ikki hafta ketadi — 1-oktabrgacha qo'lingizga tegmaydi.","why":"\"The first of October\" — 1-oktabr."},{"a":["food"],"ps":85.91,"en":99.07,"si":13,"ev":"One more thing. During the last week of term there is an international evening at the college. There will be traditional dancing from different countries and every class is asked to provide some food.","hl":"food","uz":"Yana bir narsa: chorakning oxirgi haftasida kollejda xalqaro kecha bo'ladi. Turli mamlakatlarning an'anaviy raqslari bo'ladi va har bir sinf biroz taom olib kelishi so'raladi.","why":"Dancing — kechada bo'ladigan narsa (tuzoq). Sinf olib keladi — food."}],"segs":[{"s":4.31,"e":9.28,"t":"Hello everybody and welcome to the class. I'm pleased to see so many of you here today."},{"s":9.88,"e":17.79,"t":"But don't worry, there won't be any more of you — there's always a maximum of 15 in the class and a minimum of 8.","uz":"Xavotir olmang, bundan ko'p bo'lmaysiz — sinfda doim ko'pi bilan 15 va kamida 8 kishi bo'ladi."},{"s":18.52,"e":21.79,"t":"Before we start, I'd like to tell you about the course."},{"s":22.26,"e":26.88,"t":"some of the information you'll probably know already, but some of it has changed."},{"s":28.44,"e":41.05,"t":"The class will still be on Tuesday evenings but it won't start at 7 o'clock. It will start at the later time of 7.30 and will end at 9.30, not 9 o'clock.","uz":"Dars hamon seshanba kechqurunlari bo'ladi, lekin soat 7 da emas, kechroq — 7:30 da boshlanib, 9 da emas, 9:30 da tugaydi."},{"s":41.94,"e":44.13,"t":"I hope that change is okay for everyone."},{"s":45.14,"e":48.61,"t":"Unfortunately, I can't be here any earlier than that."},{"s":49.85,"e":51.45,"t":"Another change is the room."},{"s":52.38,"e":59.52,"t":"Next week we need to move to the second floor — the room opposite the art room. That's room 26.","uz":"Keyingi hafta ikkinchi qavatga, rassomlik xonasi qarshisidagi xonaga ko'chamiz. Bu — 26-xona."},{"s":60.09,"e":63.33,"t":"Today is the only time we'll be here in Room 12."},{"s":64.92,"e":69.28,"t":"The course book will be the same as before, that is, starting French.","uz":"Darslik avvalgidek bo'ladi: \"Starting French\"."},{"s":69.98,"e":73.18,"t":"I see some of you have already bought it. That's good."},{"s":73.62,"e":84.48,"t":"However, if you want to buy it from us, it costs £8. You can order it today, but it takes two weeks, so you won't have it until the first of October.","uz":"Bizdan sotib olsangiz, narxi 8 funt. Bugun buyurtma bersangiz bo'ladi, lekin ikki hafta ketadi — 1-oktabrgacha qo'lingizga tegmaydi."},{"s":85.91,"e":99.07,"t":"One more thing. During the last week of term there is an international evening at the college. There will be traditional dancing from different countries and every class is asked to provide some food.","uz":"Yana bir narsa: chorakning oxirgi haftasida kollejda xalqaro kecha bo'ladi. Turli mamlakatlarning an'anaviy raqslari bo'ladi va har bir sinf biroz taom olib kelishi so'raladi."},{"s":99.96,"e":104.48,"t":"I thought we could take some French cheese but any other suggestions are welcome."},{"s":105.72,"e":112.73,"t":"And finally, let me remind you that most of your lessons will be completely in French. So let's begin now."}]},{"n":16,"title":"Holiday Destinations","dur":163.8,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"The Canary Islands"},{"k":"p","t":"Nice weather throughout the year."},{"k":"p","t":"La Gomera is a good place for {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Prices start at {2} pounds each for a fortnight."},{"k":"h","t":"Sardinia"},{"k":"p","t":"Variety of water sports available."},{"k":"p","t":"You can get a {3} certificate."},{"k":"p","t":"Adults travelling with children cannot go in {4}."},{"k":"h","t":"Iceland"},{"k":"p","t":"Travel around Reykjavik on a bus {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Askja region has beautiful mountains."},{"k":"p","t":"Cost for adults £1,200 – accommodation and return {6} are included in the price."}],"items":[{"a":["walking"],"ps":40.92,"en":55.74,"si":6,"ev":"But there are less well-known islands, like La Gomera. If you want a quieter experience, you can stay in traditional villages there and try out the excellent walking routes in the hills.","hl":"walking","uz":"Kamroq mashhur orollar ham bor, masalan La Gomera. Sokinroq dam olishni istasangiz, an'anaviy qishloqlarda turib, tepaliklardagi ajoyib piyoda yo'laklarini sinab ko'rishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Walking routes\" — piyoda sayr: walking."},{"a":["600","six hundred"],"ps":56.44,"en":68.73,"si":7,"ev":"Johnson's Travel currently has two-week holidays in La Gomera from as little as £600 per person, or £900 with an extra week.","hl":"600","uz":"Johnson's Travel hozir La Gomerada ikki haftalik dam olishni kishi boshiga atigi 600 funtdan taklif qilyapti, qo'shimcha hafta bilan — 900 funt.","why":"\"Fortnight\" = ikki hafta: 600. £900 — uch hafta uchun (tuzoq)."},{"a":["diving"],"ps":85.24,"en":98.72,"si":10,"ev":"Water skiing and sailing are always popular, and you could even try for a diving qualification while you're there on one of the specially organised activity weeks offered by SunWorld.","hl":"diving","uz":"Suv chang'isi va yelkanli qayiq doim mashhur, hatto Sunworld tashkil qiladigan maxsus faol hafta davomida g'avvoslik guvohnomasini olishga ham urinib ko'rishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Diving qualification\" = diving certificate."},{"a":["June"],"ps":99.64,"en":114.14,"si":11,"ev":"Sunworld designs fantastic holidays and the peak season for families begins in July. It's important to remember, however, that the month of June is reserved for adults only.","hl":"June","uz":"Sunworld ajoyib dam olishlar tayyorlaydi, oilalar uchun eng qizg'in mavsum iyulda boshlanadi. Lekin yodda tuting: iyun oyi faqat kattalar uchun.","why":"July — oilalar mavsumi (tuzoq). Bolali kattalar iyunda bora olmaydi."},{"a":["tour"],"ps":123.67,"en":133.37,"si":13,"ev":"On a trip to Iceland, you and your family could first visit all the main attractions of Reykjavik on a special guided bus tour.","hl":"tour","uz":"Islandiyaga safarda oilangiz bilan avval maxsus gidli avtobus sayohatida Reykyavikning asosiy diqqatga sazovor joylarini ko'rishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Guided bus tour\" — avtobus sayohati: tour."},{"a":["flights"],"ps":148.06,"en":160.03,"si":16,"ev":"A week with Travel The World costs £1,200 per adult for accommodation and return flights to Reykjavik and on to Askja.","hl":"flights","uz":"Travel The World bilan bir hafta kattalar uchun 1200 funt — turar joy va Reykyavikka hamda Askjaga borib-kelish parvozlari bilan.","why":"\"Return flights\" — borib-kelish aviachiptalari."}],"segs":[{"s":5.27,"e":9.76,"t":"You will hear a travel writer talking about different holiday destinations."},{"s":10.42,"e":19.29,"t":"I love being a travel writer and I love talking about my trips so thank you for inviting me into the studio today."},{"s":20.06,"e":26.43,"t":"Right, I'm going to tell you about three different holidays that I can recommend to everyone."},{"s":27.1,"e":31.13,"t":"The first is a good year round sun destination."},{"s":31.64,"e":33.21,"t":"the Canary Islands."},{"s":33.85,"e":40.35,"t":"These islands are known for their big, busy seaside hotels in Tenerife and Lanzarote."},{"s":40.92,"e":55.74,"t":"But there are less well-known islands, like La Gomera. If you want a quieter experience, you can stay in traditional villages there and try out the excellent walking routes in the hills.","uz":"Kamroq mashhur orollar ham bor, masalan La Gomera. Sokinroq dam olishni istasangiz, an'anaviy qishloqlarda turib, tepaliklardagi ajoyib piyoda yo'laklarini sinab ko'rishingiz mumkin."},{"s":56.44,"e":68.73,"t":"Johnson's Travel currently has two-week holidays in La Gomera from as little as £600 per person, or £900 with an extra week.","uz":"Johnson's Travel hozir La Gomerada ikki haftalik dam olishni kishi boshiga atigi 600 funtdan taklif qilyapti, qo'shimcha hafta bilan — 900 funt."},{"s":70.01,"e":75.52,"t":"Another island you might like to try is Sardinia in the Mediterranean."},{"s":76.38,"e":84.45,"t":"And if you and your family want a little more adventure, then a water sports holiday could be the one for you."},{"s":85.24,"e":98.72,"t":"Water skiing and sailing are always popular, and you could even try for a diving qualification while you're there on one of the specially organised activity weeks offered by SunWorld.","uz":"Suv chang'isi va yelkanli qayiq doim mashhur, hatto Sunworld tashkil qiladigan maxsus faol hafta davomida g'avvoslik guvohnomasini olishga ham urinib ko'rishingiz mumkin."},{"s":99.64,"e":114.14,"t":"Sunworld designs fantastic holidays and the peak season for families begins in July. It's important to remember, however, that the month of June is reserved for adults only.","uz":"Sunworld ajoyib dam olishlar tayyorlaydi, oilalar uchun eng qizg'in mavsum iyulda boshlanadi. Lekin yodda tuting: iyun oyi faqat kattalar uchun."},{"s":115.77,"e":123.01,"t":"Finally, if you're not interested in lying on the beach, why not try something completely different?"},{"s":123.67,"e":133.37,"t":"On a trip to Iceland, you and your family could first visit all the main attractions of Reykjavik on a special guided bus tour.","uz":"Islandiyaga safarda oilangiz bilan avval maxsus gidli avtobus sayohatida Reykyavikning asosiy diqqatga sazovor joylarini ko'rishingiz mumkin."},{"s":134.07,"e":140.41,"t":"Then take a traditional Icelandic trip on the back of a horse to the Blue Lagoon."},{"s":141.08,"e":147.07,"t":"before flying off to the lovely snow-covered mountains of the Askja region."},{"s":148.06,"e":160.03,"t":"A week with Travel The World costs £1,200 per adult for accommodation and return flights to Reykjavik and on to Askja.","uz":"Travel The World bilan bir hafta kattalar uchun 1200 funt — turar joy va Reykyavikka hamda Askjaga borib-kelish parvozlari bilan."},{"s":160.6,"e":162.59,"t":"rates for children are lower."}]},{"n":17,"title":"Seminar on the Toy Industry","dur":100.9,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"9.30 – 10.00","t":"{1} to the seminar by Sally Connor"},{"k":"row","l":"10.00 – 11.00","t":"Our Company in Tokyo – a talk by Kenji Nakamura followed by a short film"},{"k":"row","l":"11.00 – 11.30","t":"Half an hour for {2}"},{"k":"row","l":"","t":"Buffet lunch in Victoria Hall – {3} to the library"},{"k":"row","l":"2.00 – 3.30","t":"Toys in Britain: Success and Failure – a talk by Robert Price (owner of over {4} toy shops)"},{"k":"row","l":"3.30 – 5.00","t":"What's Next for Toys? – a talk by Sarah Smith, Sales {5}"},{"k":"row","l":"","t":"Tea and {6} in the Green Room (1st floor)"}],"items":[{"a":["introduction"],"ps":23.64,"en":31.81,"si":3,"ev":"After the introduction by Sally Connor, Kenji Nakamura will give a talk. That's from 10am to 11am.","hl":"introduction","uz":"Salli Konnorning kirish so'zidan keyin Kenji Nakamura nutq so'zlaydi.","why":"\"After the introduction by Sally Connor\" — kirish so'zi: introduction."},{"a":["questions"],"ps":40.06,"en":54.72,"si":5,"ev":"This will be followed by half an hour of questions. Then at 12 we'll have a break for lunch. This will be a buffet meal served in Victoria Hall which is on the opposite side of the building next to the library.","hl":"questions","uz":"Shundan so'ng yarim soat savollarga ajratiladi. Keyin soat 12 da tushlik tanaffusi: u binoning qarama-qarshi tomonida, kutubxona yonidagi Viktoriya zalida shved stoli tarzida beriladi.","why":"\"Half an hour of questions\" — yarim soat savol-javob."},{"a":["next"],"ps":40.06,"en":54.72,"si":5,"ev":"This will be followed by half an hour of questions. Then at 12 we'll have a break for lunch. This will be a buffet meal served in Victoria Hall which is on the opposite side of the building next to the library.","hl":"next","uz":"Shundan so'ng yarim soat savollarga ajratiladi. Keyin soat 12 da tushlik tanaffusi: u binoning qarama-qarshi tomonida, kutubxona yonidagi Viktoriya zalida shved stoli tarzida beriladi.","why":"\"Next to the library\" — kutubxona yonida: next."},{"a":["200","two hundred"],"ps":62.1,"en":70.85,"si":7,"ev":"This talk will be given by Robert Price, who, as you know, is the owner of a chain of over 200 toy shops in the UK.","hl":"200","uz":"Bu ma'ruzani Robert Prays o'qiydi — bilasizki, u Buyuk Britaniyadagi 200 dan ortiq o'yinchoq do'konlari tarmog'ining egasi.","why":"\"Over 200 toy shops\" — 200."},{"a":["manager"],"ps":79.8,"en":84.61,"si":9,"ev":"This will be given by Sarah Smith, who is of course our sales manager.","hl":"manager","uz":"Uni, albatta, bizning savdo menejerimiz Sara Smit o'qiydi.","why":"\"Our sales manager\" — savdo menejeri."},{"a":["juice"],"ps":85.34,"en":95.1,"si":10,"ev":"Sarah's talk will finish at 5pm. After that, tea and juice will be served in the Green Room, which is on the first floor.","hl":"juice","uz":"Saraning ma'ruzasi soat 17 da tugaydi. Shundan keyin birinchi qavatdagi Yashil xonada choy va sharbat beriladi.","why":"\"Tea and juice\" — choy va sharbat."}],"segs":[{"s":4.47,"e":7.26,"t":"You will hear a woman talking about a conference."},{"s":8.28,"e":12.99,"t":"Good morning and welcome to our seminar on the toy industry."},{"s":13.53,"e":23.17,"t":"I'd like to start by saying a few words about what you can expect from this seminar since some of the details on the original plan have changed."},{"s":23.64,"e":31.81,"t":"After the introduction by Sally Connor, Kenji Nakamura will give a talk. That's from 10am to 11am.","uz":"Salli Konnorning kirish so'zidan keyin Kenji Nakamura nutq so'zlaydi."},{"s":32.6,"e":39.58,"t":"He will tell you about the most recent developments in the toy industry in Japan and will show a short film."},{"s":40.06,"e":54.72,"t":"This will be followed by half an hour of questions. Then at 12 we'll have a break for lunch. This will be a buffet meal served in Victoria Hall which is on the opposite side of the building next to the library.","uz":"Shundan so'ng yarim soat savollarga ajratiladi. Keyin soat 12 da tushlik tanaffusi: u binoning qarama-qarshi tomonida, kutubxona yonidagi Viktoriya zalida shved stoli tarzida beriladi."},{"s":55.64,"e":61.5,"t":"After lunch, we'll return here for 'Toys in Britain - Success and Failure'."},{"s":62.1,"e":70.85,"t":"This talk will be given by Robert Price, who, as you know, is the owner of a chain of over 200 toy shops in the UK.","uz":"Bu ma'ruzani Robert Prays o'qiydi — bilasizki, u Buyuk Britaniyadagi 200 dan ortiq o'yinchoq do'konlari tarmog'ining egasi."},{"s":71.58,"e":79.04,"t":"The next talk, What's Next for Toys, will take place immediately after this at 3.30."},{"s":79.8,"e":84.61,"t":"This will be given by Sarah Smith, who is of course our sales manager.","uz":"Uni, albatta, bizning savdo menejerimiz Sara Smit o'qiydi."},{"s":85.34,"e":95.1,"t":"Sarah's talk will finish at 5pm. After that, tea and juice will be served in the Green Room, which is on the first floor.","uz":"Saraning ma'ruzasi soat 17 da tugaydi. Shundan keyin birinchi qavatdagi Yashil xonada choy va sharbat beriladi."},{"s":95.96,"e":99.97,"t":"Please join us there as this will be a chance for everyone to chat."}]},{"n":18,"title":"Sports Festival","dur":131.9,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"The Date"},{"k":"p","t":"30th June – {1} July"},{"k":"h","t":"The Opening Event"},{"k":"p","t":"Location: Prospect {2}"},{"k":"p","t":"Time: 12 p.m. – {3} p.m."},{"k":"p","t":"Workshops include: skateboarding, break-dancing, extreme {4}"},{"k":"h","t":"Further Information"},{"k":"p","t":"Look on the website for a timetable and a {5}"},{"k":"h","t":"Other Events"},{"k":"p","t":"Water sports: River Swimming Complex"},{"k":"p","t":"Track events: Athletics Stadium"},{"k":"p","t":"Indoor {6} games: Central Leisure"}],"items":[{"a":["13th","thirteenth","13"],"ps":19.77,"en":34.01,"si":3,"ev":"The International Sports Festival starts on 30 June, lasts for two weeks and ends on 13 July with prize-giving and fireworks. It's well worth attending. Here's why.","hl":"13","uz":"Xalqaro sport festivali 30-iyunda boshlanadi, ikki hafta davom etadi va 13-iyulda mukofotlash marosimi hamda mushakbozlik bilan yakunlanadi.","why":"30-iyun — boshlanishi (kitobda berilgan). Tugashi — 13-iyul."},{"a":["park"],"ps":35.1,"en":40.06,"si":4,"ev":"The fun starts on day one with a huge event in Prospect Park.","hl":"Park","uz":"Bayram birinchi kuniyoq Prospect bog'idagi katta tadbir bilan boshlanadi.","why":"\"Prospect Park\" — bog': park."},{"a":["6","six"],"ps":40.89,"en":50.33,"si":5,"ev":"Organisers will arrive early to set up, but the event for the public begins at 12pm and lasts all day until 6pm.","hl":"6","uz":"Tashkilotchilar tayyorgarlik uchun ertaroq keladi, lekin jamoatchilik uchun tadbir soat 12 da boshlanib, kun bo'yi — soat 6 gacha davom etadi.","why":"\"Arrive early\" — tashkilotchilar uchun (tuzoq). Tadbir 12 dan 6 gacha."},{"a":["cycling"],"ps":71.51,"en":76.16,"si":8,"ev":"You might also like to bring your bike and try some extreme cycling.","hl":"cycling","uz":"Velosipedingizni olib kelib, ekstremal velosport (extreme cycling) bilan shug'ullanib ko'rishingiz ham mumkin.","why":"\"Extreme cycling\" — bo'shliq: cycling. \"Bike\" — olib keladigan narsa, javob emas."},{"a":["map"],"ps":86.87,"en":100.03,"si":11,"ev":"To find out more information about exact times of each workshop, look on our website. You'll also be able to download a map which shows where everything will be in the park on the day.","hl":"map","uz":"Har bir mashg'ulotning aniq vaqtlari haqida ko'proq ma'lumot uchun saytimizga qarang. U yerdan bayram kuni bog'da hamma narsa qayerda bo'lishini ko'rsatadigan xaritani ham yuklab olishingiz mumkin.","why":"Saytda vaqt jadvali va map (xarita) bor."},{"a":["team"],"ps":114.55,"en":122.33,"si":14,"ev":"track events at the Athletic Stadium and you can also take part in indoor team games at Central Leisure.","hl":"team","uz":"Yengil atletika musobaqalari — Atletika stadionida, yopiq binodagi jamoaviy o'yinlarda esa Central Leisure'da qatnashishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Indoor team games\" — jamoaviy o'yinlar: team."}],"segs":[{"s":5.37,"e":9.6,"t":"Write one or two words or a number or a date or a time."},{"s":10.84,"e":14.43,"t":"You will hear a radio presenter talking about a sports festival."},{"s":15.74,"e":19.04,"t":"Are you wondering what to do over the summer holidays?"},{"s":19.77,"e":34.01,"t":"The International Sports Festival starts on 30 June, lasts for two weeks and ends on 13 July with prize-giving and fireworks. It's well worth attending. Here's why.","uz":"Xalqaro sport festivali 30-iyunda boshlanadi, ikki hafta davom etadi va 13-iyulda mukofotlash marosimi hamda mushakbozlik bilan yakunlanadi."},{"s":35.1,"e":40.06,"t":"The fun starts on day one with a huge event in Prospect Park.","uz":"Bayram birinchi kuniyoq Prospect bog'idagi katta tadbir bilan boshlanadi."},{"s":40.89,"e":50.33,"t":"Organisers will arrive early to set up, but the event for the public begins at 12pm and lasts all day until 6pm.","uz":"Tashkilotchilar tayyorgarlik uchun ertaroq keladi, lekin jamoatchilik uchun tadbir soat 12 da boshlanib, kun bo'yi — soat 6 gacha davom etadi."},{"s":51.16,"e":62.91,"t":"Throughout the day, many different clubs and companies will be giving free workshops, which means you'll be able to try sports that you may never have tried before."},{"s":64.31,"e":70.72,"t":"Some of the highlights of the opening event include skateboarding and breakdancing workshops."},{"s":71.51,"e":76.16,"t":"You might also like to bring your bike and try some extreme cycling.","uz":"Velosipedingizni olib kelib, ekstremal velosport (extreme cycling) bilan shug'ullanib ko'rishingiz ham mumkin."},{"s":77.08,"e":82.43,"t":"Before you start, an expert will check over your bike to make sure it's safe."},{"s":83.19,"e":85.47,"t":"There will also be a bike race."},{"s":86.87,"e":100.03,"t":"To find out more information about exact times of each workshop, look on our website. You'll also be able to download a map which shows where everything will be in the park on the day.","uz":"Har bir mashg'ulotning aniq vaqtlari haqida ko'proq ma'lumot uchun saytimizga qarang. U yerdan bayram kuni bog'da hamma narsa qayerda bo'lishini ko'rsatadigan xaritani ham yuklab olishingiz mumkin."},{"s":101.27,"e":108.16,"t":"For the remaining two weeks of the festival, you'll be able to enjoy further workshops and sessions in the area."},{"s":108.79,"e":113.89,"t":"Locations and events include water sports at River Swimming Complex,"},{"s":114.55,"e":122.33,"t":"track events at the Athletic Stadium and you can also take part in indoor team games at Central Leisure.","uz":"Yengil atletika musobaqalari — Atletika stadionida, yopiq binodagi jamoaviy o'yinlarda esa Central Leisure'da qatnashishingiz mumkin."},{"s":123.26,"e":126.49,"t":"This festival is the first of its kind in our town."},{"s":126.94,"e":129.98,"t":"and I really recommend you see what it's all about."}]},{"n":19,"title":"Dorset Chocolate Museum","dur":126.8,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Displays"},{"k":"p","t":"Exhibition showing the {1} of chocolate production"},{"k":"p","t":"See how chocolates and other {2} are made"},{"k":"h","t":"Opening times"},{"k":"p","t":"12.00 midday – 6.00 p.m."},{"k":"p","t":"July and August 12.00 midday – 8.00 p.m."},{"k":"p","t":"Not open in {3}"},{"k":"h","t":"Prices"},{"k":"p","t":"Adults: ten pounds"},{"k":"p","t":"Students: {4} pounds"},{"k":"h","t":"Group visits"},{"k":"p","t":"Discounts available for groups of at least {5} visitors"},{"k":"p","t":"Free {6} of chocolates"}],"items":[{"a":["history"],"ps":33.05,"en":40.54,"si":5,"ev":"Our fascinating displays will guide you through the history of chocolate making from its earliest use in South America to the modern day.","hl":"history","uz":"Qiziqarli ko'rgazmalarimiz shokolad tayyorlash tarixini Janubiy Amerikadagi ilk qo'llanishidan hozirgi kungacha ko'rsatib beradi.","why":"\"The history of chocolate making\" — tarix: history."},{"a":["sweets"],"ps":46.3,"en":55.26,"si":7,"ev":"Here you can watch our skilled chocolate makers making a variety of chocolate bars as well as other sweets and you can even have a try at making your own.","hl":"sweets","uz":"Bu yerda mohir shokoladchilarimiz turli shokolad plitkalari va boshqa shirinliklar tayyorlayotganini tomosha qilishingiz, hatto o'zingiz ham tayyorlab ko'rishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Other sweets\" — boshqa shirinliklar."},{"a":["January"],"ps":64.28,"en":72.96,"si":9,"ev":"From September to December we are open at weekends only. We are closed throughout January but open again from the 1st of February.","hl":"January","uz":"Sentabrdan dekabrgacha faqat dam olish kunlari ochiqmiz. Yanvar oyi davomida yopiqmiz, 1-fevraldan yana ochilamiz.","why":"September–December — faqat dam olish kunlari ochiq (yopiq emas!). Butunlay yopiq — January."},{"a":["8","eight"],"ps":73.75,"en":88.45,"si":10,"ev":"Admission is £10 for adults and £5 for children up to the age of 16, while children under five are free. Students pay £2 less, so that's £8, but only if they have a student ID card.","hl":"8","uz":"Kirish kattalar uchun 10 funt, 16 yoshgacha bolalar uchun 5 funt, besh yoshgacha bolalar bepul. Talabalar 2 funt kam to'laydi, ya'ni 8 funt, lekin faqat talaba guvohnomasi bo'lsa.","why":"\"£2 less\" — 10 − 2 = 8. Raqamlarni chalkashtirmang: 10 (kattalar), 5 (bolalar)."},{"a":["10","ten"],"ps":89.46,"en":94.21,"si":11,"ev":"Special reduced entrance fees are available for groups of 10 or more people.","hl":"10","uz":"10 va undan ortiq kishilik guruhlar uchun maxsus chegirmali narxlar bor.","why":"\"Groups of 10 or more\" — kamida 10 kishi."},{"a":["bag"],"ps":101.66,"en":110.21,"si":13,"ev":"All groups will be provided with a private tour guide and at the end each member of the group will receive a bag of lovely handmade chocolates.","hl":"bag","uz":"Barcha guruhlarga shaxsiy gid beriladi, oxirida esa har bir guruh a'zosi qo'lda tayyorlangan shokoladlar solingan xaltacha oladi.","why":"\"A bag of handmade chocolates\" — bir xalta shokolad. Chocolate boxes — do'konda sotiladi (tuzoq)."}],"segs":[{"s":5.14,"e":9.21,"t":"You will hear a recorded message giving information about a museum."},{"s":10.74,"e":18.88,"t":"This is the information line for the Dorset Chocolate Museum, the home of chocolate lovers and the ideal place to spend an afternoon."},{"s":19.8,"e":23.87,"t":"Do you know who used cocoa beans as money in the 16th century?"},{"s":24.34,"e":26.88,"t":"or where chocolate was drunk as a medicine."},{"s":28.02,"e":32.38,"t":"Dorset Chocolate Museum you'll find out about all this and more."},{"s":33.05,"e":40.54,"t":"Our fascinating displays will guide you through the history of chocolate making from its earliest use in South America to the modern day.","uz":"Qiziqarli ko'rgazmalarimiz shokolad tayyorlash tarixini Janubiy Amerikadagi ilk qo'llanishidan hozirgi kungacha ko'rsatib beradi."},{"s":41.11,"e":45.79,"t":"Then move on to the demonstration area of our small family run factory."},{"s":46.3,"e":55.26,"t":"Here you can watch our skilled chocolate makers making a variety of chocolate bars as well as other sweets and you can even have a try at making your own.","uz":"Bu yerda mohir shokoladchilarimiz turli shokolad plitkalari va boshqa shirinliklar tayyorlayotganini tomosha qilishingiz, hatto o'zingiz ham tayyorlab ko'rishingiz mumkin."},{"s":55.99,"e":63.39,"t":"We open seven days a week from 12 midday till 6pm, except in July and August when we are open until 8pm."},{"s":64.28,"e":72.96,"t":"From September to December we are open at weekends only. We are closed throughout January but open again from the 1st of February.","uz":"Sentabrdan dekabrgacha faqat dam olish kunlari ochiqmiz. Yanvar oyi davomida yopiqmiz, 1-fevraldan yana ochilamiz."},{"s":73.75,"e":88.45,"t":"Admission is £10 for adults and £5 for children up to the age of 16, while children under five are free. Students pay £2 less, so that's £8, but only if they have a student ID card.","uz":"Kirish kattalar uchun 10 funt, 16 yoshgacha bolalar uchun 5 funt, besh yoshgacha bolalar bepul. Talabalar 2 funt kam to'laydi, ya'ni 8 funt, lekin faqat talaba guvohnomasi bo'lsa."},{"s":89.46,"e":94.21,"t":"Special reduced entrance fees are available for groups of 10 or more people.","uz":"10 va undan ortiq kishilik guruhlar uchun maxsus chegirmali narxlar bor."},{"s":94.74,"e":100.89,"t":"We can also make special arrangements for schools on weekdays between 12 and 4pm."},{"s":101.66,"e":110.21,"t":"All groups will be provided with a private tour guide and at the end each member of the group will receive a bag of lovely handmade chocolates.","uz":"Barcha guruhlarga shaxsiy gid beriladi, oxirida esa har bir guruh a'zosi qo'lda tayyorlangan shokoladlar solingan xaltacha oladi."},{"s":111.13,"e":116.77,"t":"Our special range of chocolate boxes and bars is always available to buy in our gift shop."},{"s":117.4,"e":125.05,"t":"For more details, phone the gift shop on 01632 960 054."}]},{"n":20,"title":"Welcome to the Resort!","dur":122.7,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Meals"},{"k":"p","t":"Meals will be served in the dining room which is located at the {1} of the hotel."},{"k":"p","t":"Breakfast {2} a.m. – 9 a.m."},{"k":"p","t":"Lunch 12 p.m. – 3 p.m."},{"k":"p","t":"Dinner 8 p.m. – 11 p.m. (includes traditional {3} twice a week)"},{"k":"h","t":"Family Activities – Mornings"},{"k":"p","t":"Trips include visits to {4} ruins and monuments."},{"k":"p","t":"Visit to an outdoor market every {5}"},{"k":"h","t":"Afternoons"},{"k":"p","t":"Visit the beach (only {6} away)"},{"k":"p","t":"Stay by the hotel swimming pool"}],"items":[{"a":["front"],"ps":32.86,"en":37.44,"si":5,"ev":"The dining room is at the front of the hotel, next to the fitness centre.","hl":"front","uz":"Ovqatlanish xonasi mehmonxonaning old tomonida, fitnes markazi yonida joylashgan.","why":"\"At the front of the hotel\" — old tomonda."},{"a":["7","seven"],"ps":37.98,"en":44.32,"si":6,"ev":"For your information, breakfast is served between 7am and 9am.","hl":"7","uz":"Ma'lumot uchun: nonushta ertalab 7 dan 9 gacha beriladi.","why":"Nonushta: 7 am – 9 am. Bo'shliqqa boshlanish vaqti: 7."},{"a":["music"],"ps":55.48,"en":61.12,"si":8,"ev":"Traditional music is played by local musicians twice a week during dinner.","hl":"music","uz":"Haftada ikki marta kechki ovqat paytida mahalliy musiqachilar an'anaviy musiqa ijro etadi.","why":"\"Traditional music… twice a week\" — an'anaviy musiqa."},{"a":["local"],"ps":65.75,"en":81.82,"si":10,"ev":"There are family trips most mornings which you can join if you like. These include visits to local places of interest, including the ruins and various monuments. I'll give you more details about those later.","hl":"local","uz":"Ko'p kunlari ertalab oilaviy sayohatlar bo'ladi. Ular mahalliy diqqatga sazovor joylarga, jumladan xarobalar va turli yodgorliklarga tashriflarni o'z ichiga oladi.","why":"\"Local places of interest, including the ruins and various monuments\" — mahalliy xarobalar va yodgorliklar."},{"a":["Thursday"],"ps":82.58,"en":93.89,"si":11,"ev":"You can also visit an outdoor market where you'll be able to find souvenirs to take home. That's only on Thursdays so don't miss it.","hl":"Thursdays","uz":"Shuningdek, uyga esdalik sovg'alari topishingiz mumkin bo'lgan ochiq bozorga borishingiz mumkin. U faqat payshanba kunlari bo'ladi, o'tkazib yubormang.","why":"\"Only on Thursdays\" — har payshanba."},{"a":["5","five","five minutes","5 minutes"],"ps":94.55,"en":104.48,"si":12,"ev":"In the afternoons you can either walk to the beach, which is just five minutes away, or you can relax by the hotel swimming pool.","hl":"five","uz":"Tushdan keyin piyoda atigi besh daqiqalik masofadagi plyajga borishingiz yoki mehmonxona hovuzi yonida dam olishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Just five minutes away\" — 5 daqiqa."}],"segs":[{"s":4.73,"e":9.21,"t":"You will hear a woman talking to a group of families about their holiday."},{"s":10.26,"e":12.19,"t":"Good afternoon families."},{"s":12.63,"e":20.54,"t":"It's lovely to see you all at our wonderful resort. You've certainly got some great weather for your holiday."},{"s":21.11,"e":29.28,"t":"Now, in a moment you'll be shown up to your rooms. Then, in about an hour's time, at about one o'clock,"},{"s":29.78,"e":32.35,"t":"A light lunch will be served in the dining room."},{"s":32.86,"e":37.44,"t":"The dining room is at the front of the hotel, next to the fitness centre.","uz":"Ovqatlanish xonasi mehmonxonaning old tomonida, fitnes markazi yonida joylashgan."},{"s":37.98,"e":44.32,"t":"For your information, breakfast is served between 7am and 9am.","uz":"Ma'lumot uchun: nonushta ertalab 7 dan 9 gacha beriladi."},{"s":44.79,"e":54.69,"t":"Lunch is from 12pm to 3pm and dinner is served in the evening between 8pm and 11pm."},{"s":55.48,"e":61.12,"t":"Traditional music is played by local musicians twice a week during dinner.","uz":"Haftada ikki marta kechki ovqat paytida mahalliy musiqachilar an'anaviy musiqa ijro etadi."},{"s":61.78,"e":65.18,"t":"Now, a few words about activities."},{"s":65.75,"e":81.82,"t":"There are family trips most mornings which you can join if you like. These include visits to local places of interest, including the ruins and various monuments. I'll give you more details about those later.","uz":"Ko'p kunlari ertalab oilaviy sayohatlar bo'ladi. Ular mahalliy diqqatga sazovor joylarga, jumladan xarobalar va turli yodgorliklarga tashriflarni o'z ichiga oladi."},{"s":82.58,"e":93.89,"t":"You can also visit an outdoor market where you'll be able to find souvenirs to take home. That's only on Thursdays so don't miss it.","uz":"Shuningdek, uyga esdalik sovg'alari topishingiz mumkin bo'lgan ochiq bozorga borishingiz mumkin. U faqat payshanba kunlari bo'ladi, o'tkazib yubormang."},{"s":94.55,"e":104.48,"t":"In the afternoons you can either walk to the beach, which is just five minutes away, or you can relax by the hotel swimming pool.","uz":"Tushdan keyin piyoda atigi besh daqiqalik masofadagi plyajga borishingiz yoki mehmonxona hovuzi yonida dam olishingiz mumkin."},{"s":105.3,"e":107.71,"t":"That's it for now, I think."},{"s":108.63,"e":119.93,"t":"you like your rooms. Please stay behind if you have any questions. Otherwise, I'll see you in the dining room in about an hour. Thank you very much."}]},{"n":21,"title":"Fly High","dur":233.4,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Andreana's project is about {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"After university, her father worked as a teacher in a {2} school."},{"k":"p","t":"On his first flight {3} passengers were travelling to Italy on his plane."},{"k":"p","t":"Difficult passengers and bad {4} are problems that a pilot has to deal with."},{"k":"p","t":"Andreana's father says that some plane travellers feel that they lose {5} of their life when flying."},{"k":"p","t":"She says that he drinks a cup of {6} just after his plane has taken off."}],"items":[{"a":["jobs"],"ps":21.37,"en":27.17,"si":2,"ev":"I chose the first project which focuses on jobs. I found the other topic on the environment a bit difficult.","hl":"jobs","uz":"Men ish (kasblar) mavzusidagi birinchi loyihani tanladim.","why":"\"Focuses on jobs\" — kasblar mavzusi. Environment — boshqa mavzu (tuzoq)."},{"a":["primary"],"ps":42.97,"en":45.66,"si":6,"ev":"He taught in a primary school and he really enjoyed it.","hl":"primary","uz":"U boshlang'ich maktabda dars bergan va bu ish unga juda yoqqan.","why":"\"Primary school\" — boshlang'ich maktab."},{"a":["80","eighty"],"ps":55.77,"en":65.28,"si":8,"ev":"He will never forget the first flight when he was responsible for a plane with 80 happy holidaymakers on their way to Italy. Six more people were working on the plane.","hl":"80","uz":"U birinchi parvozini hech qachon unutmaydi: o'shanda Italiyaga ketayotgan 80 nafar xursand sayyoh bor samolyot uchun javobgar edi; samolyotda yana olti kishi ishlagan.","why":"80 — yo'lovchilar. 6 — ekipaj a'zolari (tuzoq)."},{"a":["weather"],"ps":82.74,"en":88.93,"si":13,"ev":"However, sometimes unexpected things happen during a flight, such as bad weather or difficult passengers.","hl":"weather","uz":"Biroq parvoz paytida ba'zan kutilmagan narsalar yuz beradi, masalan, yomon ob-havo yoki qiyin yo'lovchilar.","why":"\"Bad weather or difficult passengers\" — yomon ob-havo."},{"a":["control"],"ps":96.6,"en":105.85,"si":15,"ev":"My father believes that what nervous passengers have in common is that they need to be in control of their life and when they get on a plane they have to give up that control.","hl":"control","uz":"Otamning fikricha, qo'rqoq yo'lovchilarning umumiy jihati — ular o'z hayotlarini nazorat qilishni xohlashadi, samolyotga chiqqanda esa bu nazoratdan voz kechishga majbur bo'lishadi.","why":"\"Lose control\" — nazoratni yo'qotish: control."},{"a":["coffee"],"ps":107.54,"en":118.97,"si":16,"ev":"He always does his best to make passengers feel relaxed on the flight. Once he has taken off and he is cruising in the sky, he always has a coffee to make him feel extra awake and ready for anything.","hl":"coffee","uz":"Samolyot havoga ko'tarilib, osmonda tekis uchayotganida u doim qahva ichadi — bu unga yanada tetik va hamma narsaga tayyor bo'lish hissini beradi.","why":"\"He always has a coffee\" — qahva."}],"segs":[{"s":4.6,"e":10.46,"t":"You will hear a student called Andriana giving a presentation to her class about her father's job."},{"s":15.96,"e":20.77,"t":"Hi everyone, I have chosen to tell you about my father's job for the project we had for today."},{"s":21.37,"e":27.17,"t":"I chose the first project which focuses on jobs. I found the other topic on the environment a bit difficult.","uz":"Men ish (kasblar) mavzusidagi birinchi loyihani tanladim."},{"s":29.02,"e":32.61,"t":"My father is a pilot for an international airline company."},{"s":33.21,"e":38.08,"t":"He's been flying people around the world for the last 16 years and he loves his job."},{"s":38.81,"e":42.3,"t":"After he graduated from university, he became a teacher."},{"s":42.97,"e":45.66,"t":"He taught in a primary school and he really enjoyed it.","uz":"U boshlang'ich maktabda dars bergan va bu ish unga juda yoqqan."},{"s":46.26,"e":54.24,"t":"However, he'd always had a dream that one day he would fly, so he decided to go for an important career change and train as a pilot."},{"s":55.77,"e":65.28,"t":"He will never forget the first flight when he was responsible for a plane with 80 happy holidaymakers on their way to Italy. Six more people were working on the plane.","uz":"U birinchi parvozini hech qachon unutmaydi: o'shanda Italiyaga ketayotgan 80 nafar xursand sayyoh bor samolyot uchun javobgar edi; samolyotda yana olti kishi ishlagan."},{"s":65.91,"e":67.33,"t":"He was very nervous."},{"s":67.77,"e":71.84,"t":"Everything went well though and he was so pleased when his first flight was behind him."},{"s":73.27,"e":78.43,"t":"He often gets nervous, people asking him questions about how dangerous flying really is."},{"s":79.29,"e":82.11,"t":"He tells them that it is the safest way to travel."},{"s":82.74,"e":88.93,"t":"However, sometimes unexpected things happen during a flight, such as bad weather or difficult passengers.","uz":"Biroq parvoz paytida ba'zan kutilmagan narsalar yuz beradi, masalan, yomon ob-havo yoki qiyin yo'lovchilar."},{"s":89.62,"e":95.01,"t":"But he says that the most important thing a pilot can do is to always stay calm."},{"s":96.6,"e":105.85,"t":"My father believes that what nervous passengers have in common is that they need to be in control of their life and when they get on a plane they have to give up that control.","uz":"Otamning fikricha, qo'rqoq yo'lovchilarning umumiy jihati — ular o'z hayotlarini nazorat qilishni xohlashadi, samolyotga chiqqanda esa bu nazoratdan voz kechishga majbur bo'lishadi."},{"s":107.54,"e":118.97,"t":"He always does his best to make passengers feel relaxed on the flight. Once he has taken off and he is cruising in the sky, he always has a coffee to make him feel extra awake and ready for anything.","uz":"Samolyot havoga ko'tarilib, osmonda tekis uchayotganida u doim qahva ichadi — bu unga yanada tetik va hamma narsaga tayyor bo'lish hissini beradi."}]},{"n":22,"title":"School Trip to the Castle","dur":257.4,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Time to meet at school gate","t":"{1}"},{"k":"row","l":"Need to bring","t":"a {2}"},{"k":"row","l":"Morning activity","t":"{3} in the garden"},{"k":"row","l":"Afternoon activity","t":"trip on a {4}"},{"k":"row","l":"Hand in projects by","t":"{5}"},{"k":"row","l":"Castle website","t":"www.{6}.castle.com"}],"items":[{"a":["8.40","eight forty"],"ps":20.92,"en":27.97,"si":3,"ev":"The coach will be leaving the school at 9.10, so you all need to be there at 8.40 and no later.","hl":"8.40","uz":"Avtobus maktabdan soat 9:10 da jo'naydi, shuning uchun hammangiz 8:40 da, kechikmasdan o'sha yerda bo'lishingiz kerak.","why":"9.10 — avtobus jo'nash vaqti (tuzoq). Uchrashuv vaqti — 8.40."},{"a":["notebook"],"ps":32.31,"en":43.2,"si":5,"ev":"We will be doing all sorts of activities during the day, but don't forget that you will be doing a project on the castle so you need to bring a book, I mean a notebook with you.","hl":"notebook","uz":"Kun davomida turli mashg'ulotlar bo'ladi, lekin qal'a haqida loyiha qilishingizni unutmang — shuning uchun kitob, yo'q, daftar olib keling.","why":"\"A book, I mean a notebook\" — gapiruvchi o'zini tuzatdi: notebook. Kamera olib kelish shart emas."},{"a":["painting"],"ps":57.82,"en":67.65,"si":9,"ev":"We won't be going on a guided tour because I know how bored you all get, so instead we will go to the gardens where we will have a special painting class.","hl":"painting","uz":"Gidli ekskursiyaga bormaymiz, chunki qanchalik zerikishingizni bilaman — o'rniga bog'larga borib, maxsus rasm chizish darsida qatnashamiz.","why":"Guided tour — bo'lmaydi (tuzoq). Bog'da — painting class."},{"a":["boat"],"ps":82.81,"en":88.57,"si":13,"ev":"No, that doesn't mean you will go and eat cake. We will be going on a boat down the river.","hl":"boat","uz":"Yo'q, bu tort yeyishga borasiz degani emas. Biz daryo bo'ylab qayiqda sayr qilamiz.","why":"\"A boat down the river\" — qayiq sayri."},{"a":["Tuesday","Tuesday afternoon"],"ps":93.62,"en":103.65,"si":15,"ev":"Now those projects I mentioned earlier will be marked by Friday afternoon, so they all need to be handed in by Tuesday afternoon. Not Wednesday morning.","hl":"Tuesday","uz":"Loyihalar juma kuni tushdan keyin tekshiriladi, shuning uchun ularni seshanba tushdan keyingacha topshirish kerak — chorshanba ertalab emas.","why":"Friday — tekshirish kuni, Wednesday — noto'g'ri kun (tuzoq). Topshirish — Tuesday."},{"a":["Arundel"],"ps":110.1,"en":127.01,"si":17,"ev":"If you want more information to help you write your projects, you can look on the castle website, which is www.arundel.castle.com. I'll spell that for you. That's A-R-U-N-D-E-L.","hl":"arundel","uz":"Loyihangiz uchun ko'proq ma'lumot kerak bo'lsa, qal'a saytiga qarang: www.arundel.castle.com. Harflab aytaman: A-R-U-N-D-E-L.","why":"Harflab aytilgan nom: Arundel."}],"segs":[{"s":4.89,"e":9.37,"t":"You will hear a teacher telling a group of students about a trip they are going on."},{"s":14.78,"e":15.84,"t":"Good morning everyone."},{"s":16.63,"e":20.29,"t":"I want to tell you about the school trip to the castle next week."},{"s":20.92,"e":27.97,"t":"The coach will be leaving the school at 9.10, so you all need to be there at 8.40 and no later.","uz":"Avtobus maktabdan soat 9:10 da jo'naydi, shuning uchun hammangiz 8:40 da, kechikmasdan o'sha yerda bo'lishingiz kerak."},{"s":28.6,"e":31.26,"t":"If anyone is late, we will not wait for you."},{"s":32.31,"e":43.2,"t":"We will be doing all sorts of activities during the day, but don't forget that you will be doing a project on the castle so you need to bring a book, I mean a notebook with you.","uz":"Kun davomida turli mashg'ulotlar bo'ladi, lekin qal'a haqida loyiha qilishingizni unutmang — shuning uchun kitob, yo'q, daftar olib keling."},{"s":44.25,"e":49.18,"t":"Don't worry about bringing a camera as on the last trip, two people lost their cameras."},{"s":50.01,"e":53.34,"t":"You can always use your phones if you want to take pictures."},{"s":54.2,"e":57.21,"t":"We should arrive at the castle by 9.45."},{"s":57.82,"e":67.65,"t":"We won't be going on a guided tour because I know how bored you all get, so instead we will go to the gardens where we will have a special painting class.","uz":"Gidli ekskursiyaga bormaymiz, chunki qanchalik zerikishingizni bilaman — o'rniga bog'larga borib, maxsus rasm chizish darsida qatnashamiz."},{"s":68.25,"e":70.21,"t":"The gardens are very beautiful."},{"s":71.16,"e":75.04,"t":"All your paintings will be exhibited in the school hall next week."},{"s":76.09,"e":82.14,"t":"After lunch, you can have a look around the castle for an hour, which will be followed by a special treat."},{"s":82.81,"e":88.57,"t":"No, that doesn't mean you will go and eat cake. We will be going on a boat down the river.","uz":"Yo'q, bu tort yeyishga borasiz degani emas. Biz daryo bo'ylab qayiqda sayr qilamiz."},{"s":89.21,"e":92.54,"t":"I know that this is a trip that you will really enjoy."},{"s":93.62,"e":103.65,"t":"Now those projects I mentioned earlier will be marked by Friday afternoon, so they all need to be handed in by Tuesday afternoon. Not Wednesday morning.","uz":"Loyihalar juma kuni tushdan keyin tekshiriladi, shuning uchun ularni seshanba tushdan keyingacha topshirish kerak — chorshanba ertalab emas."},{"s":104.18,"e":109.05,"t":"Us poor teachers have lots to do, so you must hand your projects in on time."},{"s":110.1,"e":127.01,"t":"If you want more information to help you write your projects, you can look on the castle website, which is www.arundel.castle.com. I'll spell that for you. That's A-R-U-N-D-E-L.","uz":"Loyihangiz uchun ko'proq ma'lumot kerak bo'lsa, qal'a saytiga qarang: www.arundel.castle.com. Harflab aytaman: A-R-U-N-D-E-L."},{"s":127.9,"e":130.21,"t":"Okay, you can go to your lessons now."}]},{"n":23,"title":"Julie's trip to Venice","dur":257.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"You can use bus, {1} or boat to go to Venice from the airport."},{"k":"p","t":"Julie and her parents started their journey to Arsenale at {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The museum card costs £{3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Julie's favourite place to walk was over {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"The best food to eat in Venice is {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Julie's parents bought some toy {6} for her relatives."}],"items":[{"a":["train"],"ps":25.14,"en":34.08,"si":4,"ev":"It's very easy to get from the airport to Venice as you can either go by train or bus from the airport or you can do it the more romantic way which is by boat.","hl":"train","uz":"Aeroportdan Venetsiyaga borish juda oson: aeroportdan poyezd yoki avtobusda borishingiz mumkin, yoki romantikroq usul — qayiqda.","why":"Kitobda bus va boat berilgan. Yetishmayotgani — train."},{"a":["10.15","10:15","ten fifteen"],"ps":54.1,"en":61.66,"si":8,"ev":"We were on the boat for over an hour before we got to our stop. We set off at 10.15 and we arrived there at 11.30.","hl":"10.15","uz":"Bekatimizga yetguncha qayiqda bir soatdan ko'proq bo'ldik. Soat 10:15 da yo'lga chiqib, 11:30 da yetib keldik.","why":"10.15 — jo'nash (\"set off\"). 11.30 — yetib kelish (tuzoq)."},{"a":["30","thirty"],"ps":68.02,"en":86.33,"si":10,"ev":"The cheapest way of travelling around Venice is of course on foot but after a while you will probably get very tired. You can buy a three day ticket to use on the Vaporetti which only costs £20. We also bought a museum card for £30 which we could use to go into the museums, art galleries and churches.","hl":"30","uz":"Venetsiyada eng arzon yurish usuli — piyoda, lekin tez charchaysiz. Vaporetto uchun 3 kunlik chipta atigi 20 funt. Biz yana 30 funtga muzey kartasi oldik — u bilan muzeylar, galereyalar va cherkovlarga kirsa bo'ladi.","why":"£20 — vaporetto chiptasi (tuzoq). Muzey kartasi — £30."},{"a":["bridges"],"ps":96.92,"en":102.14,"si":13,"ev":"The thing I enjoyed most was walking over the many beautiful bridges and watching the boats beneath us.","hl":"bridges","uz":"Eng yoqqan narsa — ko'plab chiroyli ko'priklar ustidan yurib, ostimizdan o'tayotgan qayiqlarni tomosha qilish edi.","why":"\"Walking over the many beautiful bridges\" — ko'priklar."},{"a":["fish"],"ps":109.4,"en":115.74,"si":16,"ev":"As you would expect, there are plenty of pizza and pasta restaurants, but the nicest thing to eat in Venice is fish.","hl":"fish","uz":"Kutilganidek, pitsa va makaron restoranlari ko'p, lekin Venetsiyada eng mazali taom — baliq.","why":"Pizza va pasta — tuzoq. \"The nicest thing to eat\" — fish."},{"a":["boats"],"ps":120.89,"en":127.97,"si":18,"ev":"I took many photos for my friends and bought lots of Italian sweets. My parents bought some toy boats for our cousins.","hl":"boats","uz":"Do'stlarim uchun ko'p suratga oldim va italyan shirinliklarini sotib oldim. Ota-onam esa jiyanlarimizga o'yinchoq qayiqchalar olishdi.","why":"Sweets — Julining o'zi olgan (tuzoq). Ota-onasi — toy boats."}],"segs":[{"s":4.79,"e":9.57,"t":"You will hear a student called Julie talking to her class about a trip to Venice."},{"s":14.94,"e":19.23,"t":"Hi everyone! I'm going to tell you all about my wonderful trip to Venice last week."},{"s":19.77,"e":20.89,"t":"I went with my family."},{"s":21.37,"e":24.25,"t":"We arrived on Saturday morning at about 10am."},{"s":25.14,"e":34.08,"t":"It's very easy to get from the airport to Venice as you can either go by train or bus from the airport or you can do it the more romantic way which is by boat.","uz":"Aeroportdan Venetsiyaga borish juda oson: aeroportdan poyezd yoki avtobusda borishingiz mumkin, yoki romantikroq usul — qayiqda."},{"s":35.99,"e":42.62,"t":"The boats are called Vaporetti and they are very long and narrow so that they can sail down the canals easily."},{"s":43.45,"e":49.18,"t":"The wonderful thing about going by boat is that you can see a lot of the city before you've even checked into your hotel."},{"s":50.26,"e":52.99,"t":"We stayed in an area of Venice called Arsenal."},{"s":54.1,"e":61.66,"t":"We were on the boat for over an hour before we got to our stop. We set off at 10.15 and we arrived there at 11.30.","uz":"Bekatimizga yetguncha qayiqda bir soatdan ko'proq bo'ldik. Soat 10:15 da yo'lga chiqib, 11:30 da yetib keldik."},{"s":62.65,"e":66.43,"t":"On the way, we cruised past most of the outside of the city."},{"s":68.02,"e":86.33,"t":"The cheapest way of travelling around Venice is of course on foot but after a while you will probably get very tired. You can buy a three day ticket to use on the Vaporetti which only costs £20. We also bought a museum card for £30 which we could use to go into the museums, art galleries and churches.","uz":"Venetsiyada eng arzon yurish usuli — piyoda, lekin tez charchaysiz. Vaporetto uchun 3 kunlik chipta atigi 20 funt. Biz yana 30 funtga muzey kartasi oldik — u bilan muzeylar, galereyalar va cherkovlarga kirsa bo'ladi."},{"s":86.87,"e":88.51,"t":"And that saved us a lot of money."},{"s":90.65,"e":96.29,"t":"Apart from its fantastic buildings and squares, Venice is most famous for its canals."},{"s":96.92,"e":102.14,"t":"The thing I enjoyed most was walking over the many beautiful bridges and watching the boats beneath us.","uz":"Eng yoqqan narsa — ko'plab chiroyli ko'priklar ustidan yurib, ostimizdan o'tayotgan qayiqlarni tomosha qilish edi."},{"s":103.35,"e":105.76,"t":"Now I'd like to mention the food in Venice."},{"s":106.3,"e":108.8,"t":"There are plenty of restaurants all over the city."},{"s":109.4,"e":115.74,"t":"As you would expect, there are plenty of pizza and pasta restaurants, but the nicest thing to eat in Venice is fish.","uz":"Kutilganidek, pitsa va makaron restoranlari ko'p, lekin Venetsiyada eng mazali taom — baliq."},{"s":116.66,"e":120.09,"t":"On the last day, we sat and drank fresh juice on the Grand Canal."},{"s":120.89,"e":127.97,"t":"I took many photos for my friends and bought lots of Italian sweets. My parents bought some toy boats for our cousins.","uz":"Do'stlarim uchun ko'p suratga oldim va italyan shirinliklarini sotib oldim. Ota-onam esa jiyanlarimizga o'yinchoq qayiqchalar olishdi."},{"s":128.41,"e":130.46,"t":"It was the perfect city holiday."}]},{"n":24,"title":"A Film Actor","dur":228.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Roger arrives at the film studio at {1} a.m."},{"k":"p","t":"A woman does his {2} after someone has brushed his hair."},{"k":"p","t":"Roger is playing a police {3} in this new film."},{"k":"p","t":"Filming is delayed because the film {4} is often late."},{"k":"p","t":"When filming ends, Roger puts on his usual {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Roger has {6} after he gets home and sleeps early."}],"items":[{"a":["5","five"],"ps":16.57,"en":40.45,"si":1,"ev":"Every day I get up at 4 in the morning and I have to be ready by 4.30 to get in the car to the studio… as the studio is only half an hour away, I'm there at 5.","hl":"5","uz":"Har kuni ertalab soat 4 da turaman, 4:30 da studiyaga boradigan mashinaga tayyor bo'lishim kerak… studiya atigi yarim soatlik yo'lda, shuning uchun 5 da o'sha yerdaman.","why":"4 — uyg'onish, 4.30 — mashinaga chiqish (tuzoqlar). Studiyaga yetib kelish — 5."},{"a":["make-up","makeup"],"ps":41.46,"en":58.85,"si":2,"ev":"When she finishes doing my hair, I don't have to move from the chair because the make-up lady comes to me and prepares me for filming.","hl":"make-up","uz":"Sartarosh sochimni tugatgach, o'rindiqdan turishim shart emas — grimchi ayol kelib, meni suratga olishga tayyorlaydi.","why":"Sochni sartarosh taraydi, keyin ayol make-up (grim) qiladi."},{"a":["officer"],"ps":59.7,"en":64.13,"si":3,"ev":"At the moment I'm playing a police officer so I don't need a lot of makeup.","hl":"officer","uz":"Hozir men politsiya xodimini o'ynayapman, shuning uchun ko'p grim kerak emas.","why":"Monster — oldingi filmdagi roli (tuzoq). Hozir — police officer."},{"a":["director"],"ps":80.02,"en":91.87,"si":7,"ev":"At this point I am now ready to act, but it is never like that. The film director is either late or the engineers haven't finished with the scenery or lights. We don't usually start on time.","hl":"director","uz":"Shu paytga kelib aktyorlik qilishga tayyor bo'laman, lekin hech qachon bunday bo'lmaydi: yo kino rejissyori kechikadi, yo muhandislar dekoratsiya yoki chiroqlarni tugatmagan bo'ladi.","why":"Engineers ham sabab bo'lishi mumkin, lekin \"late\" — rejissyor (director)."},{"a":["clothes"],"ps":98.52,"en":105.34,"si":9,"ev":"This takes all day until about 5pm when they remove my makeup and I get changed back into my normal clothes.","hl":"clothes","uz":"Bu kun bo'yi, taxminan soat 17 gacha davom etadi, keyin grimimni olib tashlashadi va o'z oddiy kiyimlarimni kiyaman.","why":"\"Changed back into my normal clothes\" — odatdagi kiyim."},{"a":["dinner"],"ps":105.78,"en":115.13,"si":10,"ev":"A car then takes me home, where I have dinner and go to bed, usually about 10pm.","hl":"dinner","uz":"Keyin mashina meni uyga olib boradi, kechki ovqatni yeb, odatda soat 22 larda uxlayman.","why":"\"Have dinner and go to bed\" — kechki ovqat."}],"segs":[{"s":4.89,"e":11.36,"t":"You will hear a film actor called Roger talking on the school radio about his typical day on a film set."},{"s":16.57,"e":40.45,"t":"Hi everyone, today I will tell you about my typical day filming. It sounds like a great job, but it really is very tiring. Every day I get up at 4 in the morning and I have to be ready by 4.30 to get in the car to the studio. In the winter it's still dark and as the studio is only half an hour away, I'm there at 5 and I don't get a chance to have a quick sleep."},{"s":41.46,"e":58.85,"t":"As soon as I get to the studio, I go to the hairdresser who brushes my hair into the hairstyle of the character I'm playing. This usually takes about half an hour. When she finishes doing my hair, I don't have to move from the chair because the makeup lady comes to me and prepares me for filming."},{"s":59.7,"e":64.13,"t":"At the moment I'm playing a police officer so I don't need a lot of makeup.","uz":"Hozir men politsiya xodimini o'ynayapman, shuning uchun ko'p grim kerak emas."},{"s":64.6,"e":71.93,"t":"In my last film, I played the part of a big monster and I needed a lot of makeup which took five hours to do."},{"s":72.6,"e":75.81,"t":"wasn't comfortable sitting in the same chair for such a long time."},{"s":76.79,"e":79.55,"t":"After makeup, I am given my costume to put on."},{"s":80.02,"e":91.87,"t":"At this point I am now ready to act, but it is never like that. The film director is either late or the engineers haven't finished with the scenery or lights. We don't usually start on time.","uz":"Shu paytga kelib aktyorlik qilishga tayyor bo'laman, lekin hech qachon bunday bo'lmaydi: yo kino rejissyori kechikadi, yo muhandislar dekoratsiya yoki chiroqlarni tugatmagan bo'ladi."},{"s":92.92,"e":97.6,"t":"When they are ready, I go into the studio and we act out the different scenes."},{"s":98.52,"e":105.34,"t":"This takes all day until about 5pm when they remove my makeup and I get changed back into my normal clothes.","uz":"Bu kun bo'yi, taxminan soat 17 gacha davom etadi, keyin grimimni olib tashlashadi va o'z oddiy kiyimlarimni kiyaman."},{"s":105.78,"e":115.13,"t":"A car then takes me home, where I have dinner and go to bed, usually about 10pm. Then the same happens the next day, and every day during filming."},{"s":115.58,"e":117.31,"t":"and that's my typical day."}]},{"n":25,"title":"Radio Presenter","dur":257.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"At university Jack studied {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Before the show Jack drinks {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Jack's favourite part of the job is {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Jack was embarrassed when he couldn't remember a {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"If Jack wasn't a radio presenter he would be a {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Jack will be doing a charity show at Hatfield {6} at the weekend."}],"items":[{"a":["history"],"ps":24.47,"en":36.29,"si":4,"ev":"I started doing DJ work for the University radio station. Strangely, I wasn't studying music or art. In fact, I was a history student, but I've always loved music.","hl":"history","uz":"Universitet radiosida DJ bo'lib ishlay boshladim. Qizig'i, men musiqa yoki san'atni o'qimaganman — aslida tarix talabasi edim, lekin musiqani doim sevganman.","why":"Music va art — tuzoq. U history o'qigan."},{"a":["tea"],"ps":39.9,"en":54.17,"si":6,"ev":"I start at 6am and I'm not much of a breakfast person so I don't eat before the show. Everyone eats and drinks loads of strong coffee but I'm a tea man myself. One big cup and then I'm ready to start.","hl":"tea","uz":"Ishni ertalab soat 6 da boshlayman va nonushta qiladigan odam emasman, shuning uchun ko'rsatuvdan oldin ovqatlanmayman. Hamma kuchli qahva ichadi, men esa choyni yaxshi ko'raman — bitta katta piyola, keyin boshlashga tayyorman.","why":"Coffee — boshqalar ichadi (tuzoq). Jek — tea."},{"a":["interviews"],"ps":60.38,"en":67.26,"si":8,"ev":"I love my job because I get to play great music. The best thing of all is when I get to do interviews.","hl":"interviews","uz":"Ishimni yaxshi ko'raman, chunki zo'r musiqa qo'yaman. Lekin eng yaxshisi — intervyu olish.","why":"\"Best thing of all… interviews\" — eng yoqqan qism."},{"a":["name"],"ps":83.13,"en":90.94,"si":11,"ev":"It's not that I forget dates or times or anything like that, but once in the middle of talking to a politician, I forgot their name.","hl":"name","uz":"Sanalar yoki vaqtlarni unutaman emas, lekin bir safar siyosatchi bilan gaplashayotib, uning ismini unutib qo'ydim.","why":"Dates va times — unutmaydi (tuzoq). Unutgani — name."},{"a":["reporter"],"ps":100.22,"en":109.37,"si":14,"ev":"I was always interested in teaching or acting, but if I changed careers now, I would definitely be a reporter of some kind as I love talking to people.","hl":"reporter","uz":"Doim o'qituvchilik yoki aktyorlikka qiziqqanman, lekin hozir kasbimni o'zgartirsam, albatta qandaydir muxbir bo'lardim, chunki odamlar bilan gaplashishni yaxshi ko'raman.","why":"Teaching va acting — oldingi qiziqishlari (tuzoq). Hozir — reporter."},{"a":["house"],"ps":113.37,"en":129.66,"si":16,"ev":"If any of you are free this weekend and aren't too busy studying or going to clubs, why not come and see me at a charity event I'm doing at Hatfield House? If you want to make a note of that, it's spelt H A T F I E L D House.","hl":"House","uz":"Bu hafta oxiri bo'sh bo'lsangiz, Hatfield House'da o'tkazadigan xayriya tadbirimga keling. Yozib olmoqchi bo'lsangiz: H-A-T-F-I-E-L-D house.","why":"\"Hatfield House\" — bo'shliq: house."}],"segs":[{"s":5.14,"e":11.36,"t":"You will hear a man called Jack Pindar talking to a group of students about his job as a radio presenter."},{"s":16.44,"e":17.12,"t":"Good morning."},{"s":17.72,"e":20.45,"t":"Thanks for inviting me to come and talk to you all today."},{"s":21.14,"e":23.87,"t":"I have been a radio presenter for 10 years now."},{"s":24.47,"e":36.29,"t":"I started doing DJ work for the University radio station. Strangely, I wasn't studying music or art. In fact, I was a history student, but I've always loved music.","uz":"Universitet radiosida DJ bo'lib ishlay boshladim. Qizig'i, men musiqa yoki san'atni o'qimaganman — aslida tarix talabasi edim, lekin musiqani doim sevganman."},{"s":37.11,"e":39.33,"t":"I do the breakfast show Monday to Friday."},{"s":39.9,"e":54.17,"t":"I start at 6am and I'm not much of a breakfast person so I don't eat before the show. Everyone eats and drinks loads of strong coffee but I'm a tea man myself. One big cup and then I'm ready to start.","uz":"Ishni ertalab soat 6 da boshlayman va nonushta qiladigan odam emasman, shuning uchun ko'rsatuvdan oldin ovqatlanmayman. Hamma kuchli qahva ichadi, men esa choyni yaxshi ko'raman — bitta katta piyola, keyin boshlashga tayyorman."},{"s":55.03,"e":59.58,"t":"Once I finish the show at 10, I have my breakfast then and a glass of juice."},{"s":60.38,"e":67.26,"t":"I love my job because I get to play great music. The best thing of all is when I get to do interviews.","uz":"Ishimni yaxshi ko'raman, chunki zo'r musiqa qo'yaman. Lekin eng yaxshisi — intervyu olish."},{"s":67.96,"e":75.87,"t":"I've met some amazing people, some of them famous, and some of them just ordinary people who have done wonderful things."},{"s":76.95,"e":82.59,"t":"Unfortunately, I have made myself look silly a few times. My memory isn't that good."},{"s":83.13,"e":90.94,"t":"It's not that I forget dates or times or anything like that, but once in the middle of talking to a politician, I forgot their name.","uz":"Sanalar yoki vaqtlarni unutaman emas, lekin bir safar siyosatchi bilan gaplashayotib, uning ismini unutib qo'ydim."},{"s":91.45,"e":92.7,"t":"That was not good."},{"s":93.94,"e":99.49,"t":"I had never thought that I would have a successful career as a radio presenter when I was at university."},{"s":100.22,"e":109.37,"t":"I was always interested in teaching or acting, but if I changed careers now, I would definitely be a reporter of some kind as I love talking to people.","uz":"Doim o'qituvchilik yoki aktyorlikka qiziqqanman, lekin hozir kasbimni o'zgartirsam, albatta qandaydir muxbir bo'lardim, chunki odamlar bilan gaplashishni yaxshi ko'raman."},{"s":110.46,"e":112.7,"t":"Well, that's a little bit about me."},{"s":113.37,"e":129.66,"t":"If any of you are free this weekend and aren't too busy studying or going to clubs, why not come and see me at a charity event I'm doing at Hatfield House? If you want to make a note of that, it's spelt H A T F I E L D House.","uz":"Bu hafta oxiri bo'sh bo'lsangiz, Hatfield House'da o'tkazadigan xayriya tadbirimga keling. Yozib olmoqchi bo'lsangiz: H-A-T-F-I-E-L-D house."},{"s":130.26,"e":131.74,"t":"I hope to see some of you there"}]},{"n":26,"title":"School Geography Trip","dur":367.2,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Date of Geography trip","t":"Wednesday 15th {1}"},{"k":"row","l":"Each group will be given","t":"a {2}"},{"k":"row","l":"Length of walk","t":"4 {3}"},{"k":"row","l":"Person responsible for health issues","t":"Mr {4}"},{"k":"row","l":"Type of shoes to wear","t":"{5}"},{"k":"row","l":"Coach arrives at school at","t":"{6} p.m."}],"items":[{"a":["June"],"ps":26.2,"en":46.01,"si":4,"ev":"First of all, it is no longer on Monday 13th June. It is on Wednesday 14th. Sorry, I mean, Wednesday 15th June. So please make sure you have the new date in your diary.","hl":"June","uz":"Avvalo, sayohat endi 13-iyun, dushanba kuni emas. U 14-chorshanba… kechirasiz, 15-iyun, chorshanba kuni. Yangi sanani kundaligingizga yozib qo'ying.","why":"Gapiruvchi o'zini tuzatadi: 14th emas, 15th June. Oy — June."},{"a":["map"],"ps":70.2,"en":78.21,"si":11,"ev":"There will be no technology for you to use. You will have to use the map that each group will be given.","hl":"map","uz":"Foydalanish uchun hech qanday texnologiya bo'lmaydi. Har bir guruhga beriladigan xaritadan foydalanishingiz kerak.","why":"\"No technology… use the map\" — xarita."},{"a":["kilometres","kilometers"],"ps":83.9,"en":96.61,"si":14,"ev":"The coach will drive you to the bottom of the hill, which is about 12 km from our school, and then you will have to walk the 4 km to the top.","hl":null,"uz":"Avtobus sizni maktabimizdan taxminan 12 km uzoqlikdagi tepalik etagiga olib boradi, keyin cho'qqigacha 4 km piyoda yurasiz.","why":"12 km — avtobus yo'li, 8 km — borib-kelish (tuzoqlar). Piyoda — 4 km."},{"a":["Walsh"],"ps":119.67,"en":138.27,"si":21,"ev":"It will be easy to see him as he will be walking with Mrs Jackson and he will be wearing a bright orange coat. His name is Mr Walsh. W-A-L-S-H.","hl":"Walsh","uz":"Uni ko'rish oson bo'ladi: u Missis Jekson bilan birga yuradi va yorqin to'q sariq kurtka kiyib oladi. Uning ismi — janob Uolsh. W-A-L-S-H.","why":"Shifokor — Mr Walsh. Mrs Jackson — boshqa kishi (tuzoq)."},{"a":["boots"],"ps":148.86,"en":165.02,"si":25,"ev":"It's a good idea to wear a sun hat, but most important of all, you need to make sure that you are wearing comfortable boots, as you won't be walking on easy paths. No sandals or beach shoes.","hl":"boots","uz":"Quyosh shlyapasi kiyish yaxshi, lekin eng muhimi — qulay botinka kiying, chunki yo'llar oson bo'lmaydi. Sandal yoki plyaj poyabzali mumkin emas.","why":"Poyabzal turi — boots. Sun hat — kiyim, poyabzal emas; sandals — taqiqlangan."},{"a":["7","seven"],"ps":173.78,"en":184.77,"si":28,"ev":"The coach will collect us at about 6pm. So if there's no heavy traffic, we should be back at school at 7pm. Now!","hl":"7","uz":"Avtobus bizni soat 18 larda olib ketadi, shuning uchun tirbandlik bo'lmasa, maktabga soat 19 da qaytamiz.","why":"6pm — avtobus olib ketish vaqti (tuzoq). Maktabga yetib kelish — 7 pm."}],"segs":[{"s":7.99,"e":12.19,"t":"You will hear a teacher telling a group of students about a geography trip."},{"s":16.98,"e":17.82,"t":"OK everyone."},{"s":18.49,"e":19.74,"t":"Listen carefully."},{"s":20.38,"e":24.89,"t":"as I need to give you some information about the geography trip."},{"s":26.2,"e":46.01,"t":"First of all, it is no longer on Monday 13th June. It is on Wednesday 14th. Sorry, I mean, Wednesday 15th June. So please make sure you have the new date in your diary.","uz":"Avvalo, sayohat endi 13-iyun, dushanba kuni emas. U 14-chorshanba… kechirasiz, 15-iyun, chorshanba kuni. Yangi sanani kundaligingizga yozib qo'ying."},{"s":47.48,"e":48.29,"t":"As you know."},{"s":48.79,"e":51.71,"t":"We will be walking up quite a high mountain."},{"s":52.57,"e":57.73,"t":"Well actually, it's not really a mountain, it's a very high hill."},{"s":58.94,"e":61.05,"t":"You will be put into groups."},{"s":61.88,"e":63.39,"t":"You need to work together."},{"s":64.09,"e":69.02,"t":"team to find your way to the meeting point at the end of the walk."},{"s":70.2,"e":78.21,"t":"There will be no technology for you to use. You will have to use the map that each group will be given.","uz":"Foydalanish uchun hech qanday texnologiya bo'lmaydi. Har bir guruhga beriladigan xaritadan foydalanishingiz kerak."},{"s":79.13,"e":80.45,"t":"As I mentioned before,"},{"s":81.08,"e":82.81,"t":"It's quite a difficult walk."},{"s":83.9,"e":96.61,"t":"The coach will drive you to the bottom of the hill, which is about 12 km from our school, and then you will have to walk the 4 km to the top.","uz":"Avtobus sizni maktabimizdan taxminan 12 km uzoqlikdagi tepalik etagiga olib boradi, keyin cho'qqigacha 4 km piyoda yurasiz."},{"s":97.85,"e":98.59,"t":"Don't worry."},{"s":99.1,"e":102.14,"t":"There is actually a car park near the top."},{"s":102.71,"e":106.3,"t":"So you won't have to walk all the way back down again."},{"s":107.51,"e":111.23,"t":"We wouldn't make you walk 8 kilometers in one day."},{"s":112.6,"e":115.93,"t":"There will be a doctor with you at all times."},{"s":116.41,"e":118.78,"t":"to help anyone who might feel unwell."},{"s":119.67,"e":138.27,"t":"It will be easy to see him as he will be walking with Mrs Jackson and he will be wearing a bright orange coat. His name is Mr Walsh. W-A-L-S-H.","uz":"Uni ko'rish oson bo'ladi: u Missis Jekson bilan birga yuradi va yorqin to'q sariq kurtka kiyib oladi. Uning ismi — janob Uolsh. W-A-L-S-H."},{"s":139.45,"e":142.81,"t":"Don't forget to drink lots of water during the walk."},{"s":143.99,"e":144.41,"t":"Now."},{"s":145.08,"e":148.03,"t":"on the subject of keeping safe and well."},{"s":148.86,"e":165.02,"t":"It's a good idea to wear a sun hat, but most important of all, you need to make sure that you are wearing comfortable boots, as you won't be walking on easy paths. No sandals or beach shoes.","uz":"Quyosh shlyapasi kiyish yaxshi, lekin eng muhimi — qulay botinka kiying, chunki yo'llar oson bo'lmaydi. Sandal yoki plyaj poyabzali mumkin emas."},{"s":165.72,"e":168.96,"t":"We will have a packed lunch halfway through the walk."},{"s":169.66,"e":172.57,"t":"and drinks and cake at the end in the cafe."},{"s":173.78,"e":184.77,"t":"The coach will collect us at about 6pm. So if there's no heavy traffic, we should be back at school at 7pm. Now!","uz":"Avtobus bizni soat 18 larda olib ketadi, shuning uchun tirbandlik bo'lmasa, maktabga soat 19 da qaytamiz."},{"s":185.43,"e":186.72,"t":"Are there any questions?"}]},{"n":27,"title":"Chiswick House and Gardens Review","dur":265.0,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Chiswick Park is in","t":"{1}"},{"k":"row","l":"Chiswick House contains","t":"paintings and {2}"},{"k":"row","l":"Individual ticket for House tour costs","t":"£{3}"},{"k":"row","l":"Things to buy in flower shop","t":"{4} and souvenirs"},{"k":"row","l":"Group ticket cost for garden tour","t":"£{5}"},{"k":"row","l":"Starting date of Music Week","t":"{6}"}],"items":[{"a":["(west) London"],"ps":18.94,"en":40.8,"si":1,"ev":"London has many surprises waiting to be discovered. So imagine my surprise when I discovered the amazing Chiswick Park in West London. Hidden amongst the houses, right next to the main station. In fact, just where you would not expect to find a beautiful park, with a restaurant and an example of amazing architecture.","hl":"London","uz":"London ko'plab kutilmagan narsalarga to'la, shuning uchun G'arbiy Londonda ajoyib Chiswick bog'ini topganimda hayratlanganimni tasavvur qiling.","why":"\"In West London\" — joylashuvi: (West) London."},{"a":["furniture"],"ps":48.57,"en":55.1,"si":4,"ev":"The interior of the building is important, not only because of its beauty, but because there are important paintings and furniture in it.","hl":"furniture","uz":"Bino ichki qismi nafaqat go'zalligi, balki undagi muhim rasmlar va mebellar tufayli ham ahamiyatli.","why":"\"Paintings and furniture\" — rasmlar va mebel."},{"a":["18","eighteen"],"ps":56.22,"en":69.73,"si":5,"ev":"You can join group tours of Chiswick House, which take place every weekend. They last an hour and cost £18 per person. There are also family tickets that cost £38.","hl":"18","uz":"Chiswick House bo'ylab har dam olish kunlari guruhli ekskursiyalar bor. Ular bir soat davom etadi va kishi boshiga 18 funt turadi. 38 funtlik oilaviy chiptalar ham bor.","why":"£38 — oilaviy chipta (tuzoq). Bir kishilik — £18."},{"a":["plants"],"ps":95.8,"en":99.26,"si":10,"ev":"There is also a flower shop where you can buy plants and souvenirs.","hl":"plants","uz":"Shuningdek, gul do'koni ham bor — u yerdan o'simliklar va esdalik sovg'alari sotib olish mumkin.","why":"\"Plants and souvenirs\" — o'simliklar."},{"a":["50.00","50","fifty"],"ps":100.73,"en":111.65,"si":11,"ev":"The garden tour is £6 per person or £50 for a group of 10. It takes an hour and a half after which you will be ready for a meal or a coffee at the restaurant.","hl":"50","uz":"Bog' bo'ylab ekskursiya kishi boshiga 6 funt yoki 10 kishilik guruh uchun 50 funt. U bir yarim soat davom etadi.","why":"£6 — bir kishilik (tuzoq). Guruh chiptasi — £50."},{"a":["7th June","June 7th","7 June"],"ps":119.58,"en":124.03,"si":13,"ev":"Oh, and if you're in London from the 7th of June, there is a music week.","hl":"7th of June","uz":"Aytgancha, agar 7-iyundan boshlab Londonda bo'lsangiz, musiqa haftaligi bor.","why":"Musiqa haftaligi 7-iyundan boshlanadi. \"6 to 10\" — kunlik vaqt (tuzoq)."}],"segs":[{"s":7.16,"e":12.8,"t":"You will hear a student giving a review of his visit to Chiswick House and Gardens to his class."},{"s":18.94,"e":40.8,"t":"London has many surprises waiting to be discovered. So imagine my surprise when I discovered the amazing Chiswick Park in West London. Hidden amongst the houses, right next to the main station. In fact, just where you would not expect to find a beautiful park, with a restaurant and an example of amazing architecture.","uz":"London ko'plab kutilmagan narsalarga to'la, shuning uchun G'arbiy Londonda ajoyib Chiswick bog'ini topganimda hayratlanganimni tasavvur qiling."},{"s":41.34,"e":44.0,"t":"Chiswick House was built in 1729."},{"s":44.86,"e":47.49,"t":"It was designed by its owner, Lord Burlington."},{"s":48.57,"e":55.1,"t":"The interior of the building is important, not only because of its beauty, but because there are important paintings and furniture in it.","uz":"Bino ichki qismi nafaqat go'zalligi, balki undagi muhim rasmlar va mebellar tufayli ham ahamiyatli."},{"s":56.22,"e":69.73,"t":"You can join group tours of Chiswick House, which take place every weekend. They last an hour and cost £18 per person. There are also family tickets that cost £38.","uz":"Chiswick House bo'ylab har dam olish kunlari guruhli ekskursiyalar bor. Ular bir soat davom etadi va kishi boshiga 18 funt turadi. 38 funtlik oilaviy chiptalar ham bor."},{"s":70.33,"e":75.26,"t":"I went on one of these tours and I can tell you it was well worth every penny."},{"s":76.54,"e":84.25,"t":"Now, if being outside is more your thing, Chiswick Park, the huge garden which the house was built in will inspire you."},{"s":84.86,"e":87.04,"t":"You can go on a garden tour with a guide."},{"s":88.09,"e":94.33,"t":"You will see the greenhouses filled with flowers and beautiful gardens full of whatever flowers are in season."},{"s":95.8,"e":99.26,"t":"There is also a flower shop where you can buy plants and souvenirs.","uz":"Shuningdek, gul do'koni ham bor — u yerdan o'simliklar va esdalik sovg'alari sotib olish mumkin."},{"s":100.73,"e":111.65,"t":"The garden tour is £6 per person or £50 for a group of 10. It takes an hour and a half after which you will be ready for a meal or a coffee at the restaurant.","uz":"Bog' bo'ylab ekskursiya kishi boshiga 6 funt yoki 10 kishilik guruh uchun 50 funt. U bir yarim soat davom etadi."},{"s":112.44,"e":118.85,"t":"There is a wide selection of cakes and snacks from as little as £2 for coffee and a piece of cake."},{"s":119.58,"e":124.03,"t":"Oh, and if you're in London from the 7th of June, there is a music week.","uz":"Aytgancha, agar 7-iyundan boshlab Londonda bo'lsangiz, musiqa haftaligi bor."},{"s":124.5,"e":130.17,"t":"You can sit on the grass and listen to music from 6 in the afternoon to 10 every evening."},{"s":130.71,"e":136.25,"t":"The Music Week ends on the 13th of June with an amazing Teenagers song competition."}]},{"n":28,"title":"Amazing Holidays","dur":289.0,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"Benefits of The Great Wall of China tour:"},{"k":"li","t":"not overcrowded"},{"k":"li","t":"excellent {1}"},{"k":"h","t":"Mount Everest:"},{"k":"li","t":"last trip is on {2}"},{"k":"h","t":"Cookery holidays:"},{"k":"li","t":"China or Vietnam tour: go to food {3} for shopping"},{"k":"li","t":"Panda Rescue Centre: class on making panda rice {4}"},{"k":"li","t":"Mexico Food Adventure: visit the {5} museum."},{"k":"h","t":"For more information:"},{"k":"li","t":"www.{6}.holiday.com"}],"items":[{"a":["views"],"ps":40.28,"en":48.45,"si":5,"ev":"Okay, you won't walk all of that, but it will take you far away from the crowds and the amazing views really make it worth it.","hl":"views","uz":"Albatta, hammasini piyoda bosib o'tmaysiz, lekin u sizni olomondan uzoqlashtiradi va ajoyib manzaralar bunga arziydi.","why":"\"Far away from the crowds\" — gavjum emas (kitobda bor). \"Excellent views\" — ajoyib manzaralar."},{"a":["15th April","April 15th","15 April"],"ps":65.24,"en":78.65,"si":9,"ev":"However, this does not happen in the summer months due to the rainy season, so the last one leaves on the 15th of April. Until last year, there was another one on the 25th of April, but there isn't any more.","hl":"15th of April","uz":"Lekin yomg'irli mavsum tufayli yoz oylarida bu sayohat bo'lmaydi, shuning uchun oxirgisi 15-aprelda jo'naydi. O'tgan yilgacha 25-aprelda yana bittasi bor edi, endi yo'q.","why":"25-aprel — endi yo'q (tuzoq). Oxirgi sayohat — 15-aprel."},{"a":["markets"],"ps":87.61,"en":96.0,"si":11,"ev":"Both holidays have cookery classes and you will get a chance to shop for ingredients at the food markets which are an amazing experience.","hl":"markets","uz":"Ikkala sayohatda ham pazandachilik darslari bor va oziq-ovqat bozorlarida masalliq xarid qilish imkoniyati bo'ladi — bu ajoyib tajriba.","why":"\"Shop for ingredients at the food markets\" — bozorlar."},{"a":["balls"],"ps":106.17,"en":112.32,"si":13,"ev":"You can have a cookery class there and learn to make panda rice balls. Great for kids parties.","hl":"balls","uz":"U yerda pazandachilik darsiga qatnashib, \"panda guruch sharchalari\"ni tayyorlashni o'rganasiz. Bolalar bayramlari uchun zo'r.","why":"\"Panda rice balls\" — guruch sharchalari: balls."},{"a":["chocolate"],"ps":113.3,"en":126.53,"si":14,"ev":"By the way, if you are chocolate mad, then the Mexico Food Adventure is the one for you. You get to go to the chocolate museum and see how it is produced, plus lots of chocolate cookery classes.","hl":"chocolate","uz":"Aytgancha, shokoladga ishqibozmisiz? Unda Meksika oziq-ovqat sarguzashti aynan siz uchun: shokolad muzeyiga borib, u qanday tayyorlanishini ko'rasiz, yana ko'plab shokolad pishirish darslari bor.","why":"\"Go to the chocolate museum\" — shokolad muzeyi."},{"a":["exodus"],"ps":135.42,"en":146.37,"si":16,"ev":"It's www.exodus.holiday.com. I'll spell that for you. It's E-X-O-D-U-S.","hl":"exodus","uz":"Manzil: www.exodus.holiday.com. Harflab aytaman: E-X-O-D-U-S.","why":"Kompaniya nomi — Exodus, harflab aytiladi."}],"segs":[{"s":6.55,"e":12.89,"t":"You will hear a teacher giving some information to students about a special destination for their school trip."},{"s":14.33,"e":19.58,"t":"Well, today I want to share with you some amazing ideas for our school trip next month."},{"s":20.6,"e":27.39,"t":"been looking into a new holiday company called Exodus which promises the traveller an unforgettable experience."},{"s":27.86,"e":32.67,"t":"So let's start with their walking holiday on the Great Wall of China."},{"s":33.75,"e":39.45,"t":"It took over 2,000 years to build and is 5,500 miles long."},{"s":40.28,"e":48.45,"t":"Okay, you won't walk all of that, but it will take you far away from the crowds and the amazing views really make it worth it.","uz":"Albatta, hammasini piyoda bosib o'tmaysiz, lekin u sizni olomondan uzoqlashtiradi va ajoyib manzaralar bunga arziydi."},{"s":49.5,"e":54.17,"t":"There is also another extreme walking and climbing experience on Everest."},{"s":54.9,"e":59.33,"t":"This is a 10 day extreme holiday only for experienced walkers."},{"s":60.02,"e":64.61,"t":"You join a group and climb to the base camp of the highest mountain on earth."},{"s":65.24,"e":78.65,"t":"However, this does not happen in the summer months due to the rainy season, so the last one leaves on the 15th of April. Until last year, there was another one on the 25th of April, but there isn't any more.","uz":"Lekin yomg'irli mavsum tufayli yoz oylarida bu sayohat bo'lmaydi, shuning uchun oxirgisi 15-aprelda jo'naydi. O'tgan yilgacha 25-aprelda yana bittasi bor edi, endi yo'q."},{"s":79.54,"e":86.88,"t":"But if walking is not your thing, how about a food holiday on a Vietnam or China food adventure tour?"},{"s":87.61,"e":96.0,"t":"Both holidays have cookery classes and you will get a chance to shop for ingredients at the food markets which are an amazing experience.","uz":"Ikkala sayohatda ham pazandachilik darslari bor va oziq-ovqat bozorlarida masalliq xarid qilish imkoniyati bo'ladi — bu ajoyib tajriba."},{"s":96.79,"e":105.37,"t":"For me, the best part is going to the Panda Rescue Center. You know, those lovely black and white bears that you only find in China?"},{"s":106.17,"e":112.32,"t":"You can have a cookery class there and learn to make panda rice balls. Great for kids parties.","uz":"U yerda pazandachilik darsiga qatnashib, \"panda guruch sharchalari\"ni tayyorlashni o'rganasiz. Bolalar bayramlari uchun zo'r."},{"s":113.3,"e":126.53,"t":"By the way, if you are chocolate mad, then the Mexico Food Adventure is the one for you. You get to go to the chocolate museum and see how it is produced, plus lots of chocolate cookery classes.","uz":"Aytgancha, shokoladga ishqibozmisiz? Unda Meksika oziq-ovqat sarguzashti aynan siz uchun: shokolad muzeyiga borib, u qanday tayyorlanishini ko'rasiz, yana ko'plab shokolad pishirish darslari bor."},{"s":127.45,"e":134.88,"t":"If you want, I'll give you the website address to have a look at all the amazing experience they offer both you and your parents."},{"s":135.42,"e":146.37,"t":"It's www.exodus.holiday.com. I'll spell that for you. It's E-X-O-D-U-S.","uz":"Manzil: www.exodus.holiday.com. Harflab aytaman: E-X-O-D-U-S."}]},{"n":29,"title":"Stonebridge House","dur":219.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The house was built in the {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The Reynold family lived in the house until {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The servants had rooms in the {3} room."},{"k":"p","t":"The art collection is in the {4} room."},{"k":"p","t":"George Reynold was a {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"George's brother died in a horse {6} accident."}],"items":[{"a":["19th century","nineteenth century"],"ps":23.26,"en":36.89,"si":3,"ev":"This morning I'm going to show you around this wonderful 19th century house which was the home of the Reynolds family for more than 150 years until 1975 when it became a national museum.","hl":"19th century","uz":"Bugun ertalab sizga 19-asrga oid ajoyib uyni ko'rsataman: bu uy 150 yildan ortiq Reynolds oilasiga qarashli bo'lgan, 1975-yilda esa milliy muzeyga aylangan.","why":"\"19th century house\" — 19-asr. 150 yil — oila yashagan muddat (tuzoq)."},{"a":["1975"],"ps":23.26,"en":36.89,"si":3,"ev":"This morning I'm going to show you around this wonderful 19th century house which was the home of the Reynolds family for more than 150 years until 1975 when it became a national museum.","hl":"1975","uz":"Bugun ertalab sizga 19-asrga oid ajoyib uyni ko'rsataman: bu uy 150 yildan ortiq Reynolds oilasiga qarashli bo'lgan, 1975-yilda esa milliy muzeyga aylangan.","why":"\"Until 1975\" — oila shu yilgacha yashagan."},{"a":["attic"],"ps":46.55,"en":52.09,"si":5,"ev":"The house servants used to sleep in the attic, but they would have used a different staircase to this one.","hl":"attic","uz":"Uy xizmatkorlari chordoqda uxlashgan, lekin ular boshqa zinadan foydalanishgan.","why":"\"Sleep in the attic\" — chordoq. Bedrooms — oila xonalari (tuzoq)."},{"a":["dining"],"ps":53.24,"en":59.45,"si":6,"ev":"Now, if we go through to the dining room, you will be able to see a fine collection of paintings.","hl":"dining","uz":"Endi ovqatlanish xonasiga o'tsak, ajoyib rasmlar to'plamini ko'rasiz.","why":"\"Dining room… a fine collection of paintings\" — san'at to'plami ovqatlanish xonasida."},{"a":["lawyer"],"ps":66.39,"en":76.03,"si":8,"ev":"George came from a military family. Surprisingly, however, he became a lawyer, even though his father had wanted him to be an officer in the army.","hl":"lawyer","uz":"Jorj harbiy oiladan chiqqan. Ajablanarlisi, otasi uni armiya ofitseri bo'lishini istasa-da, u advokat bo'ldi.","why":"Officer — otasining orzusi (tuzoq). Jorj — lawyer."},{"a":["riding"],"ps":93.78,"en":104.22,"si":12,"ev":"George's son Michael died from cancer. His wife died while giving birth to their daughter Emily and George's brother had a fatal horse riding accident.","hl":"riding","uz":"Jorjning o'g'li Maykl saratondan vafot etgan, rafiqasi qizi Emilini dunyoga keltirayotganda vafot etgan, Jorjning ukasi esa otda yurishda halokatli baxtsiz hodisaga uchragan.","why":"\"Horse riding accident\" — ot minish."}],"segs":[{"s":5.98,"e":10.78,"t":"You will hear a tour guide giving information about an old British house."},{"s":16.25,"e":19.61,"t":"Good morning everyone and welcome to Stonebridge House."},{"s":20.12,"e":22.46,"t":"My name is David and I'm your tool guide."},{"s":23.26,"e":36.89,"t":"This morning I'm going to show you around this wonderful 19th century house which was the home of the Reynolds family for more than 150 years until 1975 when it became a national museum.","uz":"Bugun ertalab sizga 19-asrga oid ajoyib uyni ko'rsataman: bu uy 150 yildan ortiq Reynolds oilasiga qarashli bo'lgan, 1975-yilda esa milliy muzeyga aylangan."},{"s":37.94,"e":45.89,"t":"We are now standing in the main lobby of the house where you can see the magnificent wooden staircase that leads up to the bedrooms."},{"s":46.55,"e":52.09,"t":"The house servants used to sleep in the attic, but they would have used a different staircase to this one.","uz":"Uy xizmatkorlari chordoqda uxlashgan, lekin ular boshqa zinadan foydalanishgan."},{"s":53.24,"e":59.45,"t":"Now, if we go through to the dining room, you will be able to see a fine collection of paintings.","uz":"Endi ovqatlanish xonasiga o'tsak, ajoyib rasmlar to'plamini ko'rasiz."},{"s":60.31,"e":65.37,"t":"George Reynolds was a big fan of traditional art as we can see here today."},{"s":66.39,"e":76.03,"t":"George came from a military family. Surprisingly, however, he became a lawyer, even though his father had wanted him to be an officer in the army.","uz":"Jorj harbiy oiladan chiqqan. Ajablanarlisi, otasi uni armiya ofitseri bo'lishini istasa-da, u advokat bo'ldi."},{"s":76.95,"e":80.35,"t":"His younger brother also rebelled and became a teacher."},{"s":81.46,"e":88.64,"t":"Now the Renauld family is famous for many things, but probably most of all for the many family tragedies."},{"s":89.34,"e":93.02,"t":"The family has had more than its fair share of early deaths."},{"s":93.78,"e":104.22,"t":"George's son Michael died from cancer. His wife died while giving birth to their daughter Emily and George's brother had a fatal horse riding accident.","uz":"Jorjning o'g'li Maykl saratondan vafot etgan, rafiqasi qizi Emilini dunyoga keltirayotganda vafot etgan, Jorjning ukasi esa otda yurishda halokatli baxtsiz hodisaga uchragan."},{"s":105.14,"e":112.16,"t":"George himself always suffered from a weak heart and he died of a heart attack at the age of 52."}]},{"n":30,"title":"Excursion to Brighton","dur":269.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The coach will be parked outside the Town {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"First, there is a tour of the famous Brighton Lanes, which once were narrow {2}, famous for their jewellers and boutiques."},{"k":"p","t":"Then there's a coffee break, when people can sit either inside the Palace {3} or in the Pavilion Gardens Cafe."},{"k":"p","t":"At around 12.45, a two-course lunch will be served at the Italian Restaurant for £{4}."},{"k":"p","t":"From 3 to 4, most of Brighton's sights will be explored, such as the artists' {5}, the Aquarium, the i360 tower and Brighton Pier."},{"k":"p","t":"Finally, cream {6} will be served at the Grand Hotel."}],"items":[{"a":["hall"],"ps":21.56,"en":30.08,"si":2,"ev":"It's going to be a very full day with many things to see and do. The coach will be outside the town hall at 8 o'clock.","hl":"hall","uz":"Kun juda serqatnov bo'ladi. Avtobus soat sakkizda shahar hokimiyati (town hall) oldida turadi.","why":"\"Outside the town hall\" — hall."},{"a":["streets"],"ps":56.82,"en":66.4,"si":6,"ev":"The lanes are the original part of Brighton. There used to be narrow streets lined with fishermen's cottages, but now they are more famous for boutiques and jewellers.","hl":"streets","uz":"Lanes — Braytonning eng qadimgi qismi. Ilgari bu yerda baliqchilar kulbalari bilan o'ralgan tor ko'chalar bo'lgan, hozir esa butiklar va zargarlik do'konlari bilan mashhur.","why":"\"Narrow streets\" — tor ko'chalar."},{"a":["café","cafe"],"ps":77.14,"en":82.72,"si":8,"ev":"You can either sit inside the Palace Cafe or sit outside at the Pavilion Gardens Cafe.","hl":"Cafe","uz":"Palace kafesi ichida yoki tashqarida Pavilion Gardens kafesida o'tirishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Palace Café\" — bo'shliq: café."},{"a":["8.95"],"ps":89.05,"en":95.71,"si":10,"ev":"There is a set menu on offer for us tomorrow. The two-course meal costs only £8.95.","hl":"8.95","uz":"Ertaga biz uchun belgilangan menyu bor. Ikki taomli ovqat atigi 8,95 funt.","why":"\"Two-course meal… £8.95\"."},{"a":["studios"],"ps":111.38,"en":124.38,"si":14,"ev":"Particularly worth visiting are the artists' studios on the beach, the aquarium, the I360 Tower where visitors can admire views across Brighton and the South Coast, and of course Brighton Pier.","hl":"studios","uz":"Ayniqsa, plyajdagi rassomlar ustaxonalari, akvarium, i360 minorasi va, albatta, Brighton Pier'ni ko'rishga arziydi.","why":"\"Artists' studios\" — rassomlar ustaxonalari."},{"a":["tea"],"ps":125.78,"en":134.91,"si":15,"ev":"Finally, to round off the day, we will be going for cream tea at the Grand Hotel.","hl":"tea","uz":"Va nihoyat, kunni yakunlash uchun Grand mehmonxonasida qaymoqli choy (cream tea) ichamiz.","why":"\"Cream tea\" — qaymoq va pishiriqli an'anaviy ingliz choyi."}],"segs":[{"s":5.62,"e":9.02,"t":"You will hear a tour guide talking to a group of people."},{"s":14.65,"e":21.05,"t":"Good afternoon, my name is Sally and I will be your tour guide on tomorrow's excursion to Brighton."},{"s":21.56,"e":30.08,"t":"It's going to be a very full day with many things to see and do. The coach will be outside the town hall at 8 o'clock.","uz":"Kun juda serqatnov bo'ladi. Avtobus soat sakkizda shahar hokimiyati (town hall) oldida turadi."},{"s":31.35,"e":38.97,"t":"Please make sure you are on time and ready to board the coach when it arrives, as it is a busy road and the driver can't stop for long."},{"s":39.58,"e":47.13,"t":"We will be in Brighton at 10 o'clock and you'll be dropped off at the Poole Valley coach station which is very close to the seafront."},{"s":48.28,"e":56.06,"t":"We'll start our guided walking tour at 10.15 and we'll have a leisurely wander around the famous Brighton lanes for half an hour."},{"s":56.82,"e":66.4,"t":"The lanes are the original part of Brighton. There used to be narrow streets lined with fishermen's cottages, but now they are more famous for boutiques and jewellers.","uz":"Lanes — Braytonning eng qadimgi qismi. Ilgari bu yerda baliqchilar kulbalari bilan o'ralgan tor ko'chalar bo'lgan, hozir esa butiklar va zargarlik do'konlari bilan mashhur."},{"s":67.26,"e":76.64,"t":"At 11 we'll go to the Royal Pavilion, which was once a Royal Palace. You'll probably all fancy a quick drink before the tour at 11.30."},{"s":77.14,"e":82.72,"t":"You can either sit inside the Palace Cafe or sit outside at the Pavilion Gardens Cafe.","uz":"Palace kafesi ichida yoki tashqarida Pavilion Gardens kafesida o'tirishingiz mumkin."},{"s":83.35,"e":88.45,"t":"Lunch will be at 12.45 till 2 o'clock at the local Italian restaurant."},{"s":89.05,"e":95.71,"t":"There is a set menu on offer for us tomorrow. The two-course meal costs only £8.95.","uz":"Ertaga biz uchun belgilangan menyu bor. Ikki taomli ovqat atigi 8,95 funt."},{"s":96.86,"e":101.53,"t":"The afternoon will be busy with a trip to the Brighton Museum and Art Gallery."},{"s":102.26,"e":105.57,"t":"This has recently been refurbished and it's worth a visit."},{"s":106.1,"e":110.69,"t":"From 3 to 5 in the afternoon, you are free to explore Brighton Seafront."},{"s":111.38,"e":124.38,"t":"Particularly worth visiting are the artists' studios on the beach, the aquarium, the I360 Tower where visitors can admire views across Brighton and the South Coast, and of course Brighton Pier.","uz":"Ayniqsa, plyajdagi rassomlar ustaxonalari, akvarium, i360 minorasi va, albatta, Brighton Pier'ni ko'rishga arziydi."},{"s":125.78,"e":134.91,"t":"Finally, to round off the day, we will be going for cream tea at the Grand Hotel. Then it's a five minute walk to the coach station for a 6pm departure."},{"s":135.48,"e":136.89,"t":"Are there any questions?"}]},{"n":31,"title":"London Taxis and Private Hire Vehicles","dur":295.4,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Methods of payment","t":"{1}, or with credit and debit cards"},{"k":"row","l":"Where to stop a cab","t":"in the {2}, or at cab ranks"},{"k":"row","l":"Tariff 2","t":"Monday – Friday: 8 pm – 10 pm; Saturday & {3}: 6 am – 10 pm"},{"k":"row","l":"Tariff 3","t":"every night: 10 pm – 6 am & on Public {4}"},{"k":"row","l":"Requirements","t":"taxi drivers to complete a {5} examination"},{"k":"row","l":"Notice","t":"Private hire vehicles must always be {6} either at an operator's office, or by phone"}],"items":[{"a":["cash"],"ps":32.86,"en":39.26,"si":3,"ev":"All taxis and private hire operators take cash and some accept credit and debit cards.","hl":"cash","uz":"Barcha taksi va xususiy ijara xizmatlari naqd pul qabul qiladi, ba'zilari kredit va debet kartalarini ham.","why":"\"All… take cash\" — naqd pul."},{"a":["street"],"ps":47.38,"en":61.41,"si":5,"ev":"These are the only vehicles that should be stopped on the street or picked up at cab ranks, although taxis can also be booked in advance through a telephone service. Taxi fares have been simplified.","hl":"street","uz":"Faqat shu mashinalarni ko'chada to'xtatish yoki taksi bekatlaridan olish mumkin, ammo ularni telefon orqali oldindan ham buyurtma qilsa bo'ladi.","why":"\"Stopped on the street\" — ko'chada."},{"a":["Sunday"],"ps":90.3,"en":100.41,"si":12,"ev":"The second tariff is from Monday to Friday between 8pm and 10pm as well as Saturday and Sunday 6am to 10pm.","hl":"Sunday","uz":"Ikkinchi tarif dushanbadan jumagacha soat 20:00 dan 22:00 gacha, shuningdek shanba va yakshanba 6:00 dan 22:00 gacha amal qiladi.","why":"\"Saturday and Sunday\" — yakshanba."},{"a":["holidays"],"ps":101.4,"en":108.41,"si":13,"ev":"The third comes into effect every night between 10pm and 6am and on public holidays.","hl":"holidays","uz":"Uchinchisi har kecha 22:00 dan 6:00 gacha va bayram kunlari amal qiladi.","why":"\"Public holidays\" — bayram kunlari."},{"a":["(full) medical"],"ps":117.82,"en":128.35,"si":15,"ev":"Complete background criminal record checks are carried out as well as a full medical examination and an exam style test of their knowledge of London streets.","hl":"medical","uz":"Sudlanganlik bo'yicha to'liq tekshiruv, to'liq tibbiy ko'rik va London ko'chalarini bilish bo'yicha imtihon o'tkaziladi.","why":"\"A full medical examination\" — tibbiy ko'rik."},{"a":["booked"],"ps":136.09,"en":150.59,"si":17,"ev":"Private hire vehicles include both limousines and chauffeur services, or 'mini-cabs' as they are often called, and have to be booked in advance either by visiting a licensed operator's office or by telephone.","hl":"booked","uz":"Xususiy ijara mashinalariga limuzinlar va haydovchi xizmatlari (\"mini-cab\"lar) kiradi; ular litsenziyali operator ofisiga borib yoki telefon orqali oldindan buyurtma qilinishi kerak.","why":"\"Have to be booked in advance\" — oldindan band qilinadi."}],"segs":[{"s":5.62,"e":11.1,"t":"You will hear someone talking on the radio about taxis and private hire vehicles in London."},{"s":16.89,"e":22.62,"t":"Travelling by taxi or private hire is one of the most flexible ways to travel around London."},{"s":23.51,"e":31.84,"t":"services operate across the capital 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, subject to local availability."},{"s":32.86,"e":39.26,"t":"All taxis and private hire operators take cash and some accept credit and debit cards.","uz":"Barcha taksi va xususiy ijara xizmatlari naqd pul qabul qiladi, ba'zilari kredit va debet kartalarini ham."},{"s":40.09,"e":46.33,"t":"Historically, taxis have been referred to as black cabs, even though many are not black."},{"s":47.38,"e":61.41,"t":"These are the only vehicles that should be stopped on the street or picked up at cab ranks, although taxis can also be booked in advance through a telephone service. Taxi fares have been simplified.","uz":"Faqat shu mashinalarni ko'chada to'xtatish yoki taksi bekatlaridan olish mumkin, ammo ularni telefon orqali oldindan ham buyurtma qilsa bo'ladi."},{"s":62.04,"e":68.61,"t":"Fairs depend on three things - the time of day, the distance travelled and time taken."},{"s":69.27,"e":72.0,"t":"There are three different tariffs for the time of day."},{"s":72.76,"e":76.45,"t":"One mile, which cost you about £4 on tariff 1."},{"s":77.05,"e":79.81,"t":"£4.60 on tariff 2"},{"s":80.25,"e":83.74,"t":"and about £5, £20 on tariff 3."},{"s":84.57,"e":89.5,"t":"The first applies from Monday to Friday, from 6am to 8pm."},{"s":90.3,"e":100.41,"t":"The second tariff is from Monday to Friday between 8pm and 10pm as well as Saturday and Sunday 6am to 10pm.","uz":"Ikkinchi tarif dushanbadan jumagacha soat 20:00 dan 22:00 gacha, shuningdek shanba va yakshanba 6:00 dan 22:00 gacha amal qiladi."},{"s":101.4,"e":108.41,"t":"The third comes into effect every night between 10pm and 6am and on public holidays.","uz":"Uchinchisi har kecha 22:00 dan 6:00 gacha va bayram kunlari amal qiladi."},{"s":109.27,"e":117.09,"t":"In London, there are over 24,000 licensed taxi drivers, all of whom have to pass certain tests."},{"s":117.82,"e":128.35,"t":"Complete background criminal record checks are carried out as well as a full medical examination and an exam style test of their knowledge of London streets.","uz":"Sudlanganlik bo'yicha to'liq tekshiruv, to'liq tibbiy ko'rik va London ko'chalarini bilish bo'yicha imtihon o'tkaziladi."},{"s":129.4,"e":135.23,"t":"They must know all of London's major roads and the quickest ways to certain destinations."},{"s":136.09,"e":150.59,"t":"Private hire vehicles include both limousines and chauffeur services, or 'mini-cabs' as they are often called, and have to be booked in advance either by visiting a licensed operator's office or by telephone.","uz":"Xususiy ijara mashinalariga limuzinlar va haydovchi xizmatlari (\"mini-cab\"lar) kiradi; ular litsenziyali operator ofisiga borib yoki telefon orqali oldindan buyurtma qilinishi kerak."}]},{"n":32,"title":"Historic Tours","dur":286.4,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"South Elmham House"},{"k":"p","t":"It was built around the 1300s, but it was greatly improved in the {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"It must have been the home of a wealthy {2}, as its wall paintings suggest."},{"k":"h","t":"Haughley Hall"},{"k":"p","t":"One of its best features is the secret hiding {3} in the walls."},{"k":"p","t":"Tours take place at 11.30 and 2 pm and are £15 with a {4}, or £12 with tea."},{"k":"h","t":"Bedfield House"},{"k":"p","t":"Gardens are joined by {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Tours start at 10.30 and 2.30 and one has to pay £{6}."}],"items":[{"a":["16th century","sixteenth century"],"ps":31.77,"en":42.17,"si":3,"ev":"Although it is known to date back to the 13th century when it was built by the bishops of Norwich, but was remodelled by several rich lords in the 16th century.","hl":"16th century","uz":"Uning XIII asrda Norvich episkoplari tomonidan qurilgani ma'lum, lekin XVI asrda bir necha boy lordlar uni qayta qurishgan.","why":"13th century — qurilgan vaqt (1300s, kitobda bor). Yaxshilangan — 16th century."},{"a":["family"],"ps":42.94,"en":50.91,"si":4,"ev":"It also contains some of the oldest wall paintings in the country, which suggests a very wealthy family once lived here.","hl":"family","uz":"Unda mamlakatdagi eng qadimiy devoriy rasmlardan ba'zilari ham bor, bu yerda bir paytlar juda boy oila yashaganini ko'rsatadi.","why":"\"A very wealthy family\" — boy oila."},{"a":["places"],"ps":89.27,"en":96.77,"si":13,"ev":"It includes secret hiding places in the walls and two tunnels which are now bricked up and a three acre garden.","hl":"places","uz":"Unda devorlardagi yashirin joylar, hozir g'isht bilan bekitilgan ikkita tunnel va uch akrlik bog' bor.","why":"\"Secret hiding places\" — yashirin joylar."},{"a":["(traditional) lunch"],"ps":97.46,"en":106.27,"si":14,"ev":"Tours start at both 11.30pm and 2pm and cost either £15 with a traditional lunch or £12 with tea.","hl":"lunch","uz":"Ekskursiyalar 11:30 va 14:00 da boshlanadi: an'anaviy tushlik bilan 15 funt yoki choy bilan 12 funt.","why":"£15 — tushlik bilan, £12 — choy bilan."},{"a":["(five) bridges"],"ps":130.81,"en":134.33,"si":19,"ev":"Five bridges connect the beautiful five-acre gardens.","hl":"bridges","uz":"Beshta ko'prik besh akrlik go'zal bog'larni bog'laydi.","why":"\"Five bridges connect the gardens\" — ko'priklar."},{"a":["13.50"],"ps":135.03,"en":143.93,"si":20,"ev":"Tours take place at 10.30 and 2.30 and cost £13.50 which includes tea, coffee and cakes.","hl":"13.50","uz":"Ekskursiyalar 10:30 va 14:30 da bo'lib, narxi 13,50 funt — choy, qahva va keklar bilan.","why":"Narx: £13.50."}],"segs":[{"s":6.26,"e":11.55,"t":"You will hear a woman talking about tours of historic houses in the south of England."},{"s":17.18,"e":25.53,"t":"Good afternoon. I'm going to tell you about the three tours we are currently organizing to historic houses in southern England."},{"s":26.2,"e":31.04,"t":"Mystery surrounds the exact origins of South Elmham House."},{"s":31.77,"e":42.17,"t":"Although it is known to date back to the 13th century when it was built by the bishops of Norwich, but was remodelled by several rich lords in the 16th century.","uz":"Uning XIII asrda Norvich episkoplari tomonidan qurilgani ma'lum, lekin XVI asrda bir necha boy lordlar uni qayta qurishgan."},{"s":42.94,"e":50.91,"t":"It also contains some of the oldest wall paintings in the country, which suggests a very wealthy family once lived here.","uz":"Unda mamlakatdagi eng qadimiy devoriy rasmlardan ba'zilari ham bor, bu yerda bir paytlar juda boy oila yashaganini ko'rsatadi."},{"s":51.86,"e":56.38,"t":"On the grounds there is also the ruins of a small Norman church."},{"s":57.11,"e":62.24,"t":"Tours include walking through the Deer Park to the church and start at 2pm."},{"s":63.0,"e":67.55,"t":"It cost £12 including tea, coffee and cakes."},{"s":68.22,"e":70.72,"t":"A midday meal can also be booked."},{"s":71.64,"e":75.2,"t":"Hawley Hall was built in the late 14th century."},{"s":75.64,"e":78.14,"t":"just outside a ruined Norman Castle."},{"s":79.0,"e":82.62,"t":"It was updated and added to in the 18th century."},{"s":83.42,"e":88.67,"t":"King Henry II once owned the house and its current owner is a lord."},{"s":89.27,"e":96.77,"t":"It includes secret hiding places in the walls and two tunnels which are now bricked up and a three acre garden.","uz":"Unda devorlardagi yashirin joylar, hozir g'isht bilan bekitilgan ikkita tunnel va uch akrlik bog' bor."},{"s":97.46,"e":106.27,"t":"Tours start at both 11.30pm and 2pm and cost either £15 with a traditional lunch or £12 with tea.","uz":"Ekskursiyalar 11:30 va 14:00 da boshlanadi: an'anaviy tushlik bilan 15 funt yoki choy bilan 12 funt."},{"s":106.94,"e":108.41,"t":"Groups are also welcome."},{"s":109.21,"e":118.91,"t":"The 12th century bedfield house is deep in the countryside and used to belong to the church until the mid 15th century when the modern house was built."},{"s":119.58,"e":122.3,"t":"It was surrounded by a river or moat."},{"s":122.81,"e":129.92,"t":"and inside the building the painted surfaces and plastered ceilings have anti-witchcraft symbols."},{"s":130.81,"e":134.33,"t":"Five bridges connect the beautiful five-acre gardens.","uz":"Beshta ko'prik besh akrlik go'zal bog'larni bog'laydi."},{"s":135.03,"e":143.93,"t":"Tours take place at 10.30 and 2.30 and cost £13.50 which includes tea, coffee and cakes.","uz":"Ekskursiyalar 10:30 va 14:30 da bo'lib, narxi 13,50 funt — choy, qahva va keklar bilan."},{"s":144.41,"e":145.6,"t":"Groups are welcome."}]},{"n":33,"title":"Fitness week","dur":189.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Anyone who would like to become healthier and learn new things should {1} for this course."},{"k":"p","t":"All new members must have with them trainers, a tracksuit, shorts and T-shirts as well as a(n) swimming {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"After answering some questions, specific targets will be set according to the members' {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Every morning a(n) personal {4} will keep an eye on new members exercising."},{"k":"p","t":"At the end of the week, members will be told fitness {5} so as not to gain back the weight they've lost."},{"k":"p","t":"For the next 48 hours, there's a sale on: you can pay £{6} for 7 days."}],"items":[{"a":["sign"],"ps":14.07,"en":21.31,"si":1,"ev":"Good morning everyone. Welcome to fitness week at our special health center. I can promise you three things if you sign up for this course.","hl":"sign","uz":"Hammaga xayrli tong. Maxsus sog'lomlashtirish markazimizdagi fitnes haftaligiga xush kelibsiz. Bu kursga yozilsangiz, sizga uchta narsani va'da qilaman.","why":"\"Sign up for this course\" — yozilish: sign (up)."},{"a":["costume"],"ps":40.44,"en":42.65,"si":4,"ev":"Don't forget also to take a swimming costume.","hl":"costume","uz":"Suzish kostyumini olishni ham unutmang.","why":"\"Swimming costume\" — suzish kostyumi."},{"a":["(individual) needs"],"ps":51.22,"en":56.45,"si":6,"ev":"Then we will work out a plan with specific targets for each person based on their individual needs.","hl":"needs","uz":"Keyin har bir kishi uchun individual ehtiyojlariga asoslangan aniq maqsadlar bilan reja tuzamiz.","why":"\"Based on their individual needs\" — ehtiyojlar."},{"a":["trainer"],"ps":57.02,"en":64.03,"si":7,"ev":"For the rest of the week, we will have morning exercise sessions in the gym, where a personal trainer will ensure you are exercising correctly.","hl":"trainer","uz":"Haftaning qolgan kunlarida sport zalida ertalabki mashg'ulotlar bo'ladi, shaxsiy murabbiy to'g'ri mashq qilayotganingizni kuzatib boradi.","why":"\"Personal trainer\" — shaxsiy murabbiy."},{"a":["strategies"],"ps":64.79,"en":82.85,"si":8,"ev":"Then there will be a talk about fitness strategies and how you can maintain your progress in everyday life.","hl":"strategies","uz":"Keyin fitnes strategiyalari va erishgan natijangizni kundalik hayotda qanday saqlab qolish haqida suhbat bo'ladi.","why":"\"Fitness strategies\" — strategiyalar."},{"a":["105"],"ps":83.35,"en":96.16,"si":9,"ev":"Book your place in the next two days and you will get a 25% discount. You will pay only £15 a day, which works out at £100. No, I'm sorry. That's £105 for the whole week.","hl":"105","uz":"Joyingizni keyingi 2 kun ichida band qilsangiz, 25% chegirma olasiz. Kuniga atigi 15 funt to'laysiz, bu 100 funt bo'ladi… Kechirasiz, butun hafta uchun 105 funt.","why":"Gapiruvchi o'zini tuzatadi: 100 emas, 105 funt."}],"segs":[{"s":5.53,"e":8.32,"t":"You will hear an announcement at a fitness centre."},{"s":14.07,"e":21.31,"t":"Good morning everyone. Welcome to fitness week at our special health center. I can promise you three things if you sign up for this course.","uz":"Hammaga xayrli tong. Maxsus sog'lomlashtirish markazimizdagi fitnes haftaligiga xush kelibsiz. Bu kursga yozilsangiz, sizga uchta narsani va'da qilaman."},{"s":21.82,"e":29.92,"t":"Firstly, you will become healthier. Number two, you will learn lots of new exercise techniques and number three, you will work very hard."},{"s":30.65,"e":39.74,"t":"Our gyms and swimming pools are all new and fully equipped, so all you need to take with you is a good pair of trainers, a tracksuit, shorts and t-shirts for the gym."},{"s":40.44,"e":42.65,"t":"Don't forget also to take a swimming costume.","uz":"Suzish kostyumini olishni ham unutmang."},{"s":43.7,"e":50.49,"t":"We start on a Sunday and the first day is an introduction. Each person will be weighed and fill in a quick health questionnaire."},{"s":51.22,"e":56.45,"t":"Then we will work out a plan with specific targets for each person based on their individual needs.","uz":"Keyin har bir kishi uchun individual ehtiyojlariga asoslangan aniq maqsadlar bilan reja tuzamiz."},{"s":57.02,"e":64.03,"t":"For the rest of the week, we will have morning exercise sessions in the gym, where a personal trainer will ensure you are exercising correctly.","uz":"Haftaning qolgan kunlarida sport zalida ertalabki mashg'ulotlar bo'ladi, shaxsiy murabbiy to'g'ri mashq qilayotganingizni kuzatib boradi."},{"s":64.79,"e":82.85,"t":"After a healthy snack, the afternoon will consist of exercises in the pool and then relaxation in the spa. On the last day, you will all be individually weighed and assessed to determine how much progress you have made. Then there will be a talk about fitness strategies and how you can maintain your progress in everyday life."},{"s":83.35,"e":96.16,"t":"Book your place in the next two days and you will get a 25% discount. You will pay only £15 a day, which works out at £100. No, I'm sorry. That's £105 for the whole week.","uz":"Joyingizni keyingi 2 kun ichida band qilsangiz, 25% chegirma olasiz. Kuniga atigi 15 funt to'laysiz, bu 100 funt bo'ladi… Kechirasiz, butun hafta uchun 105 funt."}]},{"n":34,"title":"The Oasis Hotel","dur":287.7,"lines":[{"k":"row","l":"Holiday Representative","t":"available in his {1} between 10 and 11 am, or between 6 and 7 pm."},{"k":"row","l":"Price","t":"everything included except {2}."},{"k":"row","l":"Participants","t":"anyone, but not children under the age of {3}."},{"k":"row","l":"Creche and toddler group","t":"Opening hours: 7.30 am to {4} am."},{"k":"row","l":"Yoga classes","t":"Cost: £{5} an hour."},{"k":"row","l":"Water {6} class","t":"in the pool on Sunday at 10 o'clock."}],"items":[{"a":["office"],"ps":32.54,"en":48.48,"si":4,"ev":"You can usually find me chatting to holiday makers somewhere in the hotel. Or you can leave a message from me in my office next to the bar and I'll get back to you. I'm always in the office between 10 and 11 in the morning or 6 and 7 in the evening.","hl":"office","uz":"Yoki bar yonidagi ofisimga xabar qoldirsangiz, sizga javob beraman. Men har doim ertalab 10 dan 11 gacha yoki kechqurun 6 dan 7 gacha ofisda bo'laman.","why":"\"In the office between 10 and 11… or 6 and 7\" — ofisda."},{"a":["lunch"],"ps":62.42,"en":80.35,"si":8,"ev":"The cost is £20 per person and this includes the coach trip to the harbour, the boat to the volcano and a welcome drink when you board the boat. You need to take a packed lunch and the hotel can provide one for you at a very reasonable rate if you ask them the night before.","hl":"lunch","uz":"Narxi kishi boshiga 20 funt: unga bandargacha avtobus, vulqongacha qayiq va qayiqqa chiqqanda kutib olish ichimligi kiradi. Tushlik o'zingiz bilan olishingiz kerak — mehmonxona oldingi kechqurun so'rasangiz, arzon narxda tayyorlab beradi.","why":"Narxga hammasi kiradi, faqat lunch (tushlik) kirmaydi."},{"a":["twelve","12"],"ps":90.55,"en":97.98,"si":10,"ev":"Children over the age of 12 are welcome. Unfortunately, the excursion is not suitable for younger children.","hl":"12","uz":"12 yoshdan katta bolalar qatnashishi mumkin. Afsuski, ekskursiya kichikroq bolalar uchun mos emas.","why":"\"Over the age of 12\" — 12 yoshdan kichiklar bormaydi."},{"a":["11.30"],"ps":98.78,"en":108.89,"si":11,"ev":"The hotel has a creche and toddler club which opens at 7.30am for 4 hours and then again in the early evening between 6 and 8.","hl":null,"uz":"Mehmonxonada bolalar bog'chasi va kichkintoylar klubi bor: u ertalab 7:30 da 4 soatga ochiladi, keyin kechqurun yana 6 dan 8 gacha.","why":"7.30 + 4 soat = 11.30. Hisoblash kerak bo'lgan savol! 6–8 — kechki vaqt (tuzoq)."},{"a":["4.50"],"ps":125.69,"en":132.09,"si":15,"ev":"The first costs £5 an hour and yoga is offered for £4.50 an hour.","hl":"4.50","uz":"Birinchisi (massaj) soatiga 5 funt, yoga esa soatiga 4,50 funt.","why":"£5 — massaj (tuzoq). Yoga — £4.50."},{"a":["aerobics"],"ps":133.37,"en":142.69,"si":16,"ev":"On Sunday morning, the fitness instructors offer water aerobics at 10am, followed by circuit training back in the gym at 11.15.","hl":"aerobics","uz":"Yakshanba ertalab fitnes murabbiylari soat 10 da suvda aerobika, keyin 11:15 da sport zalida aylanma mashg'ulot o'tkazadi.","why":"\"Water aerobics\" — suvdagi aerobika. Circuit training — zalda (tuzoq)."}],"segs":[{"s":5.5,"e":10.4,"t":"You will hear a holiday rep welcoming a new group of guests to a hotel."},{"s":16.09,"e":17.12,"t":"Good morning, everyone."},{"s":17.75,"e":26.97,"t":"After a good night's sleep, I hope you have all recovered from your long journey and are now ready to begin the holiday of a lifetime at the Oasis Hotel."},{"s":27.7,"e":31.84,"t":"My name is Steven and I am your Sunny Tours rep for the week."},{"s":32.54,"e":48.48,"t":"You can usually find me chatting to holiday makers somewhere in the hotel. Or you can leave a message from me in my office next to the bar and I'll get back to you. I'm always in the office between 10 and 11 in the morning or 6 and 7 in the evening.","uz":"Yoki bar yonidagi ofisimga xabar qoldirsangiz, sizga javob beraman. Men har doim ertalab 10 dan 11 gacha yoki kechqurun 6 dan 7 gacha ofisda bo'laman."},{"s":49.27,"e":54.05,"t":"Now I'd like to tell you about the midweek excursion to the volcano."},{"s":54.62,"e":57.53,"t":"This is always a very popular excursion."},{"s":57.98,"e":61.69,"t":"Also, I'd advise you to book soon to avoid disappointment."},{"s":62.42,"e":80.35,"t":"The cost is £20 per person and this includes the coach trip to the harbour, the boat to the volcano and a welcome drink when you board the boat. You need to take a packed lunch and the hotel can provide one for you at a very reasonable rate if you ask them the night before.","uz":"Narxi kishi boshiga 20 funt: unga bandargacha avtobus, vulqongacha qayiq va qayiqqa chiqqanda kutib olish ichimligi kiradi. Tushlik o'zingiz bilan olishingiz kerak — mehmonxona oldingi kechqurun so'rasangiz, arzon narxda tayyorlab beradi."},{"s":81.4,"e":89.76,"t":"The coach leaves at 9 o'clock sharp from outside the main entrance and will return at 5pm just in time for dinner."},{"s":90.55,"e":97.98,"t":"Children over the age of 12 are welcome. Unfortunately, the excursion is not suitable for younger children.","uz":"12 yoshdan katta bolalar qatnashishi mumkin. Afsuski, ekskursiya kichikroq bolalar uchun mos emas."},{"s":98.78,"e":108.89,"t":"The hotel has a creche and toddler club which opens at 7.30am for 4 hours and then again in the early evening between 6 and 8.","uz":"Mehmonxonada bolalar bog'chasi va kichkintoylar klubi bor: u ertalab 7:30 da 4 soatga ochiladi, keyin kechqurun yana 6 dan 8 gacha."},{"s":109.75,"e":115.17,"t":"You may already have seen that the hotel has a fantastic state-of-the-art gym."},{"s":115.86,"e":118.14,"t":"This is free to all hotel guests."},{"s":118.62,"e":124.57,"t":"A massage facility, hairstyling, aerobics classes and yoga classes are on offer."},{"s":125.69,"e":132.09,"t":"The first costs £5 an hour and yoga is offered for £4.50 an hour.","uz":"Birinchisi (massaj) soatiga 5 funt, yoga esa soatiga 4,50 funt."},{"s":133.37,"e":142.69,"t":"On Sunday morning, the fitness instructors offer water aerobics at 10am, followed by circuit training back in the gym at 11.15.","uz":"Yakshanba ertalab fitnes murabbiylari soat 10 da suvda aerobika, keyin 11:15 da sport zalida aylanma mashg'ulot o'tkazadi."},{"s":143.61,"e":146.59,"t":"Well, that's all for now. Are there any questions?"}]},{"n":35,"title":"Spanish Art Holidays","dur":223.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"From 8 to 9, breakfast will be served on the patio; it's a(n) {1} buffet-style breakfast."},{"k":"p","t":"At {2} the group will leave the hotel for its painting destination."},{"k":"p","t":"Once there, the teacher will show her students how to paint a {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Different {4} will be used, including charcoal and acrylic paint."},{"k":"p","t":"A picnic lunch will follow; everyone should get their own from {5} before leaving the hotel."},{"k":"p","t":"Then a(n) {6} meeting will follow to discuss the day's work."}],"items":[{"a":["self-service"],"ps":21.85,"en":36.67,"si":2,"ev":"I just want to run through the daily program with you so that we are all in the right place at the right time. Now breakfast will be served on the patio between 8 and 9 in the morning. It's a buffet breakfast and self-service so you can help yourself to as much as you like.","hl":"self-service","uz":"Nonushta ertalab 8 dan 9 gacha ayvonda beriladi. Bu shved stoli va o'z-o'ziga xizmat — xohlagancha olishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Self-service\" — o'z-o'ziga xizmat."},{"a":["9.30"],"ps":42.23,"en":48.06,"si":4,"ev":"At 9.30 prompt, we meet at the entrance to the hotel and walk to our painting location.","hl":"9.30","uz":"Soat 9:30 da aniq mehmonxona kirish eshigi oldida uchrashamiz va rasm chizadigan joyimizga piyoda boramiz.","why":"\"At 9.30 prompt\" — aniq 9:30 da."},{"a":["landscape"],"ps":48.89,"en":57.85,"si":5,"ev":"This will always be about half an hour away, certainly no further than expected. Once we arrive, I'll give you all a demonstration of landscape painting or drawing.","hl":"landscape","uz":"Yetib borgach, hammangizga manzara rasmini chizishni ko'rsataman.","why":"\"Landscape painting\" — manzara."},{"a":["materials"],"ps":58.42,"en":65.69,"si":6,"ev":"We'll be exploring a variety of materials such as pencil and charcoal and watercolour and acrylic paint.","hl":"materials","uz":"Turli materiallarni sinab ko'ramiz: qalam va ko'mir, akvarel va akril bo'yoq.","why":"\"A variety of materials\" — materiallar."},{"a":["reception"],"ps":84.82,"en":92.0,"si":11,"ev":"We will have a picnic lunch at 12.30. Don't forget to collect your packed lunch in the morning from reception.","hl":"reception","uz":"Soat 12:30 da piknik tushligi bo'ladi. Ertalab qabulxonadan tushlik paketingizni olishni unutmang.","why":"\"From reception\" — qabulxona."},{"a":["group"],"ps":93.11,"en":104.57,"si":12,"ev":"After an afternoon of painting and drawing, we'll all get together for a group tutorial, now. Don't be nervous about this, it's just a chance to share our thoughts and experiences and see what everyone has produced.","hl":"group","uz":"Tushdan keyingi rasm chizishdan so'ng hammamiz guruhli muhokamaga yig'ilamiz. Xavotir olmang — bu shunchaki fikr va tajriba almashish, kim nima chizganini ko'rish imkoniyati.","why":"\"Group tutorial\" — guruhli uchrashuv: group."}],"segs":[{"s":6.17,"e":9.57,"t":"You will hear a woman talking about an art holiday."},{"s":15.42,"e":20.96,"t":"Hello everyone, I hope you all settled in and are looking forward to your first day of landscaping painting tomorrow."},{"s":21.85,"e":36.67,"t":"I just want to run through the daily program with you so that we are all in the right place at the right time. Now breakfast will be served on the patio between 8 and 9 in the morning. It's a buffet breakfast and self-service so you can help yourself to as much as you like.","uz":"Nonushta ertalab 8 dan 9 gacha ayvonda beriladi. Bu shved stoli va o'z-o'ziga xizmat — xohlagancha olishingiz mumkin."},{"s":37.37,"e":41.6,"t":"I suggest you fill up as you'll get hungry in all that fresh air and walking."},{"s":42.23,"e":48.06,"t":"At 9.30 prompt, we meet at the entrance to the hotel and walk to our painting location.","uz":"Soat 9:30 da aniq mehmonxona kirish eshigi oldida uchrashamiz va rasm chizadigan joyimizga piyoda boramiz."},{"s":48.89,"e":57.85,"t":"This will always be about half an hour away, certainly no further than expected. Once we arrive, I'll give you all a demonstration of landscape painting or drawing.","uz":"Yetib borgach, hammangizga manzara rasmini chizishni ko'rsataman."},{"s":58.42,"e":65.69,"t":"We'll be exploring a variety of materials such as pencil and charcoal and watercolour and acrylic paint.","uz":"Turli materiallarni sinab ko'ramiz: qalam va ko'mir, akvarel va akril bo'yoq."},{"s":66.52,"e":71.42,"t":"We won't be using oil paint as it takes too long to dry and would be very difficult to handle."},{"s":72.15,"e":79.04,"t":"And then you get the chance to show what you're made of and I'll be walking around, giving advice and encouragement."},{"s":79.61,"e":82.33,"t":"Please feel free to ask me any question during this time."},{"s":82.87,"e":83.84,"t":"That's what I'm"},{"s":84.82,"e":92.0,"t":"We will have a picnic lunch at 12.30. Don't forget to collect your packed lunch in the morning from reception.","uz":"Soat 12:30 da piknik tushligi bo'ladi. Ertalab qabulxonadan tushlik paketingizni olishni unutmang."},{"s":93.11,"e":104.57,"t":"After an afternoon of painting and drawing, we'll all get together for a group tutorial, now. Don't be nervous about this, it's just a chance to share our thoughts and experiences and see what everyone has produced.","uz":"Tushdan keyingi rasm chizishdan so'ng hammamiz guruhli muhokamaga yig'ilamiz. Xavotir olmang — bu shunchaki fikr va tajriba almashish, kim nima chizganini ko'rish imkoniyati."},{"s":105.08,"e":113.5,"t":"We'll be back at the hotel at about 5 o'clock. So you have plenty of time to freshen up before dinner at 6.30. Now, any questions?"}]},{"n":36,"title":"Elephant Polo","dur":313.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Elephants are social animals and so they enjoy elephant polo tournaments."},{"k":"p","t":"The {1} of a goal in elephant polo is the same as in football."},{"k":"p","t":"A player and an elephant {2} both sit on each elephant."},{"k":"p","t":"It is against the rules for the elephants to use their trunks to {3} up the ball."},{"k":"p","t":"A total of {4} elephants are required for a game to take place."},{"k":"p","t":"The participants are in action for a total of ten minutes during each game."},{"k":"p","t":"The stick used in the game is both long and heavy."},{"k":"p","t":"The elephants sometimes want to lie down in front of a goal."},{"k":"p","t":"An elephant with a bad {5} will be taken out of a game."},{"k":"p","t":"African elephants are not used because their {6} cause a problem."}],"items":[{"a":["width"],"ps":116.09,"en":123.49,"si":10,"ev":"The pitch is about three quarters the length of a football pitch and the goals are the same width as football goals.","hl":"width","uz":"Maydon futbol maydoni uzunligining to'rtdan uch qismicha, darvozalar esa futbol darvozalari bilan bir xil kenglikda.","why":"Uzunlik farq qiladi (3/4), kenglik bir xil — width."},{"a":["handler"],"ps":131.35,"en":137.09,"si":13,"ev":"A Mahout, an elephant handler, sits behind each player and guides the elephant.","hl":"handler","uz":"Har bir o'yinchining orqasida mahout — fil boshqaruvchisi o'tirib, filni yo'naltiradi.","why":"\"An elephant handler\" — fil boshqaruvchisi."},{"a":["pick"],"ps":152.63,"en":161.25,"si":16,"ev":"Quite often they will kick the ball so that they can run after it. They're not allowed to pick up the ball with their trunks, though they sometimes try.","hl":"pick","uz":"Ko'pincha ular to'p ortidan yugurish uchun uni tepib yuborishadi. Fillarga to'pni xartumi bilan ko'tarish mumkin emas, garchi ba'zan urinib ko'rishsa ham.","why":"\"Not allowed to pick up the ball\" — ko'tarish taqiqlangan."},{"a":["nine","9"],"ps":164.82,"en":178.81,"si":18,"ev":"There are four elephants per team in a tournament plus the referees elephant. That's nine on the pitch at any one time. We usually have 16 animals available on any given day in four teams.","hl":"nine","uz":"Turnirda har jamoada to'rttadan fil, yana hakamning fili — ya'ni maydonda bir vaqtda to'qqizta. Odatda har kuni to'rt jamoa uchun 16 ta hayvon tayyor turadi.","why":"4+4+1 = 9. 16 — jami hayvonlar (tuzoq)."},{"a":["attitude"],"ps":249.18,"en":260.38,"si":31,"ev":"If the elephants didn't enjoy it, or if there was any form of misbehaving, they would be removed from the game. Sent off, if you like. It's not worth risking an elephant with an attitude problem.","hl":"attitude","uz":"Agar fillarga yoqmasa yoki o'zini yomon tutsa, o'yindan chiqariladi — xohlasangiz, \"chetlatish\" deng. Fe'l-atvori yomon filni xavf ostiga qo'yishga arzimaydi.","why":"\"An attitude problem\" — yomon fe'l-atvor: attitude."},{"a":["ears"],"ps":283.16,"en":291.68,"si":35,"ev":"The sport always uses Indian elephants. The problem with African ones is that their ears get in the way, and they're much taller.","hl":"ears","uz":"Bu sportda doim hind fillari ishlatiladi. Afrika fillarining muammosi — quloqlari xalaqit beradi va ular ancha baland.","why":"\"Their ears get in the way\" — quloqlar."}],"segs":[{"s":6.36,"e":9.66,"t":"You will hear someone talking about the sport of elephant polo."},{"s":10.55,"e":13.63,"t":"For questions 9 to 18, complete the sentences."},{"s":14.55,"e":17.21,"t":"You now have 45 seconds to look at part two."},{"s":65.05,"e":70.59,"t":"Of course, polo is normally played on horses and it's a very fast game."},{"s":71.77,"e":78.4,"t":"We don't claim that Elephant Polo is the fastest game in the world, but we always maintain it's the biggest."},{"s":79.0,"e":82.53,"t":"The elephants do actually enjoy polo, definitely."},{"s":83.16,"e":93.57,"t":"It's a lot of fun for them because they're social animals. And a polo tournament is a week when dozens of elephants meet up, many from the same family, like a reunion."},{"s":94.1,"e":99.68,"t":"And of course they get fed extremely well. Better than in their normal life."},{"s":100.25,"e":105.76,"t":"They use up a lot of energy and get through masses of sugar cane, especially at half time."},{"s":106.94,"e":115.52,"t":"The players sit on elephants and hit a white wooden ball using a long bamboo stick that has a polo mallet head on the end of it."},{"s":116.09,"e":123.49,"t":"The pitch is about three quarters the length of a football pitch and the goals are the same width as football goals.","uz":"Maydon futbol maydoni uzunligining to'rtdan uch qismicha, darvozalar esa futbol darvozalari bilan bir xil kenglikda."},{"s":123.99,"e":127.81,"t":"There's a basic saddle and the players are strapped onto the elephants."},{"s":128.25,"e":130.81,"t":"We've never had a serious accident."},{"s":131.35,"e":137.09,"t":"A Mahout, an elephant handler, sits behind each player and guides the elephant.","uz":"Har bir o'yinchining orqasida mahout — fil boshqaruvchisi o'tirib, filni yo'naltiradi."},{"s":137.53,"e":144.51,"t":"Sometimes the mahoots have their own games. Guiding the elephant and hitting the ball as well. That takes incredible skill."},{"s":145.5,"e":152.16,"t":"During a game, if the ball hits an elephant, that's fine. Their legs are quite thick and they do get in the way."},{"s":152.63,"e":161.25,"t":"Quite often they will kick the ball so that they can run after it. They're not allowed to pick up the ball with their trunks, though they sometimes try.","uz":"Ko'pincha ular to'p ortidan yugurish uchun uni tepib yuborishadi. Fillarga to'pni xartumi bilan ko'tarish mumkin emas, garchi ba'zan urinib ko'rishsa ham."},{"s":161.69,"e":164.09,"t":"That would be a free hit to the other side."},{"s":164.82,"e":178.81,"t":"There are four elephants per team in a tournament plus the referees elephant. That's nine on the pitch at any one time. We usually have 16 animals available on any given day in four teams.","uz":"Turnirda har jamoada to'rttadan fil, yana hakamning fili — ya'ni maydonda bir vaqtda to'qqizta. Odatda har kuni to'rt jamoa uchun 16 ta hayvon tayyor turadi."},{"s":179.61,"e":185.47,"t":"There are two halves, called chuckers, in a game of elephant polo, the same as in normal polo."},{"s":186.17,"e":188.7,"t":"We played 10 minutes of actual play."},{"s":189.66,"e":192.32,"t":"Whenever the whistle blows, the clock stops."},{"s":192.86,"e":199.26,"t":"A novice team might score one or two goals if they're lucky, while an advanced team might score about ten."},{"s":200.12,"e":207.23,"t":"The polo rules are that a man can only hold the stick with his right arm even if he is left handed."},{"s":207.77,"e":209.57,"t":"Women can use both hands."},{"s":210.23,"e":214.97,"t":"using the stick is hard work because it's long and the head is heavy."},{"s":215.7,"e":221.37,"t":"By the end of the game, your arm will be aching, but it's an easy game to pick up with a little practice."},{"s":222.36,"e":231.45,"t":"During the game, you chase after the ball on your elephant going quite quickly and you can easily miss it, though the elephant will often help you out with his foot."},{"s":232.18,"e":234.59,"t":"The elephants usually supply the entertainment."},{"s":235.06,"e":240.16,"t":"They might decide to lie down across the goal for fun, but that's an absolute no-no."},{"s":241.4,"e":248.51,"t":"Ultimately, it's about elephants charging up and down the pitch, scoring great goals themselves and having a lot of fun."},{"s":249.18,"e":260.38,"t":"If the elephants didn't enjoy it, or if there was any form of misbehaving, they would be removed from the game. Sent off, if you like. It's not worth risking an elephant with an attitude problem.","uz":"Agar fillarga yoqmasa yoki o'zini yomon tutsa, o'yindan chiqariladi — xohlasangiz, \"chetlatish\" deng. Fe'l-atvori yomon filni xavf ostiga qo'yishga arzimaydi."},{"s":261.24,"e":269.85,"t":"You get all sorts. You get big elephants that are a bit older and wiser. And we use a lot of small ones that can be exceptionally quick."},{"s":270.52,"e":277.31,"t":"We try to remove what you might call the elephant factor by swapping elephants and mahoots with the other team at half time."},{"s":278.07,"e":282.3,"t":"If you've got elephants that don't normally live together, there could be some tension."},{"s":283.16,"e":291.68,"t":"The sport always uses Indian elephants. The problem with African ones is that their ears get in the way, and they're much taller.","uz":"Bu sportda doim hind fillari ishlatiladi. Afrika fillarining muammosi — quloqlari xalaqit beradi va ular ancha baland."},{"s":302.2,"e":304.67,"t":"In the exam you will hear the recording twice."},{"s":305.56,"e":306.69,"t":"to listen again now."},{"s":307.22,"e":308.77,"t":"Go to the beginning of the track."}]},{"n":37,"title":"Indoor skydiving","dur":302.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The fans in the tunnel are normally used for putting air into underground systems."},{"k":"p","t":"It has been said that the machine looks like a huge {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The walls in the tunnel are made of {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The only parts of the body that can get hurt in the tunnel are the elbows and knees."},{"k":"p","t":"You have to be over 4 years old to use the tunnel."},{"k":"p","t":"You have to wear ear {3} when you use the tunnel."},{"k":"p","t":"Beginners have two 15-minute lessons in the tunnel with an instructor."},{"k":"p","t":"During lessons, you get into a position as if you have a {4} of air in your hands."},{"k":"p","t":"The person who created the wind tunnel refers to it as a smile {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Indoor skydiving has become a sport called body {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["hairdryer","hair dryer"],"ps":140.09,"en":143.42,"si":23,"ev":"The machine has been described as being like an enormous hair dryer.","hl":"hair dryer","uz":"Bu mashina ulkan soch quritgichga o'xshatilgan.","why":"\"An enormous hair dryer\" — ulkan soch quritgich."},{"a":["glass"],"ps":158.49,"en":162.14,"si":27,"ev":"The tunnel is 4 metres wide and has glass walls.","hl":"glass","uz":"Tunnel to'rt metr kenglikda, devorlari shishadan.","why":"\"Glass walls\" — shisha devorlar."},{"a":["plugs"],"ps":209.43,"en":228.57,"si":36,"ev":"Watching them do all that before I went into the tunnel left me feeling a little anxious, even though I knew the tunnel was safe. And the roar of the electric motors that power the fans, like a plane taking off and so loud you need earplugs, added to my fear. What happened when you went into the tunnel?","hl":"plugs","uz":"Ventilyatorlarni harakatlantiradigan elektr motorlarining samolyot ko'tarilayotgandek guvillashi — shunchalik balandki, quloq tiqinlari kerak bo'ladi — qo'rquvimni yanada oshirdi.","why":"\"So loud you need earplugs\" — ear plugs."},{"a":["ball"],"ps":234.9,"en":251.71,"si":38,"ev":"But since the average freefall from a plane lasts only one minute, you realise it is more than plenty. Held down by my instructor, I floated in the position I was told to keep to, with my hands out in front of me as if I was holding a ball of air for the whole session.","hl":"ball","uz":"Samolyotdan erkin tushish o'rtacha bir daqiqa davom etishini bilsangiz, bu yetarlidan ham ko'p. Instruktorim yordamida menga aytilgan holatda — qo'llarimni oldinga cho'zib, go'yo havo to'pini ushlab turgandek — suzib yurdim.","why":"\"As if I was holding a ball of air\" — havo to'pi."},{"a":["machine"],"ps":265.37,"en":274.11,"si":41,"ev":"In fact, the person who came up with the idea and set up the centre calls it a 'smile machine' because nobody can go into the tunnel without smiling.","hl":"machine","uz":"Aslida bu g'oyani o'ylab topib, markazni ochgan odam uni \"tabassum mashinasi\" deb ataydi, chunki tunnelga hech kim tabassumsiz kira olmaydi.","why":"\"A smile machine\" — tabassum mashinasi."},{"a":["flying"],"ps":288.15,"en":293.47,"si":47,"ev":"In fact, in some places it has developed into its own sport known as body flying.","hl":"flying","uz":"Aslida ba'zi joylarda u \"body flying\" degan alohida sport turiga aylangan.","why":"\"Body flying\" — bo'shliq: flying."}],"segs":[{"s":5.78,"e":9.28,"t":"You will hear a radio interview about indoor skydiving."},{"s":10.1,"e":13.31,"t":"For questions 9 to 18, complete the sentences."},{"s":14.46,"e":17.28,"t":"You now have 45 seconds to look at part two."},{"s":65.24,"e":75.26,"t":"Okay, now we come to our regular spot on extreme sports and this week our fearless reporter Tom Walker has been trying out something called indoor skydiving."},{"s":75.8,"e":76.73,"t":"And he's with me"},{"s":77.5,"e":77.85,"t":"[Music"},{"s":78.3,"e":81.92,"t":"What's this all about? Well, it's the same as skydiving."},{"s":82.42,"e":88.19,"t":"jumping from an aeroplane and free falling through the air without opening your parachute for some time."},{"s":88.76,"e":91.36,"t":"Except that you do it in an indoor wind tunnel."},{"s":92.02,"e":94.81,"t":"and there's no plane and no parachute."},{"s":95.38,"e":97.95,"t":"And so I was told, no danger."},{"s":98.65,"e":101.31,"t":"so it gives you a taste of doing an extreme sport."},{"s":101.85,"e":103.36,"t":"but it isn't quite so extreme."},{"s":104.09,"e":104.7,"t":"Right."},{"s":105.4,"e":106.91,"t":"Now, where did you do it?"},{"s":107.42,"e":112.29,"t":"I did it in a vertical winds tunnel and an adventure sports centre called Runway."},{"s":113.05,"e":118.24,"t":"What exactly is a vertical wind tunnel? Well, it's a tunnel that gets filled with air."},{"s":118.78,"e":122.59,"t":"The air is provided by four enormous industrial fans."},{"s":123.1,"e":126.75,"t":"of a kind that usually provide air for underground systems."},{"s":127.8,"e":130.08,"t":"These fans produce a column of air."},{"s":130.52,"e":132.64,"t":"that rushes through the tunnel from below."},{"s":133.08,"e":136.06,"t":"at more than 160 km/h."},{"s":136.79,"e":139.29,"t":"When you're in the tunnel, you float on this air."},{"s":140.09,"e":143.42,"t":"The machine has been described as being like an enormous hair dryer.","uz":"Bu mashina ulkan soch quritgichga o'xshatilgan."},{"s":144.06,"e":149.41,"t":"It allows you to fly as if you had fallen from a plane, but you are only two metres off the ground."},{"s":150.01,"e":152.54,"t":"And it's completely safe, is it? Yes."},{"s":153.3,"e":157.76,"t":"bars across the top of the tunnel to stop you flying off up and out of the tunnel."},{"s":158.49,"e":162.14,"t":"The tunnel is 4 metres wide and has glass walls.","uz":"Tunnel to'rt metr kenglikda, devorlari shishadan."},{"s":162.84,"e":167.71,"t":"The only small problem you might have is that you keep bashing into these walls."},{"s":168.31,"e":175.65,"t":"But you're not really going to hurt yourself a lot by doing this. The only injuries you are likely to get are sore elbows and knees."},{"s":176.15,"e":181.21,"t":"In fact, it's so safe that the centre is open to anyone over the age of four."},{"s":181.94,"e":186.59,"t":"In America, where the idea was invented by the military in 1994,"},{"s":187.1,"e":189.44,"t":"Tensioners in their 80s regularly have a go."},{"s":190.23,"e":191.13,"t":"Wow!"},{"s":191.7,"e":198.49,"t":"So how did you get on when you went there? Well, when I got there I watched the training instructors running through their routine."},{"s":199.13,"e":208.64,"t":"They were doing all sorts of moves in the tunnel, such as barrel rolls, something they call helicopters, spinning on their heads in mid-air and backflips."},{"s":209.43,"e":228.57,"t":"Watching them do all that before I went into the tunnel left me feeling a little anxious, even though I knew the tunnel was safe. And the roar of the electric motors that power the fans, like a plane taking off and so loud you need earplugs, added to my fear. What happened when you went into the tunnel?","uz":"Ventilyatorlarni harakatlantiradigan elektr motorlarining samolyot ko'tarilayotgandek guvillashi — shunchalik balandki, quloq tiqinlari kerak bo'ladi — qo'rquvimni yanada oshirdi."},{"s":229.34,"e":234.43,"t":"Like all beginners, I was given a couple of two-minute sessions in the tunnel, which seemed short."},{"s":234.9,"e":251.71,"t":"But since the average freefall from a plane lasts only one minute, you realise it is more than plenty. Held down by my instructor, I floated in the position I was told to keep to, with my hands out in front of me as if I was holding a ball of air for the whole session.","uz":"Samolyotdan erkin tushish o'rtacha bir daqiqa davom etishini bilsangiz, bu yetarlidan ham ko'p. Instruktorim yordamida menga aytilgan holatda — qo'llarimni oldinga cho'zib, go'yo havo to'pini ushlab turgandek — suzib yurdim."},{"s":252.34,"e":261.28,"t":"The only time he had to correct me was on the occasions I threatened to fly out of reach or, as if by instinct, disappear out of the entry/exit door."},{"s":261.78,"e":264.8,"t":"Sounds exciting! Yeah, it's great fun!"},{"s":265.37,"e":274.11,"t":"In fact, the person who came up with the idea and set up the centre calls it a 'smile machine' because nobody can go into the tunnel without smiling.","uz":"Aslida bu g'oyani o'ylab topib, markazni ochgan odam uni \"tabassum mashinasi\" deb ataydi, chunki tunnelga hech kim tabassumsiz kira olmaydi."},{"s":274.78,"e":276.29,"t":"So you recommend it?"},{"s":276.76,"e":279.61,"t":"Yes, it's just like real skydiving."},{"s":280.09,"e":281.73,"t":"except that you don't have the view."},{"s":282.3,"e":283.42,"t":"or the expense."},{"s":284.09,"e":287.65,"t":"and it's good both for beginners and extreme skydivers."},{"s":288.15,"e":293.47,"t":"In fact, in some places it has developed into its own sport known as body flying.","uz":"Aslida ba'zi joylarda u \"body flying\" degan alohida sport turiga aylangan."},{"s":293.94,"e":296.19,"t":"There are already competitions in that sport."},{"s":297.24,"e":298.01,"t":"Thanks Tom."},{"s":298.9,"e":300.7,"t":"If you want to find out more about the wind"}]},{"n":38,"title":"Paradise Wildlife Park","dur":353.5,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Project Life Lion is connected with diseases spread by domestic dogs."},{"k":"p","t":"The Park has created its own environmental {1} system, and other organisations use it."},{"k":"p","t":"A wide variety of {2} events (e.g. barbecues) are held at the Park."},{"k":"p","t":"For charity events, the Park will provide cheap tickets and competition prizes."},{"k":"p","t":"The Park's sister company gives people a chance to be a radio {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"People paying to adopt an animal get a certificate, a photograph, information about the animal and a free ticket for two people."},{"k":"p","t":"People who visit the Park more than five times in a year benefit from having a season ticket."},{"k":"p","t":"When the weather is cold, visitors can still enjoy using the indoor play {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"One of the Experience Days involves being an animal {5} for a day."},{"k":"p","t":"The Park is looking for people to do customer service and {6} work."}],"items":[{"a":["management"],"ps":128.18,"en":139.97,"si":11,"ev":"To do that, we have our own independently written Environmental Management System, which is now being used as a model by other organisations across the UK so that they can establish their own.","hl":"Management","uz":"Buning uchun bizda mustaqil yozilgan o'z Ekologik boshqaruv tizimimiz bor; hozir uni Buyuk Britaniyadagi boshqa tashkilotlar namuna sifatida ishlatmoqda.","why":"\"Environmental Management System\" — boshqaruv tizimi."},{"a":["corporate"],"ps":148.7,"en":163.77,"si":13,"ev":"The park is a venue for all manner of corporate events such as product launches, team building, special events, barbecues, the list is endless and we play host to many charity and fundraising events each year.","hl":"corporate","uz":"Park har xil korporativ tadbirlar o'tkaziladigan joy: mahsulot taqdimotlari, jamoa mashg'ulotlari, maxsus tadbirlar, barbekyular — ro'yxat cheksiz.","why":"\"Corporate events\" — korporativ tadbirlar."},{"a":["presenter"],"ps":178.68,"en":185.15,"si":16,"ev":"If you've always dreamed of being a radio presenter, we offer you the opportunity to take the first steps.","hl":"presenter","uz":"Agar doim radio boshlovchisi bo'lishni orzu qilgan bo'lsangiz, sizga ilk qadamlarni qo'yish imkoniyatini beramiz.","why":"\"A radio presenter\" — radio boshlovchisi."},{"a":["area"],"ps":279.54,"en":285.95,"si":30,"ev":"With our heated indoor play area there is still lots of fun to be had even when the weather is a bit chilly.","hl":"area","uz":"Isitiladigan yopiq o'yin maydonchamiz tufayli havo biroz salqin bo'lganda ham ko'ngilochar narsalar ko'p.","why":"\"Heated indoor play area\" — o'yin maydonchasi."},{"a":["keeper"],"ps":309.53,"en":321.09,"si":34,"ev":"And the other is called Shadow a Keeper and gives people a chance to become an animal keeper for a full day.","hl":"Keeper","uz":"Yana biri \"Shadow a Keeper\" deb ataladi: u odamlarga bir kun davomida hayvon parvarishlovchisi bo'lish imkonini beradi.","why":"\"Animal keeper for a full day\" — parvarishlovchi."},{"a":["voluntary"],"ps":330.26,"en":348.41,"si":38,"ev":"We have a number of jobs available for enthusiastic people who are interested in customer service work… And we also welcome applications from adults seeking voluntary work.","hl":"voluntary","uz":"Mijozlarga xizmat ko'rsatishga qiziqqan g'ayratli odamlar uchun bir qancha ish o'rinlari bor… Ko'ngilli ish izlayotgan kattalarning arizalarini ham mamnuniyat bilan qabul qilamiz.","why":"\"Voluntary work\" — ko'ngillilik ishi."}],"segs":[{"s":5.14,"e":10.97,"t":"You will hear an interview with a representative of a wildlife park called Paradise Wildlife Park."},{"s":11.77,"e":15.26,"t":"For questions 9 to 18, complete the sentences."},{"s":16.28,"e":19.42,"t":"You now have 45 seconds to look at part 2."},{"s":67.45,"e":74.21,"t":"OK, now I understand that the park is involved in one or two projects at the moment. That's right."},{"s":74.78,"e":83.55,"t":"Since 1994, we've been working with various partners to raise money and help coordinate something called Project Life Lion."},{"s":84.6,"e":90.69,"t":"project involves sending teams to villages which border the Serengeti National Park in East Africa."},{"s":91.19,"e":98.08,"t":"to vaccinate domestic dogs against canine distemper virus, CDV and rabies."},{"s":98.84,"e":105.41,"t":"In 1994, over one third of the Serengeti lions died as a result of C.D.V."},{"s":106.17,"e":110.11,"t":"passed from domestic dogs to the wild animal population."},{"s":111.06,"e":118.88,"t":"In addition to that, we are currently taking part in the Atlantic Rainforest Project and supporting the Community Conservation Project."},{"s":119.51,"e":127.52,"t":"about environmental issues."},{"s":128.18,"e":139.97,"t":"To do that, we have our own independently written Environmental Management System, which is now being used as a model by other organisations across the UK so that they can establish their own.","uz":"Buning uchun bizda mustaqil yozilgan o'z Ekologik boshqaruv tizimimiz bor; hozir uni Buyuk Britaniyadagi boshqa tashkilotlar namuna sifatida ishlatmoqda."},{"s":140.92,"e":148.06,"t":"Now, apart from the day-to-day business of visitors to the park, you also put on events, don't you? Yes."},{"s":148.7,"e":163.77,"t":"The park is a venue for all manner of corporate events such as product launches, team building, special events, barbecues, the list is endless and we play host to many charity and fundraising events each year.","uz":"Park har xil korporativ tadbirlar o'tkaziladigan joy: mahsulot taqdimotlari, jamoa mashg'ulotlari, maxsus tadbirlar, barbekyular — ro'yxat cheksiz."},{"s":164.34,"e":169.18,"t":"For them, we are happy to help with discounted tickets and competition prizes."},{"s":170.3,"e":178.08,"t":"Now, tell me about the Centre for Television and Radio Training. I gather you're connected with that. Yes, it's our sister company."},{"s":178.68,"e":185.15,"t":"If you've always dreamed of being a radio presenter, we offer you the opportunity to take the first steps.","uz":"Agar doim radio boshlovchisi bo'lishni orzu qilgan bo'lsangiz, sizga ilk qadamlarni qo'yish imkoniyatini beramiz."},{"s":185.88,"e":197.31,"t":"The centre has a range of courses from a one day experience to a five day full time course which leads to your own two hour show on our own station Paradise FM."},{"s":198.04,"e":202.78,"t":"courses take place at our studio complex. Wow, that sounds great!"},{"s":203.51,"e":213.95,"t":"Now back to animals, which is after all what the park is really all about. One thing that I see you run is something called 'adopt an animal'. Tell me about that."},{"s":214.42,"e":218.91,"t":"Yes, adopting an animal is a great way to mark a special occasion."},{"s":219.38,"e":221.95,"t":"for yourself or for a friend or loved one."},{"s":222.68,"e":225.02,"t":"All our animals are available for adoption."},{"s":225.5,"e":233.98,"t":"And to ensure that they're all affordable, whatever their size, adoptions are available in shared units of £50 and last for 12 months."},{"s":234.94,"e":244.96,"t":"If you adopt an animal, you receive a certificate, a photograph of and information about your chosen animal, and a complimentary ticket for two people to the park."},{"s":245.66,"e":251.23,"t":"Now, talking of tickets, people can get season tickets for the park, can't they? That's right."},{"s":251.8,"e":255.65,"t":"Our season tickets are very popular and extremely good value for money."},{"s":256.31,"e":261.28,"t":"If you visit us more than five times during the year, you will be saving money."},{"s":262.01,"e":266.62,"t":"Season tickets are valid for 12 months and allow unlimited access to the park."},{"s":267.35,"e":278.81,"t":"And we can even take people's passport-sized photographs for them for the season ticket, free of charge. But are you open all year? Yes. We're open 365 days a year."},{"s":279.54,"e":285.95,"t":"With our heated indoor play area there is still lots of fun to be had even when the weather is a bit chilly.","uz":"Isitiladigan yopiq o'yin maydonchamiz tufayli havo biroz salqin bo'lganda ham ko'ngilochar narsalar ko'p."},{"s":286.81,"e":297.31,"t":"Now, people can also take part in what you call experience days, can't they? Yes. The experience days are great to give to someone who is 12 or over as a gift."},{"s":297.98,"e":305.53,"t":"One of them is called Feed the Big Cats and gives people the opportunity to hand feed the big cats for half an hour."},{"s":306.17,"e":309.09,"t":"Another is called 'Walk with our Wolves'."},{"s":309.53,"e":321.09,"t":"during which people take a walk in the woods with these impressive animals. And the other is called Shadow a Keeper and gives people a chance to become an animal keeper for a full day."},{"s":322.33,"e":325.76,"t":"Finally, if I wanted to work in the park..."},{"s":326.55,"e":327.84,"t":"What chance would I have?"},{"s":328.31,"e":329.73,"t":"pretty good right now."},{"s":330.26,"e":348.41,"t":"We have a number of jobs available for enthusiastic people who are interested in customer service work… And we also welcome applications from adults seeking voluntary work.","uz":"Mijozlarga xizmat ko'rsatishga qiziqqan g'ayratli odamlar uchun bir qancha ish o'rinlari bor… Ko'ngilli ish izlayotgan kattalarning arizalarini ham mamnuniyat bilan qabul qilamiz."}]},{"n":39,"title":"The Ideas Competition","dur":279.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The money given to the winner is not a loan."},{"k":"p","t":"The winner might be an {1} with a plan for improving a water supply."},{"k":"p","t":"The winner might have an idea about how to help the poorest people in the world."},{"k":"p","t":"If you enter the competition by phone you must explain your idea in a maximum of one {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"One of the categories is for people who want to start a business that provides a product or service that currently doesn't exist."},{"k":"p","t":"One of the categories is for people who want to take part in a project that is {3} responsible."},{"k":"p","t":"One of the rules is that {4} entries for the competition are not allowed."},{"k":"p","t":"Before you phone, it may be a good idea to prepare a {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"To win, you must show that you have a lot of {6} for your idea."},{"k":"p","t":"Judges will listen to the ideas presented by 2 people."}],"items":[{"a":["engineer"],"ps":135.58,"en":147.26,"si":14,"ev":"Are you an engineer with an idea that could transform sanitation and bring clean water to Africa? Or an architect with a vision that could solve the problems in Britain's inner cities?","hl":"engineer","uz":"Siz Afrikada sanitariyani o'zgartirib, toza suv keltira oladigan g'oyasi bor muhandismisiz?","why":"\"An engineer… clean water\" — muhandis. Architect — boshqa misol (tuzoq)."},{"a":["minute"],"ps":162.62,"en":175.2,"si":18,"ev":"If you phone, after leaving your name and address, you will have up to one minute to pitch your idea. If you choose to email, you will have to pitch your idea in no more than 100 words.","hl":"minute","uz":"Telefon qilsangiz, ism va manzilingizni qoldirgach, g'oyangizni taqdim qilish uchun ko'pi bilan bir daqiqa vaqtingiz bo'ladi. Email orqali bo'lsa — yuz so'zdan oshmasligi kerak.","why":"Telefonda — one minute. 100 words — email uchun (tuzoq)."},{"a":["socially"],"ps":194.52,"en":200.48,"si":22,"ev":"The third is for those who want to use their skills to support a socially responsible project.","hl":"socially","uz":"Uchinchisi — o'z ko'nikmalarini ijtimoiy mas'uliyatli loyihani qo'llab-quvvatlashga sarflamoqchi bo'lganlar uchun.","why":"\"Socially responsible project\" — ijtimoiy mas'uliyatli."},{"a":["multiple"],"ps":205.78,"en":217.66,"si":24,"ev":"Now, there are some other very important details if you are thinking of going in for the competition. Only one entry per person is allowed. Multiple entries are not permitted.","hl":"Multiple","uz":"Har bir kishidan faqat bitta ariza qabul qilinadi. Bir nechta ariza topshirishga ruxsat yo'q.","why":"\"Multiple entries are not permitted\" — bir nechta ariza."},{"a":["script"],"ps":230.42,"en":233.5,"si":27,"ev":"If it helps, write down a script and read that.","hl":"script","uz":"Yordam bersa, matn (ssenariy) yozib, uni o'qing.","why":"\"Write down a script\" — yozma matn."},{"a":["passion"],"ps":257.91,"en":265.98,"si":32,"ev":"Entrants must be able to demonstrate great passion for their project, with thought having been given to how it could be put into practice.","hl":"passion","uz":"Ishtirokchilar o'z loyihasiga katta ishtiyoqini ko'rsata olishi kerak.","why":"\"Great passion\" — ishtiyoq."}],"segs":[{"s":5.56,"e":7.97,"t":"You will hear an announcement about a competition."},{"s":8.92,"e":12.45,"t":"For questions 9 to 18, complete the sentences."},{"s":13.5,"e":16.54,"t":"You now have 45 seconds to look at part two."},{"s":64.6,"e":75.23,"t":"So are you thinking about that idea again? That absolute money spinner? The ultimate business brainchild that could change your fortunes and transform your life forever?"},{"s":75.9,"e":80.06,"t":"No, you think it's impossible. People like you should stick to dreaming."},{"s":80.76,"e":85.31,"t":"But what if you were given a real chance to change your life and achieve that goal?"},{"s":86.01,"e":89.82,"t":"How would you react if the support you need suddenly landed in your lap?"},{"s":90.46,"e":94.72,"t":"Not in the form of alone, but free. Well now's your chance."},{"s":95.22,"e":106.11,"t":"In this competition, we're offering £100,000 to a budding entrepreneur and there are no obligations other than that you have to use the money to follow through your idea."},{"s":107.03,"e":111.07,"t":"All you have to do is convince us that your plan is worth backing."},{"s":111.74,"e":117.57,"t":"The £100,000 prize is to help pay for your financial commitments while you pursue your goals."},{"s":118.65,"e":122.69,"t":"The competition is open to a variety of ideas and people."},{"s":123.64,"e":129.73,"t":"Perhaps you have a particular skill that you know could be put to more effective use in a different sector or country."},{"s":130.39,"e":134.75,"t":"Perhaps, given the right backing, you could change hundreds of lives."},{"s":135.58,"e":147.26,"t":"Are you an engineer with an idea that could transform sanitation and bring clean water to Africa? Or an architect with a vision that could solve the problems in Britain's inner cities?","uz":"Siz Afrikada sanitariyani o'zgartirib, toza suv keltira oladigan g'oyasi bor muhandismisiz?"},{"s":147.9,"e":154.27,"t":"Or are you a farmer who could teach the world's poorest people how to grow crops in the worst conditions?"},{"s":154.94,"e":159.26,"t":"If you were any of these, you could win the competition and the prize money."},{"s":160.02,"e":161.69,"t":"Here are the details for entering."},{"s":162.62,"e":175.2,"t":"If you phone, after leaving your name and address, you will have up to one minute to pitch your idea. If you choose to email, you will have to pitch your idea in no more than 100 words.","uz":"Telefon qilsangiz, ism va manzilingizni qoldirgach, g'oyangizni taqdim qilish uchun ko'pi bilan bir daqiqa vaqtingiz bo'ladi. Email orqali bo'lsa — yuz so'zdan oshmasligi kerak."},{"s":175.86,"e":179.81,"t":"There are three categories of entry and you will have to choose one of them."},{"s":180.76,"e":187.07,"t":"The first category is for those with an innovative idea for a business offering a new product or service."},{"s":187.7,"e":193.57,"t":"The second is for those who plan to learn new skills by taking a course such as an MBA."},{"s":194.52,"e":200.48,"t":"The third is for those who want to use their skills to support a socially responsible project.","uz":"Uchinchisi — o'z ko'nikmalarini ijtimoiy mas'uliyatli loyihani qo'llab-quvvatlashga sarflamoqchi bo'lganlar uchun."},{"s":201.05,"e":204.83,"t":"The winner will be chosen from across all three categories."},{"s":205.78,"e":217.66,"t":"Now, there are some other very important details if you are thinking of going in for the competition. Only one entry per person is allowed. Multiple entries are not permitted.","uz":"Har bir kishidan faqat bitta ariza qabul qilinadi. Bir nechta ariza topshirishga ruxsat yo'q."},{"s":218.46,"e":224.64,"t":"If you make a mistake while delivering your pitch, you will not be allowed to call back and leave another entry."},{"s":225.5,"e":229.53,"t":"We suggest that you practice delivering your pitch before phoning."},{"s":230.42,"e":233.5,"t":"If it helps, write down a script and read that.","uz":"Yordam bersa, matn (ssenariy) yozib, uni o'qing."},{"s":233.98,"e":236.89,"t":"And remember, you can't go over the time limit."},{"s":237.78,"e":241.89,"t":"Our judges will be looking for a number of qualities when they make their decision."},{"s":242.74,"e":247.58,"t":"The best idea will have big potential and demonstrate a great deal of innovation."},{"s":248.31,"e":257.02,"t":"The judges will want to be sure that the idea, if it was carried out, would change the life of the entrant and preferably the lives of others."},{"s":257.91,"e":265.98,"t":"Entrants must be able to demonstrate great passion for their project, with thought having been given to how it could be put into practice.","uz":"Ishtirokchilar o'z loyihasiga katta ishtiyoqini ko'rsata olishi kerak."},{"s":266.65,"e":269.82,"t":"The top 100 will then be whittled down to 10."},{"s":270.3,"e":276.7,"t":"who will be invited to present their ideas in person to a panel of judges. The winner will then be announced."}]},{"n":40,"title":"Spectacled Bears","dur":534.4,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Angela says that it was the great name of the spectacled bear that first interested her."},{"k":"p","t":"Angela mentions that the bear's markings can be found on its {1} as well as its eyes and cheeks."},{"k":"p","t":"Angela is pleased by evidence that spectacled bears have been seen in {2} areas of Argentina."},{"k":"p","t":"Angela says the bears usually live in {3}, though they can also be found in other places."},{"k":"p","t":"Spectacled bears behave differently from other types of bear during {4}, which Angela finds surprising."},{"k":"p","t":"Angela is upset that some humans are the biggest danger to spectacled bears."},{"k":"p","t":"Angela says that spectacled bears usually eat berries and tree bark."},{"k":"p","t":"Bears climb trees and make a platform, which fascinated Angela."},{"k":"p","t":"When bears eat meat, they much prefer {5} although they do eat other creatures."},{"k":"p","t":"One man has produced an amusing {6} about the time he spent studying the bears."}],"items":[{"a":["chest"],"ps":60.31,"en":79.65,"si":7,"ev":"Although these golden markings vary greatly from one bear to another and may not be limited to the eyes, they can extend as far as the bear's cheeks or even chest.","hl":"chest","uz":"Bu oltinrang dog'lar ayiqdan ayiqqa juda farq qiladi va faqat ko'z atrofida bo'lmasligi mumkin — ular yonoqlarigacha, hatto ko'kragigacha cho'zilishi mumkin.","why":"\"Cheeks or even chest\" — ko'krak."},{"a":["northern"],"ps":94.1,"en":108.41,"si":10,"ev":"We thought that it was only found in certain places in Venezuela and Chile, but I was thrilled to read some reports that suggested it might also be living in northern parts of Argentina and eastern Panama.","hl":"northern","uz":"Biz uni faqat Venesuela va Chilining ayrim joylarida uchraydi deb o'ylardik, lekin u Argentinaning shimoliy qismlarida va Panamaning sharqida ham yashashi mumkinligi haqidagi xabarlarni o'qib, juda xursand bo'ldim.","why":"Argentina — northern (shimoliy). Eastern — Panama haqida (tuzoq)."},{"a":["forests"],"ps":128.12,"en":131.58,"si":12,"ev":"They are most commonly found in forests though.","hl":"forests","uz":"Lekin ular ko'pincha o'rmonlarda uchraydi.","why":"Cho'llar va tog'lar ham tilga olinadi, lekin \"most commonly… forests\"."},{"a":["winter"],"ps":132.22,"en":147.39,"si":13,"ev":"Like me, you may be surprised to learn that they don't sleep all through the winter, as many other types of bear do.","hl":"winter","uz":"Men kabi siz ham ular boshqa ko'plab ayiqlar kabi butun qish uxlamasligini bilib hayron qolishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Don't sleep all through the winter\" — qishda boshqacha."},{"a":["mice"],"ps":229.37,"en":238.62,"si":22,"ev":"Very occasionally they do eat meat. Something like birds or insects. Though they like small mice best if they can get them.","hl":"mice","uz":"Juda kamdan-kam hollarda ular go'sht — qush yoki hasharot kabi narsalarni yeyishadi, lekin topa olsalar, mayda sichqonlarni eng yaxshi ko'rishadi.","why":"\"Like small mice best\" — sichqonlar."},{"a":["diary"],"ps":239.7,"en":258.91,"si":23,"ev":"We're really trying to make people more aware of the bears and we've made a television series about one man's efforts to make people understand the dangers facing the animals. He spent a long time in Peru studying them and has published a very funny diary of his time there.","hl":"diary","uz":"Biz odamlarni ayiqlardan xabardor qilishga harakat qilyapmiz va bir kishining sa'y-harakatlari haqida teleserial suratga oldik. U Peruda ayiqlarni uzoq o'rgangan va u yerdagi vaqti haqida juda kulgili kundalik nashr qilgan.","why":"TV series — tuzoq. Kulgili narsa — diary (kundalik)."}],"segs":[{"s":4.98,"e":10.62,"t":"You will hear a woman called Angela Thomas, who works for a wildlife organisation."},{"s":11.13,"e":13.41,"t":"talking about the spectacled bear."},{"s":14.39,"e":14.91,"t":"quest"},{"s":22.9,"e":24.7,"t":"Thanks for inviting me tonight."},{"s":25.3,"e":36.93,"t":"As you know, my main interest is in conservation and I'm lucky enough to work with lots of different organisations looking after animals both in captivity and in the wild."},{"s":37.62,"e":52.51,"t":"I'd been fascinated by all kinds of bears for a long time before I started working in this field, but it was the spectacled bear that really attracted me. Some people find it appealing because of its size and shape."},{"s":53.02,"e":59.84,"t":"And it's less well known than other types of bear. But for me, I thought it was such a great name."},{"s":60.31,"e":79.65,"t":"It comes from the patches of yellowish fur around the bear's eyes, which grow in a sort of circle shape like glasses. Although these golden markings vary greatly from one bear to another and may not be limited to the eyes, they can extend as far as the bear's cheeks or even chest."},{"s":80.73,"e":86.59,"t":"I'd like to explain what we know about this bear and why I find it so fascinating."},{"s":87.32,"e":93.63,"t":"It's the only survivor of a type of bear that once ranged across America during the last Ice Age."},{"s":94.1,"e":108.41,"t":"We thought that it was only found in certain places in Venezuela and Chile, but I was thrilled to read some reports that suggested it might also be living in northern parts of Argentina and eastern Panama.","uz":"Biz uni faqat Venesuela va Chilining ayrim joylarida uchraydi deb o'ylardik, lekin u Argentinaning shimoliy qismlarida va Panamaning sharqida ham yashashi mumkinligi haqidagi xabarlarni o'qib, juda xursand bo'ldim."},{"s":110.04,"e":127.55,"t":"It's quite difficult to find spectacled bears in the wild because they are quite shy animals and tend to live in a wide variety of habitats which can range from dry coastal deserts to high mountain areas above 4,000 metres."},{"s":128.12,"e":131.58,"t":"They are most commonly found in forests though.","uz":"Lekin ular ko'pincha o'rmonlarda uchraydi."},{"s":132.22,"e":147.39,"t":"Being such timid animals they tend to come out at night, which is another thing that makes them difficult to see, though like me, you may be surprised to learn that they don't sleep all through the winter, as many other types of bear do."},{"s":148.38,"e":159.07,"t":"We're not sure about the actual number of spectacled bears that remain in the wild, but it's been estimated that there are only about 2,400 still around."},{"s":159.74,"e":170.91,"t":"The bears are endangered not so much because they are hunted by other animals, but what I find really sad is the fact that humans destroy their habitat."},{"s":171.99,"e":184.0,"t":"Spectacled bears are quite small compared with other bears and of course they do have other enemies. These mostly include mountain lions and jaguars."},{"s":184.86,"e":186.91,"t":"they remain a smaller threat."},{"s":188.38,"e":195.71,"t":"The bears are primarily vegetarian and their normal diet is tree bark and berries."},{"s":196.28,"e":201.25,"t":"On rare occasions, though, they eat honey, which I thought was just something in children's books."},{"s":201.78,"e":219.68,"t":"I was interested to find that they are incredibly good climbers and one thing I found really funny is that they've been known to sit up in a tree for days. They make a platform. Why? I couldn't guess. But they're waiting for fruit to ripen so they can eat it."},{"s":220.34,"e":228.61,"t":"It's quite surprising that although they rarely eat meat, they have extremely strong jaws and wide, flat teeth."},{"s":229.37,"e":238.62,"t":"Very occasionally they do eat meat. Something like birds or insects. Though they like small mice best if they can get them.","uz":"Juda kamdan-kam hollarda ular go'sht — qush yoki hasharot kabi narsalarni yeyishadi, lekin topa olsalar, mayda sichqonlarni eng yaxshi ko'rishadi."},{"s":239.7,"e":258.91,"t":"We're really trying to make people more aware of the bears and we've made a television series about one man's efforts to make people understand the dangers facing the animals. He spent a long time in Peru studying them and has published a very funny diary of his time there.","uz":"Biz odamlarni ayiqlardan xabardor qilishga harakat qilyapmiz va bir kishining sa'y-harakatlari haqida teleserial suratga oldik. U Peruda ayiqlarni uzoq o'rgangan va u yerdagi vaqti haqida juda kulgili kundalik nashr qilgan."},{"s":259.45,"e":264.89,"t":"I hope everyone will read it and support our efforts to help these fascinating creatures."},{"s":265.43,"e":267.77,"t":"So, are there any questions?"}]},{"n":41,"title":"My Vacation Job in Australia","dur":480.1,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Chris thinks the best place to find a job like he had is the Internet."},{"k":"p","t":"Chris is studying {1} at university."},{"k":"p","t":"For most of the time he was working for the travel company, Chris lived in a {2} outside of the town."},{"k":"p","t":"Chris was often asked to go to a {3} at the weekend."},{"k":"p","t":"In the mornings, Chris had to drive tourists to see the sunrise in the desert."},{"k":"p","t":"Many of the tourists were unaware of the need to keep their {4} covered up when they were in the sun."},{"k":"p","t":"The tourists particularly wanted to know how to tell the difference between the tracks of the wild animals."},{"k":"p","t":"In the afternoons, the tourists were able to see some {5} that had more than one use."},{"k":"p","t":"Chris says that the local government would like to have a larger airport to attract tourists."},{"k":"p","t":"Chris advises other students to send off their job application forms in the month of {6} at the latest."}],"items":[{"a":["history"],"ps":69.56,"en":76.03,"si":9,"ev":"Studying tourism at university wasn't essential to get the job. In fact, my subject's history.","hl":"history","uz":"Ishga kirish uchun universitetda turizmni o'qish shart emas edi. Aslida mening fanim — tarix.","why":"Tourism — tuzoq. Chrisning fani — history."},{"a":["caravan"],"ps":84.02,"en":93.09,"si":11,"ev":"At first, I was given a room in a hotel in town, but I found that I felt quite lonely, so I moved into a caravan on the outskirts.","hl":"caravan","uz":"Avval menga shahardagi mehmonxonadan xona berishdi, lekin o'zimni yolg'iz his qildim, shuning uchun chekkadagi karvon-uyga (furgon) ko'chdim.","why":"Hotel — boshida (tuzoq). Ko'p vaqt — caravan."},{"a":["party"],"ps":99.7,"en":108.8,"si":13,"ev":"As there wasn't a cinema or restaurant nearby, people frequently had a party on Saturday night and I was always invited.","hl":"party","uz":"Yaqin atrofda kinoteatr yoki restoran yo'qligi uchun odamlar shanba oqshomlari tez-tez ziyofat qilishardi va meni doim taklif qilishardi.","why":"\"A party on Saturday night\" — ziyofat."},{"a":["shoulders"],"ps":135.22,"en":147.77,"si":18,"ev":"They knew, of course, about covering their head and neck with a hat, but often left their shoulders uncovered.","hl":"shoulders","uz":"Ular, albatta, bosh va bo'yinni shlyapa bilan yopish kerakligini bilishardi, lekin ko'pincha yelkalarini ochiq qoldirishardi.","why":"Head va neck — buni bilishgan (tuzoq). Bilishmagan — shoulders."},{"a":["plants"],"ps":175.03,"en":184.61,"si":22,"ev":"I used to take the afternoon group to a waterhole where they were shown which plants could be eaten and which were also used to make weapons for hunting.","hl":"plants","uz":"Tushdan keyingi guruhni suv havzasiga olib borardim: u yerda qaysi o'simliklarni yeyish mumkinligi va qaysilari ov qurollari yasashda ham ishlatilishi ko'rsatilardi.","why":"\"More than one use\" — ham yeyiladi, ham qurol yasaladi: plants."},{"a":["January"],"ps":220.28,"en":230.53,"si":27,"ev":"The busy tourist season in the area where I worked is from May to October, so you need to make sure your application is in by the January of the year you're hoping to work.","hl":"January","uz":"Men ishlagan hududda turistik mavsum maydan oktabrgacha, shuning uchun arizangiz ishlamoqchi bo'lgan yilingizning yanvarigacha topshirilgan bo'lishi kerak.","why":"May–October — mavsum, March — javob kelishi (tuzoqlar). Ariza muddati — January."}],"segs":[{"s":5.56,"e":8.13,"t":"You will hear a man called Chris Graham"},{"s":8.57,"e":13.47,"t":"talking to a group of students about a vacation job he had in Australia."},{"s":22.2,"e":28.25,"t":"Hello everyone, my name is Chris Graham and I spent my last vacation working in Australia."},{"s":29.02,"e":38.4,"t":"The place I was in is a popular tourist spot so there are lots of student jobs advertised in the newspaper, from hotel work to being a tour guide."},{"s":39.06,"e":43.61,"t":"I saw my job for a bus driver on the internet and so I applied."},{"s":44.12,"e":45.85,"t":"I'd recommend you do that too."},{"s":46.36,"e":52.7,"t":"The whole idea of getting to know another country really appealed to me and I'm really pleased I had the opportunity to go."},{"s":53.69,"e":64.13,"t":"I worked for a company which tries to help tourists understand what life used to be like before Europeans arrived - a time before clothes, cars and electricity."},{"s":64.86,"e":68.83,"t":"Many of the local people, the aborigines, work for the company."},{"s":69.56,"e":76.03,"t":"Studying tourism at university wasn't essential to get the job. In fact, my subject's history.","uz":"Ishga kirish uchun universitetda turizmni o'qish shart emas edi. Aslida mening fanim — tarix."},{"s":76.63,"e":83.04,"t":"What I did do was a short training course when I first arrived though to learn about the local plants and animals."},{"s":84.02,"e":93.09,"t":"At first, I was given a room in a hotel in town, but I found that I felt quite lonely, so I moved into a caravan on the outskirts.","uz":"Avval menga shahardagi mehmonxonadan xona berishdi, lekin o'zimni yolg'iz his qildim, shuning uchun chekkadagi karvon-uyga (furgon) ko'chdim."},{"s":93.66,"e":99.07,"t":"Lots of other staff lived on the site and I got to meet lots of the local people there too."},{"s":99.7,"e":108.8,"t":"Everyone was really friendly and as there wasn't a cinema or restaurant nearby, people frequently had a party on Saturday night and I was always invited."},{"s":110.1,"e":117.82,"t":"I worked six days a week and I had to get up really early in the morning when most people, and even the birds and animals, are asleep."},{"s":118.81,"e":122.33,"t":"This is so the tourists can get to take photos of the sunrise."},{"s":122.94,"e":128.67,"t":"I used to pick them up from their hotels around 5am and then head out of town and into the desert."},{"s":129.82,"e":134.69,"t":"The tourists were from all over the world and often had no experience of the heat."},{"s":135.22,"e":147.77,"t":"They knew, of course, about covering their head and neck with a hat, but often left their shoulders uncovered, which wasn't very sensible, especially if they hadn't been in the country for long and weren't used to the sun."},{"s":149.08,"e":156.57,"t":"After we had been into the desert, I would take the tourists to the local cultural centre where they had the opportunity to ask questions."},{"s":157.27,"e":165.95,"t":"The tourists were especially keen to find out how to distinguish the tracks of kangaroos from wallabies and wild dogs."},{"s":167.06,"e":174.33,"t":"After the morning session, I usually went back home, had a shower and a rest, then started again around two in the afternoon."},{"s":175.03,"e":184.61,"t":"I used to take the afternoon group to a waterhole where they were shown which plants could be eaten and which were also used to make weapons for hunting.","uz":"Tushdan keyingi guruhni suv havzasiga olib borardim: u yerda qaysi o'simliklarni yeyish mumkinligi va qaysilari ov qurollari yasashda ham ishlatilishi ko'rsatilardi."},{"s":185.82,"e":198.78,"t":"At one time, there were very few tourists in the particular area I worked in because you needed to get a coach from the small railway station in the nearest large town a good 200km away."},{"s":199.77,"e":207.39,"t":"There's now an airport, but the local government is keen to get one built which can take more flights, especially from abroad."},{"s":208.09,"e":215.17,"t":"I'm not sure about that, as I think it's busy enough as it is, but it would be good for the local economy, no doubt about it."},{"s":216.02,"e":219.74,"t":"Anyway, I really recommend working in Australia during your vacation."},{"s":220.28,"e":230.53,"t":"The busy tourist season in the area where I worked is from May to October, so you need to make sure your application is in by the January of the year you're hoping to work.","uz":"Men ishlagan hududda turistik mavsum maydan oktabrgacha, shuning uchun arizangiz ishlamoqchi bo'lgan yilingizning yanvarigacha topshirilgan bo'lishi kerak."},{"s":231.16,"e":239.36,"t":"You might not hear until March as it takes a while to process the applications and get references, but make sure you don't leave it too late."}]},{"n":42,"title":"Singing twins: Tim and Sam Tanner","dur":487.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The name of the talent competition which the twins won is Funtime."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim is exactly 10 minutes older than Sam."},{"k":"p","t":"The twins were born in the month of {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"The main physical difference between Tim and Sam is their {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim has a less {3} personality than Sam."},{"k":"p","t":"At school, both Tim and Sam were good at football."},{"k":"p","t":"Sam started taking {4} lessons when he was thirteen."},{"k":"p","t":"The fact that the twins share the same {5} sometimes leads to arguments."},{"k":"p","t":"Tim says a key part of the twins' image is the {6} they wear."},{"k":"p","t":"The title of the twins' next album is Time Dance."}],"items":[{"a":["October"],"ps":72.47,"en":82.27,"si":12,"ev":"She was quite relieved when we suddenly appeared in October rather than January, over two months earlier than expected.","hl":"October","uz":"Biz kutilgan yanvar o'rniga oktabrda, ikki oydan ko'proq erta tug'ilganimizda u ancha yengil tortgan.","why":"January — kutilgan oy (tuzoq). Tug'ilgan oy — October."},{"a":["voice"],"ps":99.19,"en":115.17,"si":16,"ev":"Even our dad makes a mistake sometimes calling me Sam and my brother Tim because there's hardly any difference in our hair and with the same height and build. But as soon as we open our mouths he'll know which one it is by the voice. Sam's is a bit deeper than mine, but most people don't even notice that.","hl":"voice","uz":"Sochimiz deyarli farq qilmaydi, bo'yimiz va qaddi-qomatimiz bir xil, lekin og'iz ochishimiz bilan ovozidan kimligini biladi. Semning ovozi menikidan biroz pastroq.","why":"Hair, height, build — bir xil. Farq — voice (ovoz)."},{"a":["confident"],"ps":130.23,"en":134.11,"si":21,"ev":"People that know us say I'm not as confident as Sami's, which is probably true.","hl":"confident","uz":"Bizni taniydiganlar men Semchalik o'ziga ishonchli emasligimni aytishadi, bu ehtimol to'g'ri.","why":"\"Not as confident as Sam\" — kamroq ishonchli."},{"a":["singing"],"ps":166.01,"en":176.29,"si":29,"ev":"I began learning the guitar and he started proper singing lessons with a private teacher when we were about 13. But a year or so later we both got into dancing in a big way.","hl":"singing","uz":"Men gitara chalishni o'rgana boshladim, u esa taxminan 13 yoshimizda xususiy o'qituvchidan qo'shiq darslarini ola boshladi.","why":"Guitar — Tim (tuzoq). Sem — singing. Dancing — keyinroq."},{"a":["shoes"],"ps":191.96,"en":196.83,"si":34,"ev":"But of course occasionally we have a row, usually about shoes because we share them too.","hl":"shoes","uz":"Albatta, ba'zan janjallashamiz, odatda poyabzal uchun, chunki ularni ham bo'lishamiz.","why":"Phone va computer ham umumiy, lekin janjal — shoes haqida."},{"a":["glasses"],"ps":211.32,"en":230.56,"si":37,"ev":"Our image is based on being twins and looking alike and because we both have poor eyesight we enjoy choosing different styles of glasses for performances, you know maybe green ones to go with green suits or dark ones with t-shirts and jeans. So the glasses are a major aspect of the way people see us on stage.","hl":"glasses","uz":"Imijimiz egizak va bir-birimizga o'xshashligimizga asoslangan. Ikkimizning ham ko'zimiz yomon bo'lgani uchun chiqishlarga turli uslubdagi ko'zoynaklar tanlashni yaxshi ko'ramiz. Ko'zoynaklar — sahnadagi qiyofamizning asosiy qismi.","why":"\"Glasses are a major aspect\" — ko'zoynak."}],"segs":[{"s":5.34,"e":7.39,"t":"You will hear a singer called Tim Tanner."},{"s":7.86,"e":10.4,"t":"who sings with his twin brother, Sam Tanner."},{"s":10.97,"e":12.93,"t":"talking about their lives and career."},{"s":14.46,"e":19.33,"t":"Hi there, my name's Tim Tanner and I usually sing with my twin brother Sam Tanner."},{"s":19.83,"e":21.5,"t":"I'm going to tell you about our career."},{"s":22.42,"e":32.03,"t":"Sam and I have been pretty famous as the Singing Twin Brothers for about three years and we've appeared on lots of TV shows including Summer Holiday Special and Funtime."},{"s":32.47,"e":40.13,"t":"which is the talent show where we were voted best act. You probably saw it. It's the one where the people in the acts had to be related to each other."},{"s":41.18,"e":45.66,"t":"After that we had four hit singles in a row and I guess the rest is history really."},{"s":46.42,"e":50.62,"t":"People often ask us what it's like to be twins who've grown up looking so alike."},{"s":51.35,"e":57.31,"t":"Sam and I have shared almost every experience and we never usually apart for more than an hour at a time."},{"s":58.04,"e":67.01,"t":"I was born 10 minutes before Sam, so officially I'm the older brother. Although we do actually have a real older brother Ken, who's a year older than us."},{"s":67.83,"e":71.77,"t":"We were born premature, you know, earlier than we were supposed to be."},{"s":72.47,"e":82.27,"t":"Mum says it was hard carrying both of us when she was pregnant, and she was quite relieved when we suddenly appeared in October rather than January, over two months earlier than expected."},{"s":83.54,"e":87.52,"t":"brother Ken's birthdays in December, so we're pretty close in age."},{"s":88.06,"e":90.69,"t":"It must have been tough for our parents with three young boys."},{"s":91.61,"e":98.72,"t":"Sam and I aren't completely identical, but most people can't tell us apart. It's only mum who never mixes us up."},{"s":99.19,"e":115.17,"t":"Even our dad makes a mistake sometimes calling me Sam and my brother Tim because there's hardly any difference in our hair and with the same height and build. But as soon as we open our mouths he'll know which one it is by the voice. Sam's is a bit deeper than mine, but most people don't even notice that.","uz":"Sochimiz deyarli farq qilmaydi, bo'yimiz va qaddi-qomatimiz bir xil, lekin og'iz ochishimiz bilan ovozidan kimligini biladi. Semning ovozi menikidan biroz pastroq."},{"s":116.09,"e":117.85,"t":"In character, we're quite similar."},{"s":118.58,"e":123.74,"t":"Both always loved music and since we were five we've wanted to be pop stars."},{"s":124.31,"e":127.74,"t":"We've always had a real interest in going out and being sociable too."},{"s":128.5,"e":129.69,"t":"I'm a bit shy though."},{"s":130.23,"e":134.11,"t":"People that know us say I'm not as confident as Sami's, which is probably true.","uz":"Bizni taniydiganlar men Semchalik o'ziga ishonchli emasligimni aytishadi, bu ehtimol to'g'ri."},{"s":134.74,"e":139.9,"t":"Although I'm not exactly shy, you know? After all, you can't appear on TV if you are!"},{"s":140.86,"e":144.25,"t":"At school we used to pretend to be each other sometimes for a laugh."},{"s":144.76,"e":151.55,"t":"Sometimes we'd swap places for spelling tests, but nobody noticed because we got the same marks, which were pretty low."},{"s":152.34,"e":155.49,"t":"better at sports and both played in the school football team."},{"s":156.18,"e":157.85,"t":"I was also good at basketball."},{"s":158.3,"e":161.47,"t":"But Sam wasn't as keen, preferring volleyball for some reason."},{"s":162.87,"e":165.5,"t":"both much more interested in music."},{"s":166.01,"e":176.29,"t":"I began learning the guitar and he started proper singing lessons with a private teacher when we were about 13. But a year or so later we both got into dancing in a big way.","uz":"Men gitara chalishni o'rgana boshladim, u esa taxminan 13 yoshimizda xususiy o'qituvchidan qo'shiq darslarini ola boshladi."},{"s":176.73,"e":181.25,"t":"And then we went to a special school where we could do loads of stuff that's turned out to be useful."},{"s":181.72,"e":182.69,"t":"Things like drama."},{"s":183.74,"e":185.44,"t":"We share everything."},{"s":185.88,"e":191.2,"t":"and have one phone and computer between us. And we get on well almost 100% of the time."},{"s":191.96,"e":196.83,"t":"But of course occasionally we have a row, usually about shoes because we share them too.","uz":"Albatta, ba'zan janjallashamiz, odatda poyabzal uchun, chunki ularni ham bo'lishamiz."},{"s":197.34,"e":204.29,"t":"But if we both want to wear the same ones for a show, then we'll argue for about 20 seconds and then one of us will give in and it'll all be over."},{"s":205.27,"e":210.27,"t":"We managed to share the computer pretty well without fighting over it, which some people might find surprising."},{"s":211.32,"e":230.56,"t":"Our image is based on being twins and looking alike and because we both have poor eyesight we enjoy choosing different styles of glasses for performances, you know maybe green ones to go with green suits or dark ones with t-shirts and jeans. So the glasses are a major aspect of the way people see us on stage.","uz":"Imijimiz egizak va bir-birimizga o'xshashligimizga asoslangan. Ikkimizning ham ko'zimiz yomon bo'lgani uchun chiqishlarga turli uslubdagi ko'zoynaklar tanlashni yaxshi ko'ramiz. Ko'zoynaklar — sahnadagi qiyofamizning asosiy qismi."}]},{"n":43,"title":"New Zealand journey","dur":445.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Grace travelled around South Island on something called green bus."},{"k":"p","t":"The first part of Grace's journey took her along the {1} coast of the island."},{"k":"p","t":"When Grace took a day trip to a place called Kaikoura, she particularly wanted to see {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Grace has kept in touch with a friend from Japan since she returned home."},{"k":"p","t":"Grace took her own {3} to New Zealand, so didn't need to hire one."},{"k":"p","t":"The best part of the trip for Grace was jet-boating on the Buller River with a company called Adventure Tours."},{"k":"p","t":"Grace had to visit a hospital because she injured her {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"At a market, Grace bought a {5} to take home."},{"k":"p","t":"The name of the hostel that Grace particularly recommends is the Lakeside."},{"k":"p","t":"Grace plans to go {6} with friends when she next visits North Island."}],"items":[{"a":["west"],"ps":55.54,"en":65.28,"si":9,"ev":"Then we headed off down the west coast, stopping at various places and then inland up to our final destination, Christchurch on the east coast.","hl":"west","uz":"Keyin g'arbiy qirg'oq bo'ylab janubga yo'l oldik, turli joylarda to'xtadik, so'ng ichkariga — sharqiy qirg'oqdagi so'nggi manzilimiz Kraystcherchga bordik.","why":"Birinchi qism — west coast. East — oxirgi manzil (tuzoq)."},{"a":["dolphins"],"ps":85.4,"en":90.78,"si":13,"ev":"It was dolphins I was keenest to see, but there are whales too.","hl":"dolphins","uz":"Eng ko'p ko'rishni xohlaganim — delfinlar edi, lekin u yerda kitlar ham bor.","why":"\"Keenest to see\" — eng ko'p xohlagan: dolphins. Whales — tuzoq."},{"a":["bike"],"ps":119.35,"en":123.39,"si":20,"ev":"I actually took my own bike along with me and did a fair bit of cycling around.","hl":"bike","uz":"Aslida o'z velosipedimni olib borgan edim va ancha velosipedda aylandim.","why":"Surfboard va quad bike — ijaraga olgan (tuzoq). O'ziniki — bike."},{"a":["foot"],"ps":150.71,"en":166.59,"si":25,"ev":"I fell and hurt my shoulder horse riding on a beach… I didn't need treatment. But then I actually had to go to Christchurch Hospital after doing something to my foot climbing over some rocks.","hl":"foot","uz":"Plyajda ot minayotib yiqilib, yelkamni lat yedirdim… davolanish kerak bo'lmadi. Lekin keyin toshlar ustidan o'tayotib oyog'imni shikastlab, Kraystcherch kasalxonasiga borishga majbur bo'ldim.","why":"Shoulder — kasalxonaga bormagan (tuzoq). Kasalxona — foot."},{"a":["mask"],"ps":182.42,"en":189.85,"si":29,"ev":"I got a fantastic wooden mask as a souvenir, but there were also paintings and jewelry and stuff that would have been nice to bring home too.","hl":"mask","uz":"Esdalik sifatida ajoyib yog'och niqob oldim, lekin rasmlar, taqinchoqlar ham bor edi — ularni ham olib kelsa yaxshi bo'lardi.","why":"\"A wooden mask as a souvenir\" — niqob. Paintings, jewellery — olmagan."},{"a":["walking"],"ps":210.97,"en":222.4,"si":35,"ev":"It's got famous mud pools and hot springs, which I might get to visit, but sightseeing's not my main aim. In fact, the reason I'm going is that some friends have offered to take me walking with them round all the best places.","hl":"walking","uz":"U yerda mashhur loy hovuzlari va issiq buloqlar bor, lekin diqqatga sazovor joylarni ko'rish asosiy maqsadim emas. Aslida do'stlarim meni eng yaxshi joylar bo'ylab piyoda sayrga olib borishni taklif qilishdi.","why":"\"Take me walking with them\" — piyoda sayr."}],"segs":[{"s":5.05,"e":10.14,"t":"You will hear a woman called Grace Connolly talking about her travel experiences in New Zealand."},{"s":14.01,"e":19.42,"t":"Hi there, my name's Grace Connolly and I'm just back from a fantastic trip to New Zealand."},{"s":20.09,"e":24.0,"t":"It really was the trip of a lifetime and I'd like to tell you all about it."},{"s":24.86,"e":28.99,"t":"New Zealand has two main islands, the North Island and the South Island."},{"s":29.59,"e":33.21,"t":"I went to the South Island and it's even more beautiful than I expected."},{"s":34.07,"e":41.73,"t":"There are many ways to see it. You can hire a car and drive, or some people go around by motorbike. You can even see the island by boat."},{"s":42.55,"e":48.13,"t":"I went on what's known as the green bus. Our driver was so helpful and really helped to make it a memorable journey."},{"s":49.05,"e":50.88,"t":"So what route did we take?"},{"s":51.54,"e":55.01,"t":"Well, we started in Nelson in the northwest of the island."},{"s":55.54,"e":65.28,"t":"Then we headed off down the west coast, stopping at various places and then inland up to our final destination, Christchurch on the east coast, the second largest city in New Zealand."},{"s":66.71,"e":72.38,"t":"I also went on a day tour to a place called Kaikoura which is 150km north of there."},{"s":73.21,"e":80.25,"t":"It's on the coast and is famous for its sea life and also for being one of the most exciting places in the world to see ocean birds."},{"s":81.11,"e":84.8,"t":"To really experience the day you have to opt for one of these trips."},{"s":85.4,"e":90.78,"t":"It was dolphins I was keenest to see, but there are whales too. It was an absolutely amazing day."},{"s":91.9,"e":95.2,"t":"I made so many new friends on the trip, which was always fun."},{"s":96.09,"e":100.29,"t":"There were people from all over the world, Korea, Russia, North America."},{"s":100.79,"e":103.36,"t":"I've stayed in regular contact with a girl I met from Japan."},{"s":103.93,"e":107.68,"t":"Most of us were quite young, but there was one guy from Germany in his 60s."},{"s":108.86,"e":114.88,"t":"New Zealand's famous for the sports you can do, but it can work out expensive to hire the equipment you need to do things."},{"s":115.74,"e":118.59,"t":"You had to pay rental charges and so on for everything."},{"s":119.35,"e":123.39,"t":"I actually took my own bike along with me and did a fair bit of cycling around.","uz":"Aslida o'z velosipedimni olib borgan edim va ancha velosipedda aylandim."},{"s":124.06,"e":130.56,"t":"I rented a surfboard for a day or half day, and though it was more expensive, I also went out on a quad bike one day."},{"s":131.64,"e":135.9,"t":"But the highlight of the trip for me was jet boating at a place called Buller River."},{"s":136.5,"e":144.38,"t":"I'd strongly recommend Adventure Tours, the company I did it with. Nothing was too much trouble, and they really made it fun and exciting."},{"s":145.02,"e":149.47,"t":"I didn't try the other company, which was called Great Days, but friends said it was okay too."},{"s":150.71,"e":166.59,"t":"Every trip has some problems. I fell and hurt my shoulder horse riding on a beach. Luckily the sand was soft enough to prevent it being anything serious and I didn't need treatment. But then I actually had to go to Christchurch Hospital after doing something to my foot climbing over some rocks."},{"s":167.03,"e":170.14,"t":"Anyway, there was nothing major and was fine after a couple of days."},{"s":171.38,"e":176.45,"t":"There are interesting things to buy on the South Island. Nelson Saturday Market's brilliant."},{"s":176.95,"e":181.69,"t":"There are stalls selling food, honey, bread and fruit, all sorts of things."},{"s":182.42,"e":189.85,"t":"I got a fantastic wooden mask as a souvenir, but there were also paintings and jewelry and stuff that would have been nice to bring home too.","uz":"Esdalik sifatida ajoyib yog'och niqob oldim, lekin rasmlar, taqinchoqlar ham bor edi — ularni ham olib kelsa yaxshi bo'lardi."},{"s":190.9,"e":195.07,"t":"The accommodation was great the whole way. The hostels we stayed in were all good."},{"s":195.93,"e":200.09,"t":"the fairway in Christchurch, or my favorite the lakeside in Nelson."},{"s":200.63,"e":202.88,"t":"That's the place I'd advise anyone to stay."},{"s":203.42,"e":205.69,"t":"If you go, say \"Grace told you about it.\""},{"s":206.46,"e":210.3,"t":"I'm already planning a return visit to New Zealand to North Island this time."},{"s":210.97,"e":222.4,"t":"It's got famous mud pools and hot springs, which I might get to visit, but sightseeing's not my main aim. In fact, the reason I'm going is that some friends have offered to take me walking with them round all the best places.","uz":"U yerda mashhur loy hovuzlari va issiq buloqlar bor, lekin diqqatga sazovor joylarni ko'rish asosiy maqsadim emas. Aslida do'stlarim meni eng yaxshi joylar bo'ylab piyoda sayrga olib borishni taklif qilishdi."},{"s":223.22,"e":224.38,"t":"I'm really looking forward to"},{"s":225.11,"e":227.2,"t":"So before I go on to tell you even"}]},{"n":44,"title":"Museum director","dur":520.8,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Carl says that the museum was last renovated in the year 1973."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl says that improvements in the {1} in museums often goes unnoticed."},{"k":"p","t":"There are now a total of 421 exhibits which visitors can see in the museum."},{"k":"p","t":"The exhibits are now arranged according to their {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"One of Carl's favourite pieces is a 4,500-year-old cup with a design of a {3} on the bottom."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl describes a strange farm model in the museum that features cows and a farmer."},{"k":"p","t":"Some visitors to the museum are frightened by the {4} of one large statue."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl also describes a vase which shows a man fighting with a {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Carl finds it surprising that one of the coins in the museum has such {6} decoration."},{"k":"p","t":"One simple exhibit that Carl likes is a plain stone with a picture of a fish on it."}],"items":[{"a":["lighting"],"ps":54.97,"en":70.33,"si":10,"ev":"People notice new cabinets and signs, but often not the fact that the lighting has been improved. Although it can change the whole way they see an object, and it's an area in which great technical progress has been made in the last few years.","hl":"lighting","uz":"Odamlar yangi vitrinalar va yozuvlarni payqaydi, lekin yoritish yaxshilanganini ko'pincha sezmaydi.","why":"\"Not the fact that the lighting has been improved\" — yoritish."},{"a":["age"],"ps":95.83,"en":108.54,"si":16,"ev":"Where before they were grouped according to their place of origin, we've now created a pathway through the museum that allows you to view them in order of age, starting with the oldest.","hl":"age","uz":"Avval ular kelib chiqqan joyiga qarab guruhlangan edi, endi muzey bo'ylab yo'lak yaratdik — eksponatlarni eng qadimiysidan boshlab yoshi bo'yicha ko'rasiz.","why":"Place of origin — avvalgi tartib (tuzoq). Hozir — age."},{"a":["leaf"],"ps":131.51,"en":139.93,"si":20,"ev":"Round the side, you see this quite lovely flower pattern. And then if you pick it up and look underneath, you can see the shape of a leaf there.","hl":"leaf","uz":"Yon tomonida juda chiroyli gulni ko'rasiz, agar ko'tarib, tagiga qarasangiz, u yerda barg shaklini ko'rasiz.","why":"Flower — yon tomonida (tuzoq). Tagida — leaf."},{"a":["eyes"],"ps":176.22,"en":182.37,"si":29,"ev":"Like there's one statue that's got a big head with lots of curly hair and eyes that seem to follow you around the room.","hl":"eyes","uz":"Masalan, bitta haykal bor: katta boshi, jingalak sochlari va xona bo'ylab sizni kuzatib yurgandek ko'zlari bor.","why":"\"Eyes that seem to follow you\" — qo'rqitadigan narsa: eyes."},{"a":["monster"],"ps":200.31,"en":205.18,"si":34,"ev":"You see this man, the hero, sailing with his soldiers and then battling with a monster.","hl":"monster","uz":"Bu odamni — qahramonni askarlari bilan suzib ketayotgan, keyin esa yirtqich maxluq bilan jang qilayotganini ko'rasiz.","why":"\"Battling with a monster\" — maxluq."},{"a":["detailed"],"ps":221.94,"en":233.02,"si":39,"ev":"There's one of a famous emperor that's special because the decoration on it is remarkably detailed. And you'd never think so much information could be included in one small object.","hl":"detailed","uz":"Mashhur imperator tasvirlangan bitta tanga bor — u alohida, chunki undagi bezak hayratlanarli darajada mayda ishlangan.","why":"\"Remarkably detailed\" — juda batafsil."}],"segs":[{"s":5.34,"e":11.04,"t":"You will hear a museum director called Karl Halford talking about the museum where he works."},{"s":14.36,"e":14.78,"t":"Hi there"},{"s":15.35,"e":19.9,"t":"My name's Karl Halford and I work at the local museum where I'm the director."},{"s":20.54,"e":25.66,"t":"The museum's recently reopened its Antiquities section which has been closed for over a year."},{"s":26.2,"e":27.58,"t":"Let me tell you all about it."},{"s":28.63,"e":31.1,"t":"Firstly, we wanted to give it a complete new look."},{"s":31.77,"e":42.33,"t":"As you know, the museum was founded in 1902 and remained unchanged, barring the extension in 1958 until our last renovation project in 1973."},{"s":42.84,"e":45.34,"t":"So it was high time we freshened things up a little."},{"s":46.39,"e":50.21,"t":"We've made a lot of changes, and not only to the exhibits themselves."},{"s":50.68,"e":54.24,"t":"like we've replaced the display cabinets and so on."},{"s":54.97,"e":70.33,"t":"People notice new cabinets and signs, but often not the fact that the lighting has been improved. Although it can change the whole way they see an object, and it's an area in which great technical progress has been made in the last few years.","uz":"Odamlar yangi vitrinalar va yozuvlarni payqaydi, lekin yoritish yaxshilanganini ko'pincha sezmaydi."},{"s":72.54,"e":74.65,"t":"What about the exhibits themselves?"},{"s":75.58,"e":77.05,"t":"altered the selection on show."},{"s":77.72,"e":82.78,"t":"Part of our collection of around 650 objects is actually still stored underground."},{"s":83.29,"e":89.6,"t":"And so we've got 429 out on display, compared to 390 previously."},{"s":90.78,"e":95.29,"t":"A significant change we've made is in the organization of the exhibits."},{"s":95.83,"e":108.54,"t":"Where before they were grouped according to their place of origin, we've now created a pathway through the museum that allows you to view them in order of age, starting with the oldest.","uz":"Avval ular kelib chiqqan joyiga qarab guruhlangan edi, endi muzey bo'ylab yo'lak yaratdik — eksponatlarni eng qadimiysidan boshlab yoshi bo'yicha ko'rasiz."},{"s":109.34,"e":117.15,"t":"We've also provided more information on the signs, such as who first discovered them, how we think they were used and so on."},{"s":118.71,"e":127.29,"t":"I'm often asked to talk about some of your favourite pieces. And it's hard to choose. But there's a fascinating cup. Just a simple cup."},{"s":127.8,"e":130.65,"t":"which is over 4,500 years old."},{"s":131.51,"e":139.93,"t":"Round the side, you see this quite lovely flower pattern. And then if you pick it up and look underneath, you can see the shape of a leaf there.","uz":"Yon tomonida juda chiroyli gulni ko'rasiz, agar ko'tarib, tagiga qarasangiz, u yerda barg shaklini ko'rasiz."},{"s":140.82,"e":144.13,"t":"It's a sort of mystery as to why someone would have put that there."},{"s":144.66,"e":145.98,"t":"and it survived so long"},{"s":147.83,"e":150.46,"t":"Another little mystery is a little set of figures."},{"s":151.03,"e":152.67,"t":"There's a farmer with two cows."},{"s":153.18,"e":157.89,"t":"Although they're certainly not horses or oxen, they do seem to be ploughing a field."},{"s":158.52,"e":165.34,"t":"But it's not 100% clear, because one's pointing forward and the other's pointing the opposite way. So how would that work?"},{"s":166.07,"e":167.1,"t":"Probably never know."},{"s":168.89,"e":175.07,"t":"The exhibits attract all sorts of visitors, young and old, though some of them are a bit scary for younger children."},{"s":176.22,"e":182.37,"t":"Like there's one statue that's got a big head with lots of curly hair and eyes that seem to follow you around the room.","uz":"Masalan, bitta haykal bor: katta boshi, jingalak sochlari va xona bo'ylab sizni kuzatib yurgandek ko'zlari bor."},{"s":183.22,"e":185.73,"t":"You notice kids looking back at them nervously."},{"s":186.17,"e":188.22,"t":"It's obviously a deliberate part of the design."},{"s":188.76,"e":192.7,"t":"And in fact, a lot of ancient art was about terrifying things."},{"s":193.66,"e":199.68,"t":"Like there's a special vase, which we've lovingly restored, that's painted all the way round with this amazing scene."},{"s":200.31,"e":205.18,"t":"You see this man, the hero, sailing with his soldiers and then battling with a monster.","uz":"Bu odamni — qahramonni askarlari bilan suzib ketayotgan, keyin esa yirtqich maxluq bilan jang qilayotganini ko'rasiz."},{"s":205.62,"e":207.23,"t":"And yet, we're not told."},{"s":207.99,"e":210.72,"t":"We don't know the outcome, who wins that fight?"},{"s":212.38,"e":215.07,"t":"but there's a lot that's interesting on a smaller scale too."},{"s":215.83,"e":221.12,"t":"We've included quite a few coins in the display because they're such good tellers of historical tales."},{"s":221.94,"e":233.02,"t":"There's one of a famous emperor that's special because the decoration on it is remarkably detailed. And you'd never think so much information could be included in one small object.","uz":"Mashhur imperator tasvirlangan bitta tanga bor — u alohida, chunki undagi bezak hayratlanarli darajada mayda ishlangan."},{"s":233.75,"e":236.51,"t":"But you can see the shape of his ears, his nose, and so on"},{"s":237.78,"e":243.29,"t":"At the other end of the artistic scale, we have a small rock, just a basic natural thing, not a statue."},{"s":243.77,"e":253.21,"t":"But we like to think about the young man, we assume he was a young man, out by the river and how he carved or just scratched the image of a fish onto it."},{"s":254.2,"e":261.5,"t":"Perhaps he caught an extra big one and wanted to celebrate the fact. Again, we'll never know for sure. But I love this simplicity."},{"s":263.0,"e":264.73,"t":"Before I go on, I wanted to show you"}]},{"n":45,"title":"Thorndale Method","dur":413.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"There is one centre in the UK situated outside Bristol."},{"k":"p","t":"The Thorndale method has had success with people addicted to {1} and {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Addicts take part in a 10-day course of treatment."},{"k":"p","t":"In a one-hour treatment session, smokers cannot stop smoking even when they want no more."},{"k":"p","t":"Smokers must keep smoking until they become {3} sick."},{"k":"p","t":"Many patients find the course too difficult to finish and give up early."},{"k":"p","t":"Those who manage to finish the course are most {4} to want to smoke again."},{"k":"p","t":"Alcoholics are allowed to become drunk under the watchful eyes of {5} personnel."},{"k":"p","t":"When they are later shown a video, most alcoholics feel great {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["alcohol"],"ps":65.4,"en":82.78,"si":5,"ev":"The new system being used here is called aversion therapy, although the idea itself is not new. And of all the clinics treating addicts of various kinds worldwide, the Thorndale Clinic has the highest success rate in treating abusers of alcohol and tobacco.","hl":"alcohol","uz":"Dunyo bo'ylab giyohvand va qaram odamlarni davolaydigan klinikalar ichida Thorndale klinikasi spirtli ichimlik va tamaki iste'molchilarini davolashda eng yuqori natijaga ega.","why":"\"Alcohol and tobacco\" — 1-bo'shliq: alcohol."},{"a":["tobacco"],"ps":65.4,"en":82.78,"si":5,"ev":"The new system being used here is called aversion therapy, although the idea itself is not new. And of all the clinics treating addicts of various kinds worldwide, the Thorndale Clinic has the highest success rate in treating abusers of alcohol and tobacco.","hl":"tobacco","uz":"Dunyo bo'ylab giyohvand va qaram odamlarni davolaydigan klinikalar ichida Thorndale klinikasi spirtli ichimlik va tamaki iste'molchilarini davolashda eng yuqori natijaga ega.","why":"\"Alcohol and tobacco\" — 2-bo'shliq: tobacco."},{"a":["physically"],"ps":119.7,"en":125.09,"si":10,"ev":"In fact, they are not allowed to stop smoking until they have been physically sick.","hl":"physically","uz":"Aslida ular jismonan ko'ngli aynimaguncha (qusmaguncha) chekishni to'xtatishga ruxsat yo'q.","why":"\"Physically sick\" — jismonan."},{"a":["unlikely"],"ps":154.65,"en":161.44,"si":16,"ev":"On the other hand, smokers who keep going to the end of the course are most unlikely to want a cigarette again.","hl":"unlikely","uz":"Boshqa tomondan, kursni oxirigacha o'tagan chekuvchilar yana sigaret chekishni xohlashi juda kam ehtimol.","why":"\"Most unlikely\" — juda kam ehtimol. \"Most likely\" — erta tashlaganlar haqida (tuzoq)."},{"a":["trained"],"ps":180.06,"en":184.41,"si":20,"ev":"During this stage, they are carefully monitored by trained personnel.","hl":"trained","uz":"Bu bosqichda ularni malakali xodimlar diqqat bilan kuzatib boradi.","why":"\"Trained personnel\" — o'qitilgan xodimlar."},{"a":["embarrassment"],"ps":194.42,"en":202.27,"si":22,"ev":"Nearly all subjects feel great embarrassment when faced with these forgotten scenes of uncontrolled drunkenness.","hl":"embarrassment","uz":"Deyarli hamma unutilgan, nazoratsiz mastlik sahnalarini ko'rganda qattiq uyaladi.","why":"\"Great embarrassment\" — qattiq uyalish."}],"segs":[{"s":6.07,"e":11.33,"t":"You will hear part of a radio talk about an institution that helps addicts."},{"s":24.44,"e":32.38,"t":"Why do perfectly sane, normal people pay up to £1,000 a week to make themselves sick?"},{"s":33.02,"e":35.33,"t":"Jane Seaworthy has been finding out."},{"s":36.31,"e":50.91,"t":"Well actually, the people attending the Thorndale Clinic, situated on the outskirts of Bristol, all have a problem, and it's a problem that has become increasingly common in the last two decades. That of addiction."},{"s":51.48,"e":64.51,"t":"There are over 50 addiction clinics operating in the United Kingdom, but what makes Thordale so special is a new kind of treatment that they have been applying with remarkable success."},{"s":65.4,"e":82.78,"t":"The new system being used here is called aversion therapy, although the idea itself is not new. And of all the clinics treating addicts of various kinds worldwide, the Thorndale Clinic has the highest success rate in treating abusers of alcohol and tobacco.","uz":"Dunyo bo'ylab giyohvand va qaram odamlarni davolaydigan klinikalar ichida Thorndale klinikasi spirtli ichimlik va tamaki iste'molchilarini davolashda eng yuqori natijaga ega."},{"s":83.64,"e":89.66,"t":"Addicts attending a 10-day course of treatment live, eat and sleep in the same building."},{"s":90.2,"e":95.01,"t":"and unlike other systems, are encouraged to indulge in their addiction."},{"s":95.45,"e":108.61,"t":"Instead of treating subjects with drugs that reduce their dependence, this course sets out to induce in its patients a strong feeling of disgust directed towards the object of their addiction."},{"s":109.34,"e":118.46,"t":"For example, a one-hour treatment session for smokers involves smoking rapidly without stopping well beyond the point where they want no more."},{"s":119.7,"e":125.09,"t":"In fact, they are not allowed to stop smoking until they have been physically sick.","uz":"Aslida ular jismonan ko'ngli aynimaguncha (qusmaguncha) chekishni to'xtatishga ruxsat yo'q."},{"s":125.62,"e":129.34,"t":"As you can imagine, this is not a pleasant process."},{"s":129.85,"e":140.48,"t":"It has to be repeated three times a day for the entire ten-day period in order that the subjects develop a strong enough hatred for their earlier addiction."},{"s":141.62,"e":142.59,"t":"Unfortunately, the"},{"s":143.06,"e":146.69,"t":"Many people find the course too painful to complete."},{"s":147.16,"e":154.08,"t":"and those who do give up early are not considered cured, as they will most likely return to their former habit."},{"s":154.65,"e":161.44,"t":"On the other hand, smokers who keep going to the end of the course are most unlikely to want a cigarette again.","uz":"Boshqa tomondan, kursni oxirigacha o'tagan chekuvchilar yana sigaret chekishni xohlashi juda kam ehtimol."},{"s":162.3,"e":170.01,"t":"Treatment for alcoholism has to be somewhat different, mainly because alcohol abuse involves loss of memory."},{"s":170.52,"e":173.5,"t":"This problem is overcome in a simple way."},{"s":174.74,"e":179.29,"t":"Patients are encouraged to drink excessively in the setting of a bar."},{"s":180.06,"e":184.41,"t":"During this stage, they are carefully monitored by trained personnel.","uz":"Bu bosqichda ularni malakali xodimlar diqqat bilan kuzatib boradi."},{"s":185.11,"e":193.73,"t":"Their behaviour is also recorded on videocassette and the following day they are shown their drunken performance from the night before."},{"s":194.42,"e":202.27,"t":"Nearly all subjects feel great embarrassment when faced with these forgotten scenes of uncontrolled drunkenness.","uz":"Deyarli hamma unutilgan, nazoratsiz mastlik sahnalarini ko'rganda qattiq uyaladi."},{"s":203.1,"e":210.53,"t":"Usually a 10 day course of treatment is all that is required to shift a patient's emotional attitude to drinking."},{"s":220.06,"e":221.92,"t":"You will hear the piece again."},{"s":223.54,"e":231.52,"t":"Why do perfectly sane, normal people pay up to £1,000 a week to make themselves sick?"},{"s":232.12,"e":234.43,"t":"Jane Seaworthy has been finding out."},{"s":235.42,"e":250.01,"t":"While actually, the people attending the Thorndale Clinic, situated on the outskirts of Bristol, all have a problem, and it's a problem that has become increasingly common in the last two decades. That of addiction."},{"s":250.62,"e":263.65,"t":"There are over 50 addiction clinics operating in the United Kingdom, but what makes Thordale so special is a new kind of treatment that they have been applying with remarkable success."},{"s":264.5,"e":271.1,"t":"The new system being used here is called aversion therapy, although the idea itself is not new."},{"s":271.58,"e":281.89,"t":"And of all the clinics treating addicts of various kinds worldwide, the Thorndale Clinic has the highest success rate in treating abusers of alcohol and tobacco."},{"s":282.74,"e":288.8,"t":"Addicts attending a 10-day course of treatment live, eat and sleep in the same building."},{"s":289.3,"e":294.11,"t":"and unlike other systems, are encouraged to indulge in their addiction."},{"s":294.55,"e":307.71,"t":"Instead of treating subjects with drugs that reduce their dependence, this course sets out to induce in its patients a strong feeling of disgust directed towards the object of their addiction."},{"s":308.44,"e":317.57,"t":"For example, a one-hour treatment session for smokers involves smoking rapidly without stopping well beyond the point where they want no more."},{"s":318.81,"e":324.22,"t":"In fact, they are not allowed to stop smoking until they have been physically sick."},{"s":324.76,"e":328.48,"t":"As you can imagine, this is not a pleasant process."},{"s":328.98,"e":339.58,"t":"It has to be repeated three times a day for the entire ten-day period in order that the subjects develop a strong enough hatred for their earlier addiction."},{"s":340.73,"e":341.66,"t":"Unfortunately,"},{"s":342.17,"e":345.79,"t":"Many people find the course too painful to complete."},{"s":346.26,"e":353.21,"t":"and those who do give up early are not considered cured, as they will most likely return to their former habit."},{"s":353.75,"e":360.54,"t":"On the other hand, smokers who keep going to the end of the course are most unlikely to want a cigarette again."},{"s":361.4,"e":369.12,"t":"Treatment for alcoholism has to be somewhat different, mainly because alcohol abuse involves loss of memory."},{"s":369.62,"e":372.61,"t":"This problem is overcome in a simple way."},{"s":373.85,"e":378.4,"t":"Patients are encouraged to drink excessively in the setting of a bar."},{"s":379.16,"e":383.52,"t":"During this stage, they are carefully monitored by trained personnel."},{"s":384.22,"e":392.77,"t":"Their behaviour is also recorded on videocassette and the following day they are shown their drunken performance from the night before."},{"s":393.5,"e":401.31,"t":"Nearly all subjects feel great embarrassment when faced with these forgotten scenes of uncontrolled drunkenness."},{"s":402.17,"e":409.6,"t":"Usually a 10 day course of treatment is all that is required to shift a patient's emotional attitude to drinking."}]},{"n":46,"title":"Society and the Media","dur":380.9,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"The three forms of media are TV, radio and newspapers."},{"k":"p","t":"Politicians use the media during political {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Entertainers use it to stay in the public eye."},{"k":"p","t":"The percentage of people who did not have a particular point of view about the privacy of celebrities was {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"The most influential form of media is TV. We can be deceived by TV when we are shown carefully selected {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"Some TV stations turn true events into {4}."},{"k":"p","t":"A newspaper had to pay 1 million pounds for printing lies about a pop singer. Sometimes a paper can avoid being sued if it makes a public {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"There are two kinds of newspaper; the \"quality\" papers and the {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["campaigns"],"ps":49.37,"en":53.44,"si":5,"ev":"Politicians use it in their political campaigns in order to gain support.","hl":"campaigns","uz":"Siyosatchilar undan qo'llab-quvvatlash olish uchun o'z siyosiy kampaniyalarida foydalanadi.","why":"\"Political campaigns\" — saylov kampaniyalari."},{"a":["4%","4 percent","four percent"],"ps":91.83,"en":97.82,"si":12,"ev":"11% believed they were still entitled to their privacy and 4% had no opinion either way.","hl":"4%","uz":"11% ular hali ham shaxsiy hayot daxlsizligiga haqli deb hisoblagan, 4% esa hech qanday fikr bildirmagan.","why":"11% — boshqa fikr (tuzoq). \"No opinion\" — 4%."},{"a":["images"],"ps":116.28,"en":127.45,"si":16,"ev":"The belief that if we can see through images what is happening we cannot be tricked or lied to is a fallacy. Carefully chosen or edited images can deceive us more than words.","hl":"images","uz":"Agar nima bo'layotganini tasvirlar orqali ko'rsak, bizni aldab bo'lmaydi degan ishonch — xato. Puxta tanlangan yoki tahrirlangan tasvirlar so'zlardan ham ko'proq aldashi mumkin.","why":"\"Carefully chosen or edited images\" — tasvirlar."},{"a":["fiction"],"ps":139.19,"en":142.62,"si":19,"ev":"This kind of false information turns fact into fiction.","hl":"fiction","uz":"Bunday yolg'on ma'lumot haqiqatni to'qimaga (fiction) aylantiradi.","why":"\"Turns fact into fiction\" — to'qima."},{"a":["apology"],"ps":169.94,"en":176.54,"si":26,"ev":"Sometimes the papers are lucky and get away with making a public apology and withdrawing what they had previously said about somebody.","hl":"apology","uz":"Ba'zan gazetalarga omad kulib boqadi va ular ommaviy uzr so'rash hamda aytganlarini qaytarib olish bilan qutulib qolishadi.","why":"\"Making a public apology\" — ommaviy uzr."},{"a":["tabloids"],"ps":177.43,"en":185.89,"si":27,"ev":"A distinction has to be made between newspapers though, as they do tend to fall into two groups, the tabloids and the so-called quality newspapers.","hl":"tabloids","uz":"Biroq gazetalarni farqlash kerak, chunki ular ikki guruhga bo'linadi: tabloidlar va \"sifatli\" gazetalar.","why":"Quality papers — kitobda berilgan. Ikkinchi tur — tabloids."}],"segs":[{"s":6.01,"e":11.71,"t":"You're going to hear somebody giving their opinion about the media and its influence on society."},{"s":21.46,"e":26.37,"t":"There is no escaping the fact that the media has become one of the most powerful influences in our lives."},{"s":27.0,"e":32.73,"t":"TV, radio and newspapers are the three main forms of media that we have daily contact with."},{"s":33.5,"e":40.25,"t":"Because of their importance, it is inevitable that controversy will often go hand in hand with such a powerful force."},{"s":40.89,"e":48.45,"t":"The media is not always used wisely or responsibly and is often a source of gossip, scandal or propaganda."},{"s":49.37,"e":53.44,"t":"Politicians use it in their political campaigns in order to gain support.","uz":"Siyosatchilar undan qo'llab-quvvatlash olish uchun o'z siyosiy kampaniyalarida foydalanadi."},{"s":54.14,"e":58.97,"t":"Entertainers and celebrities use it to promote themselves and keep themselves in the public eye."},{"s":59.86,"e":66.49,"t":"This is, of course, to their advantage, but on the other hand, they are also open to the disadvantages of publicity."},{"s":67.35,"e":72.86,"t":"Private lives are brought out into the open and the word 'private' no longer suits the situation."},{"s":73.78,"e":80.8,"t":"Celebrities find themselves being followed and photographed at all times of day or night and in the most personal situations."},{"s":81.62,"e":86.14,"t":"A server has been carried out asking people what they thought of this invasion of privacy."},{"s":86.58,"e":91.13,"t":"and a massive 85% thought that celebrities were asking for it."},{"s":91.83,"e":97.82,"t":"11% believed they were still entitled to their privacy and 4% had no opinion either way.","uz":"11% ular hali ham shaxsiy hayot daxlsizligiga haqli deb hisoblagan, 4% esa hech qanday fikr bildirmagan."},{"s":98.84,"e":103.77,"t":"The survey also asked which form of media people felt they were most influenced by."},{"s":104.47,"e":109.47,"t":"Over two-thirds of the people asked said TV rather than radio or newspapers."},{"s":110.23,"e":115.65,"t":"This then leads us to the question of how reliable the information that we get from TV is."},{"s":116.28,"e":127.45,"t":"The belief that if we can see through images what is happening we cannot be tricked or lied to is a fallacy. Carefully chosen or edited images can deceive us more than words.","uz":"Agar nima bo'layotganini tasvirlar orqali ko'rsak, bizni aldab bo'lmaydi degan ishonch — xato. Puxta tanlangan yoki tahrirlangan tasvirlar so'zlardan ham ko'proq aldashi mumkin."},{"s":128.06,"e":132.03,"t":"It is in fact the images that are not shown which often speak the truth."},{"s":132.79,"e":138.43,"t":"Some channels have even been accused of showing scenes that were not actually from the place being reported about."},{"s":139.19,"e":142.62,"t":"This kind of false information turns fact into fiction.","uz":"Bunday yolg'on ma'lumot haqiqatni to'qimaga (fiction) aylantiradi."},{"s":143.13,"e":145.66,"t":"But how is the viewer meant to distinguish between the two?"},{"s":146.87,"e":147.36,"t":"problem."},{"s":148.25,"e":152.96,"t":"Radio and newspapers, on the other hand, rely on words to get their story across."},{"s":153.4,"e":157.18,"t":"and if they intentionally lie, they run the risk of being taken to court later."},{"s":157.91,"e":161.76,"t":"This of course happens regularly, particularly when a celebrity is involved."},{"s":162.74,"e":168.99,"t":"One rock singer was recently awarded £1 million when a tabloid paper said he was a homosexual."},{"s":169.94,"e":176.54,"t":"Sometimes the papers are lucky and get away with making a public apology and withdrawing what they had previously said about somebody.","uz":"Ba'zan gazetalarga omad kulib boqadi va ular ommaviy uzr so'rash hamda aytganlarini qaytarib olish bilan qutulib qolishadi."},{"s":177.43,"e":185.89,"t":"A distinction has to be made between newspapers though, as they do tend to fall into two groups, the tabloids and the so-called quality newspapers.","uz":"Biroq gazetalarni farqlash kerak, chunki ular ikki guruhga bo'linadi: tabloidlar va \"sifatli\" gazetalar."},{"s":186.39,"e":187.52,"t":"The question is though."},{"s":187.96,"e":191.9,"t":"Can we really trust anybody to tell us the facts objectively?"},{"s":201.69,"e":203.55,"t":"You will hear the piece again."},{"s":204.06,"e":204.45,"t":"(be"},{"s":206.04,"e":210.94,"t":"There is no escaping the fact that the media has become one of the most powerful influences in our lives."},{"s":211.61,"e":217.31,"t":"TV, radio and newspapers are the three main forms of media that we have daily contact with."},{"s":217.98,"e":224.8,"t":"Because of their importance, it is inevitable that controversy will often go hand in hand with such a powerful force."},{"s":225.43,"e":232.99,"t":"The media is not always used wisely or responsibly and is often a source of gossip, scandal or propaganda."},{"s":233.91,"e":238.01,"t":"Politicians use it in their political campaigns in order to gain support."},{"s":238.68,"e":243.55,"t":"Entertainers and celebrities use it to promote themselves and keep themselves in the public eye."},{"s":244.41,"e":251.07,"t":"This is, of course, to their advantage, but on the other hand, they are also open to the disadvantages of publicity."},{"s":251.93,"e":257.41,"t":"Private lives are brought out into the open and the word 'private' no longer suits the situation."},{"s":258.36,"e":265.34,"t":"Celebrities find themselves being followed and photographed at all times of day or night and in the most personal situations."},{"s":266.2,"e":270.72,"t":"A server has been carried out asking people what they thought of this invasion of privacy."},{"s":271.16,"e":275.68,"t":"and a massive 85% thought that celebrities were asking for it."},{"s":276.41,"e":279.55,"t":"11% believed they were still entitled to their privacy."},{"s":280.09,"e":282.37,"t":"and 4% had no opinion either way."},{"s":283.42,"e":288.32,"t":"The survey also asked which form of media people felt they were most influenced by."},{"s":289.05,"e":294.01,"t":"over two-thirds of the people asked said TV rather than radio or newspapers."},{"s":294.81,"e":300.22,"t":"This then leads us to the question of how reliable the information that we get from TV is."},{"s":300.86,"e":307.26,"t":"The belief that if we can see through images what is happening, we cannot be tricked or lied to is a fallacy."},{"s":307.96,"e":312.03,"t":"Carefully chosen or edited images can deceive us more than words."},{"s":312.63,"e":316.61,"t":"It is in fact the images that are not shown which often speak the truth."},{"s":317.37,"e":323.01,"t":"Some channels have even been accused of showing scenes that were not actually from the place being reported about."},{"s":323.77,"e":327.17,"t":"This kind of false information turns fact into fiction."},{"s":327.86,"e":330.24,"t":"How is the viewer meant to distinguish between the two?"},{"s":332.79,"e":337.5,"t":"Radio and newspapers, on the other hand, rely on words to get their story across."},{"s":337.98,"e":341.76,"t":"and if they intentionally lie, they run the risk of being taken to court later."},{"s":342.49,"e":346.3,"t":"This of course happens regularly, particularly when a celebrity is involved."},{"s":347.32,"e":353.57,"t":"One rock singer was recently awarded £1 million when a tabloid paper said he was a homosexual."},{"s":354.46,"e":361.05,"t":"Sometimes the papers are lucky and get away with making a public apology and withdrawing what they had previously said about somebody."},{"s":361.94,"e":370.4,"t":"A distinction has to be made between newspapers though, as they do tend to fall into two groups, the tabloids and the so-called quality newspapers."},{"s":370.9,"e":376.41,"t":"The question is though, can we really trust anybody to tell us the facts objectively?"}]},{"n":47,"title":"Women's basketball","dur":461.3,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Britt first designed her website when she was at high school."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt's website is now called {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt says that team sports is the main topic now covered by her website."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt began writing her book in the month of {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt says that women's basketball has been an Olympic sport since the year 1976."},{"k":"p","t":"The first women basketball players suffered broken {3} as well as discomfort as a result of their clothing."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt says that both handkerchiefs and {4} were often found on court after early women's games."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt mentions {5} gum as something that women basketball players were not allowed to use on court."},{"k":"p","t":"Britt tells us about a women's team with the name Red Heads."},{"k":"p","t":"When talking about her book, Britt describes herself as a {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["matchgirl.com"],"ps":36.31,"en":50.14,"si":3,"ev":"I designed a site about girls basketball which I was passionate about and called it femalebasket.com I knew the name wasn't right and before it got really successful I changed it to matchgirl.com and that was a really good move","hl":"matchgirl.com","uz":"Men qizlar basketboli haqida sayt yaratib, uni femalebasket.com deb atadim. Nom to'g'ri emasligini bilardim va sayt juda mashhur bo'lishidan oldin uni matchgirl.com ga o'zgartirdim.","why":"femalebasket.com — eski nom (tuzoq). Hozirgisi — matchgirl.com."},{"a":["May"],"ps":85.37,"en":96.25,"si":11,"ev":"I knew I wanted to write it late last year and started to loosely plan it out in January of this year. It wasn't until May that I had enough time to get down to doing everything I'd envisioned, but it was all done by the end of July.","hl":"May","uz":"Uni yozishni o'tgan yil oxirida xohlaganimni bilardim va bu yil yanvarda taxminiy reja tuzdim. Faqat mayga kelib, o'ylaganlarimni bajarishga vaqtim yetdi, iyul oxirida esa hammasi tayyor edi.","why":"January — reja tuzgan (tuzoq), July — tugatgan. Yozishni boshlagan — May."},{"a":["bones"],"ps":138.74,"en":145.85,"si":18,"ev":"And it wasn't only the discomfort they suffered, it led to quite a few broken bones, cos players tended to trip over their skirts and stuff.","hl":"bones","uz":"Ular nafaqat noqulaylikdan aziyat chekishgan — bu ko'plab suyak sinishlariga ham olib kelgan, chunki o'yinchilar yubkalariga qoqilib ketishardi.","why":"\"Broken bones\" — suyak sinishi."},{"a":["hairpins"],"ps":150.81,"en":159.2,"si":20,"ev":"Then, at the end of a woman's game, there'd be like handkerchiefs and hairpins scattered all over the court, which of course wasn't the case with the men either.","hl":"hairpins","uz":"Ayollar o'yini oxirida esa maydonda ro'mollar va soch to'g'nag'ichlari sochilib yotardi.","why":"\"Handkerchiefs and hairpins\" — soch to'g'nag'ichlari."},{"a":["chewing"],"ps":178.87,"en":188.22,"si":25,"ev":"Not so much the equipment, but silly things like chewing gum were specifically prohibited in the women's game because it was considered unfeminine. Not because it was dangerous or anything.","hl":"chewing","uz":"Asbob-uskunalar emas, balki saqich chaynash kabi bema'ni narsalar ayollar o'yinida maxsus taqiqlangan edi, chunki bu ayolga xos emas deb hisoblangan.","why":"\"Chewing gum… prohibited\" — saqich."},{"a":["perfectionist"],"ps":214.58,"en":218.27,"si":29,"ev":"I know I ought to be proud of what I've done, but I'm such a perfectionist.","hl":"perfectionist","uz":"Qilgan ishimdan faxrlanishim kerakligini bilaman, lekin men juda mukammallikka intiluvchiman.","why":"\"Such a perfectionist\" — mukammallikka intiluvchi."}],"segs":[{"s":5.05,"e":9.21,"t":"You will hear a woman called Britt Foxton talking about women's basketball."},{"s":12.44,"e":23.81,"t":"Hi, my name's Britt Foxton and I'm the founder of a website devoted to women's basketball and I've also just written a book on the same subject. But first up, let me tell you how I got started with the site."},{"s":24.57,"e":35.49,"t":"Although it really got going once I was at university, it actually started out as a high school project, you know, a design a website kind of thing. But it wasn't like anyone expected it to become real or anything."},{"s":36.31,"e":50.14,"t":"I designed a site about girls basketball which I was passionate about and called it femalebasket.com I knew the name wasn't right and before it got really successful I changed it to matchgirl.com and that was a really good move","uz":"Men qizlar basketboli haqida sayt yaratib, uni femalebasket.com deb atadim. Nom to'g'ri emasligini bilardim va sayt juda mashhur bo'lishidan oldin uni matchgirl.com ga o'zgartirdim."},{"s":51.16,"e":56.41,"t":"And although it started with basketball, the sites kind of evolved to include other games as well."},{"s":56.98,"e":63.61,"t":"It features a variety of articles, reviews and editorials on everything ranging from basketball to computer games"},{"s":64.15,"e":67.81,"t":"plus a smattering of more traditionally girly material as well."},{"s":69.05,"e":74.11,"t":"Coverage of team sports is at the heart of it. Anything about makeup or fashion is just peripheral."},{"s":75.03,"e":76.54,"t":"then there's my book"},{"s":77.11,"e":79.49,"t":"That was a quite different sort of challenge."},{"s":80.22,"e":84.67,"t":"It's on the subject of girls basketball and overall took about three months to do."},{"s":85.37,"e":96.25,"t":"I knew I wanted to write it late last year and started to loosely plan it out in January of this year. It wasn't until May that I had enough time to get down to doing everything I'd envisioned, but it was all done by the end of July.","uz":"Uni yozishni o'tgan yil oxirida xohlaganimni bilardim va bu yil yanvarda taxminiy reja tuzdim. Faqat mayga kelib, o'ylaganlarimni bajarishga vaqtim yetdi, iyul oxirida esa hammasi tayyor edi."},{"s":97.53,"e":108.48,"t":"In research in the book, I came across some pretty interesting facts. Like, women actually began playing basketball less than a year after the men's game was invented back in 1892."},{"s":109.08,"e":119.29,"t":"It didn't become an Olympic sport until 1976, however, whereas the men's game was in there from 1936. And that tells you a lot about how it developed."},{"s":120.82,"e":124.64,"t":"People ask me whether we'd recognise the game the way it started or if it's changed."},{"s":125.59,"e":128.25,"t":"Well, the biggest difference is in clothing."},{"s":129.11,"e":133.85,"t":"Then, in the USA, women were required to pay in full length dresses."},{"s":134.33,"e":138.17,"t":"The only body parts that could be exposed were fingers, necks and heads."},{"s":138.74,"e":145.85,"t":"And it wasn't only the discomfort they suffered, it led to quite a few broken bones, cos players tended to trip over their skirts and stuff.","uz":"Ular nafaqat noqulaylikdan aziyat chekishgan — bu ko'plab suyak sinishlariga ham olib kelgan, chunki o'yinchilar yubkalariga qoqilib ketishardi."},{"s":147.03,"e":149.6,"t":"Of course, no way did the men have these problems."},{"s":150.81,"e":159.2,"t":"Then, at the end of a woman's game, there'd be like handkerchiefs and hairpins scattered all over the court, which of course wasn't the case with the men either.","uz":"Ayollar o'yini oxirida esa maydonda ro'mollar va soch to'g'nag'ichlari sochilib yotardi."},{"s":160.02,"e":165.5,"t":"And so you can see how the two developed in quite different ways, even with a differently sized court for many years."},{"s":166.58,"e":169.92,"t":"Of course things did change but quite slowly really."},{"s":170.42,"e":172.86,"t":"appropriate clothing came in gradually."},{"s":173.66,"e":177.95,"t":"Even well into the 20th century some other rules apply to women but not to men."},{"s":178.87,"e":188.22,"t":"Not so much the equipment, but silly things like chewing gum were specifically prohibited in the women's game because it was considered unfeminine. Not because it was dangerous or anything.","uz":"Asbob-uskunalar emas, balki saqich chaynash kabi bema'ni narsalar ayollar o'yinida maxsus taqiqlangan edi, chunki bu ayolga xos emas deb hisoblangan."},{"s":189.02,"e":199.23,"t":"And I've got some good stories from those years in the book, I think. Like when in 1936, a team of women basketball players called the Red Heads toured the country playing exhibitions against men's teams."},{"s":199.99,"e":208.73,"t":"Stranging was though, these girls not only had to wear the same clothes, they all had to have red hair. Most of them had to dye it specially, isn't that unbelievable?"},{"s":209.72,"e":213.95,"t":"But looking back on the writing of the book, if I did it again, I'd do it all differently."},{"s":214.58,"e":218.27,"t":"I know I ought to be proud of what I've done, but I'm such a perfectionist.","uz":"Qilgan ishimdan faxrlanishim kerakligini bilaman, lekin men juda mukammallikka intiluvchiman."},{"s":218.78,"e":225.92,"t":"Given the chance, I'd add significantly more information on the cultural traditions and really address the growing basketball fanbase."},{"s":226.46,"e":229.34,"t":"But who knows? Maybe there's another book in there somewhere."},{"s":230.01,"e":231.9,"t":"Now, before I show you some of the"},{"s":235.64,"e":237.18,"t":"Now play the recording again."},{"s":239.96,"e":251.29,"t":"Hi, my name's Britt Foxton and I'm the founder of a website devoted to women's basketball and I've also just written a book on the same subject. But first up, let me tell you how I got started with the site."},{"s":252.09,"e":263.01,"t":"Although it really got going once I was at university, it actually started out as a high school project, you know, a design a website kind of thing. But it wasn't like anyone expected it to become real or anything."},{"s":263.83,"e":269.69,"t":"I designed a site about girls basketball which I was passionate about and called it femalebasket.com"},{"s":270.42,"e":275.58,"t":"I knew the name wasn't right and before it got really successful I changed it to Matchgirl.com"},{"s":276.12,"e":277.63,"t":"and that was a really good move."},{"s":278.68,"e":283.93,"t":"And although it started with basketball, the sites kind of evolved to include other games as well."},{"s":284.5,"e":291.13,"t":"It features a variety of articles, reviews and editorials on everything ranging from basketball to computer games"},{"s":291.67,"e":295.33,"t":"plus a smattering of more traditionally girly material as well."},{"s":296.57,"e":301.63,"t":"Coverage of team sports is at the heart of it. Any thing about makeup or fashion is just peripheral."},{"s":302.55,"e":304.03,"t":"Then there's my book."},{"s":304.63,"e":307.01,"t":"That was a quite different sort of challenge."},{"s":307.74,"e":312.19,"t":"It's on the subject of girls basketball and overall took about three months to do."},{"s":312.89,"e":317.69,"t":"I knew I wanted to write it late last year and started to loosely plan it out in January of this year."},{"s":318.2,"e":323.77,"t":"It wasn't until May that I had enough time to get down to do and everything I'd envisioned, but it was all done by the end of July."},{"s":325.05,"e":336.0,"t":"In research in the book, I came across some pretty interesting facts. Like, women actually began playing basketball less than a year after the men's game was invented back in 1892."},{"s":336.6,"e":346.81,"t":"It didn't become an Olympic sport until 1976, however, whereas the men's game was in there from 1936. And that tells you a lot about how it developed."},{"s":348.34,"e":352.16,"t":"People ask me whether we'd recognise the game the way it started or if it's changed."},{"s":353.11,"e":355.77,"t":"Well, the biggest difference is in clothing."},{"s":356.63,"e":361.37,"t":"Then, in the USA, women were required to pay in full length dresses."},{"s":361.85,"e":365.69,"t":"The only body parts that could be exposed were fingers, necks and heads."},{"s":366.26,"e":373.37,"t":"And it wasn't only the discomfort they suffered, it led to quite a few broken bones, cos players tended to trip over their skirts and stuff."},{"s":374.62,"e":377.12,"t":"Of course, no way did the men have these problems."},{"s":378.33,"e":386.72,"t":"Then, at the end of a woman's game, there'd be like handkerchiefs and hairpins scattered all over the court, which of course wasn't the case with the men either."},{"s":387.54,"e":393.02,"t":"And so you can see how the two developed in quite different ways, even with a differently sized court for many years."},{"s":394.17,"e":397.44,"t":"Of course things did change but quite slowly really."},{"s":397.94,"e":400.38,"t":"appropriate clothing came in gradually."},{"s":401.18,"e":405.47,"t":"Even well into the 20th century some other rules apply to women but not to men."},{"s":406.36,"e":415.74,"t":"Not so much the equipment, but silly things like chewing gum were specifically prohibited in the women's game because it was considered unfeminine. Not because it was dangerous or anything."},{"s":416.54,"e":426.75,"t":"And I've got some good stories from those years in the book, I think. Like when in 1936, a team of women basketball players called the Red Heads toured the country playing exhibitions against men's teams."},{"s":427.51,"e":436.25,"t":"Stranging was though, these girls not only had to wear the same clothes, they all had to have red hair. Most of them had to dye it specially, isn't that unbelievable?"},{"s":437.24,"e":441.5,"t":"But looking back on the writing of the book, if I did it again, I'd do it all differently."},{"s":442.1,"e":445.79,"t":"I know I ought to be proud of what I've done, but I'm such a perfectionist."},{"s":446.3,"e":453.47,"t":"Given the chance, I'd add significantly more information on the cultural traditions and really address the growing basketball fanbase."},{"s":453.98,"e":456.86,"t":"But who knows? Maybe there's another book in there somewhere."},{"s":457.53,"e":459.45,"t":"Now, before I show you some of the"}]},{"n":48,"title":"Volunteering in Africa","dur":416.7,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Elizabeth worked for a travel agency before she went to Africa."},{"k":"p","t":"Elizabeth first found out about working as a volunteer from a {1} she saw at the dentist's."},{"k":"p","t":"The course in London that Elizabeth attended was called {2}."},{"k":"p","t":"Elizabeth's job in Africa was to teach {3} how to market their goods."},{"k":"p","t":"On arrival in Africa, Elizabeth spent 3 weeks doing a training course with other volunteers."},{"k":"p","t":"Elizabeth used a {4} to travel short distances in Africa."},{"k":"p","t":"Elizabeth feels that she got on best with local women in the area of Africa where she lived."},{"k":"p","t":"Back in England, Elizabeth found that she was disturbed by the {5} in the city."},{"k":"p","t":"At the moment, Elizabeth buys and sells furniture from Africa."},{"k":"p","t":"Nowadays, Elizabeth spends more time on her favourite pastime, which is {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["poster"],"ps":50.36,"en":63.93,"si":7,"ev":"Then I was at the dentist one day waiting to go in and I'd read all the magazines in the waiting room so I started looking at a poster. It was all about volunteers working in Africa. And it interested you? Yes. I took down the name and address and applied.","hl":"poster","uz":"Bir kuni tish shifokorida navbat kutib o'tirgandim, kutish zalidagi barcha jurnallarni o'qib bo'lib, plakatga qaray boshladim. U Afrikada ishlaydigan ko'ngillilar haqida edi.","why":"Magazines — o'qib bo'lgan (tuzoq). Ma'lumot — poster."},{"a":["changes"],"ps":68.25,"en":81.6,"si":9,"ev":"Then just before I left for Africa, there was a training weekend in London which they call 'changes' and which gives you some idea of what you're letting yourself in for. What particular skills could you offer? I had a degree in economics and I'd done some teaching at one time.","hl":"changes","uz":"Afrikaga jo'nashimdan oldin Londonda \"Changes\" deb ataladigan o'quv dam olish kunlari bo'ldi — u nima kutayotgani haqida tasavvur beradi.","why":"Kurs nomi: Changes."},{"a":["farmers"],"ps":68.25,"en":87.01,"si":9,"ev":"Then just before I left for Africa, there was a training weekend in London which they call 'changes' and which gives you some idea of what you're letting yourself in for. What particular skills could you offer? I had a degree in economics and I'd done some teaching at one time. What they wanted to send me to Africa to do was to train local farmers in the marketing of their produce.","hl":"farmers","uz":"Qanday ko'nikmalarni taklif qila olardingiz? — Iqtisodiyot bo'yicha diplomim bor edi va bir vaqtlar o'qituvchilik qilganman. Meni Afrikaga mahalliy fermerlarni mahsulotlarini sotishga o'rgatish uchun yuborishmoqchi edi.","why":"\"Train local farmers in the marketing\" — fermerlar."},{"a":["motorbike"],"ps":119.54,"en":127.61,"si":17,"ev":"My area covered 1,200 square kilometers and I had a truck for long distance travel but for more local trips I rode a motorbike.","hl":"motorbike","uz":"Hududim 1200 kvadrat kilometr edi; uzoq safarlar uchun yuk mashinam bor edi, lekin yaqin joylarga mototsiklda borardim.","why":"Truck — uzoq masofa (tuzoq). Qisqa masofa — motorbike."},{"a":["traffic"],"ps":155.06,"en":170.69,"si":24,"ev":"I found the supermarkets especially overwhelming. Just the enormous choice of food. Also the traffic disturbed me. I had to move from my flat in the city to a small cottage in the country just to get some of the peace and quiet I'd become accustomed to in Africa. And what are you working on at the moment?","hl":"traffic","uz":"Ayniqsa supermarketlar meni dovdiratib qo'ydi — oziq-ovqatning ulkan tanlovi. Shuningdek, transport tirbandligi ham bezovta qildi.","why":"Supermarkets — \"overwhelming\". Bezovta qilgan — traffic."},{"a":["gardening"],"ps":198.46,"en":205.76,"si":32,"ev":"Oh yes, in many ways. I used to spend all my time working, but now I make sure I have more time for gardening, my favorite hobby.","hl":"gardening","uz":"O, ha, ko'p jihatdan. Avval butun vaqtimni ishga sarflardim, endi esa sevimli mashg'ulotim — bog'dorchilikka ko'proq vaqt ajrataman.","why":"\"Gardening, my favourite hobby\" — bog'dorchilik."}],"segs":[{"s":5.62,"e":10.21,"t":"You'll hear an interview with Elizabeth Holmes about her experience working in Africa."},{"s":20.76,"e":27.65,"t":"Visitors to the small Devon village of Wimple might be forgiven for looking twice as they passed the garden of Elizabeth Holmes."},{"s":28.5,"e":32.09,"t":"In the middle of the garden, there stands a traditional African hut."},{"s":32.66,"e":36.61,"t":"a reminder of the two years Elizabeth spent in Africa as a volunteer."},{"s":37.62,"e":43.01,"t":"Elizabeth, what persuaded you to leave your secure job in a travel agent and go to Africa?"},{"s":44.57,"e":46.21,"t":"been feeling restless for ages."},{"s":46.9,"e":49.89,"t":"I wanted to see the real world, not just tourist places."},{"s":50.36,"e":63.93,"t":"Then I was at the dentist one day waiting to go in and I'd read all the magazines in the waiting room so I started looking at a poster. It was all about volunteers working in Africa. And it interested you? Yes. I took down the name and address and applied.","uz":"Bir kuni tish shifokorida navbat kutib o'tirgandim, kutish zalidagi barcha jurnallarni o'qib bo'lib, plakatga qaray boshladim. U Afrikada ishlaydigan ko'ngillilar haqida edi."},{"s":64.57,"e":67.68,"t":"I had an interview locally and did some aptitude tests."},{"s":68.25,"e":81.6,"t":"Then just before I left for Africa, there was a training weekend in London which they call 'changes' and which gives you some idea of what you're letting yourself in for. What particular skills could you offer? I had a degree in economics and I'd done some teaching at one time.","uz":"Afrikaga jo'nashimdan oldin Londonda \"Changes\" deb ataladigan o'quv dam olish kunlari bo'ldi — u nima kutayotgani haqida tasavvur beradi."},{"s":82.33,"e":87.01,"t":"What they wanted to send me to Africa to do was to train local farmers in the marketing of their produce."},{"s":87.93,"e":93.57,"t":"I flew out with 15 other volunteers all going to do different things like nursing, teaching and so on."},{"s":94.3,"e":101.34,"t":"When we got there, we were supposed to have a four-week course at a training centre learning something about the local culture and the basics of the language, you know..."},{"s":101.78,"e":103.52,"t":"greetings and things like that."},{"s":104.31,"e":108.8,"t":"Anyway, there was a problem and it only lasted three weeks in the end. Not enough, really."},{"s":109.4,"e":112.22,"t":"Did it take a long time to get used to your new lifestyle?"},{"s":114.71,"e":118.85,"t":"difficult for the first few weeks, but after that I settled in very well."},{"s":119.54,"e":127.61,"t":"My area covered 1,200 square kilometers and I had a truck for long distance travel but for more local trips I rode a motorbike.","uz":"Hududim 1200 kvadrat kilometr edi; uzoq safarlar uchun yuk mashinam bor edi, lekin yaqin joylarga mototsiklda borardim."},{"s":128.73,"e":131.52,"t":"How did you get on with the local people? Very well."},{"s":132.09,"e":137.57,"t":"The men were very polite, but they tended to keep their distance, unlike the women who were always inviting me to meals."},{"s":138.1,"e":142.59,"t":"They showed me how they wove and dyed material to make clothes for themselves and their children."},{"s":143.1,"e":149.53,"t":"I used to get magazines sent from England and we'd spend ages looking at them. I expect you found it very different when you returned to England."},{"s":150.07,"e":151.81,"t":"Yes, I certainly did."},{"s":152.47,"e":154.62,"t":"After two years of living very simply,"},{"s":155.06,"e":170.69,"t":"I found the supermarkets especially overwhelming. Just the enormous choice of food. Also the traffic disturbed me. I had to move from my flat in the city to a small cottage in the country just to get some of the peace and quiet I'd become accustomed to in Africa. And what are you working on at the moment?","uz":"Ayniqsa supermarketlar meni dovdiratib qo'ydi — oziq-ovqatning ulkan tanlovi. Shuningdek, transport tirbandligi ham bezovta qildi."},{"s":171.22,"e":171.58,"t":"Well..."},{"s":172.12,"e":177.76,"t":"I didn't want to just go back to working in someone else's office, so I set up my own business which I run from home."},{"s":178.36,"e":180.0,"t":"ideal in African furniture."},{"s":180.86,"e":184.51,"t":"I bought some small pieces back with me as souvenirs and everyone loved them in Britain."},{"s":185.75,"e":189.5,"t":"However, I'm still in touch with the organisation that sent me to Africa as a volunteer."},{"s":190.17,"e":195.07,"t":"I organise events to raise funds and give talks about my experience to encourage other people to go."},{"s":195.64,"e":197.89,"t":"Has the experience in Africa changed you at all?"},{"s":198.46,"e":205.76,"t":"Oh yes, in many ways. I used to spend all my time working, but now I make sure I have more time for gardening, my favorite hobby.","uz":"O, ha, ko'p jihatdan. Avval butun vaqtimni ishga sarflardim, endi esa sevimli mashg'ulotim — bog'dorchilikka ko'proq vaqt ajrataman."},{"s":206.36,"e":210.17,"t":"Well, I'd like to thank Elizabeth for coming into the studio today."}]},{"n":49,"title":"This Evening's Programmes","dur":412.9,"lines":[{"k":"h","t":"7.30 pm 'Art Review': Student Art Exhibition"},{"k":"p","t":"This evening's programme is taking place at the National museum in London."},{"k":"p","t":"The exhibition is of work by students in the {1} year of their art course."},{"k":"p","t":"At the exhibition, you can see things as different as curtains and glass."},{"k":"p","t":"Some of the works of art have been made using {2} technology."},{"k":"h","t":"8.00 pm Play: 'The Vanishing Lady'"},{"k":"p","t":"In the play, a young couple on a train think they hear the sound of someone using a {3}."},{"k":"p","t":"A {4} tells the couple about an old lady whom he has seen."},{"k":"p","t":"After writing this play, the author, Porten, became a writer for films."},{"k":"h","t":"9.30 pm 'Business Scenes': Interview with Peter Field"},{"k":"p","t":"Peter used to work for a computer {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter says the material he uses for his boats is a particular kind of {6}."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter collects old maps as a hobby."}],"items":[{"a":["final"],"ps":49.34,"en":58.49,"si":3,"ev":"This year is no exception, as everything is the work of final year art students from a local college. You'll be surprised at the variety of things you can see.","hl":"final","uz":"Bu yil ham istisno emas: hamma narsa mahalliy kollejning bitiruvchi (oxirgi kurs) san'at talabalari ishi.","why":"\"Final year art students\" — oxirgi kurs."},{"a":["industrial"],"ps":66.81,"en":74.37,"si":5,"ev":"Many exhibits demonstrate how industrial technology can be employed in art.","hl":"industrial","uz":"Ko'plab eksponatlar sanoat texnologiyalarini san'atda qanday qo'llash mumkinligini ko'rsatadi.","why":"\"Industrial technology\" — sanoat texnologiyasi."},{"a":["gun"],"ps":98.39,"en":108.57,"si":8,"ev":"They're walking through a carriage on a train and suddenly hear a noise that sounds to them like a gun being fired.","hl":"gun","uz":"Ular poyezd vagonidan o'tib ketayotganda to'satdan o'q uzilgandek tovush eshitishadi.","why":"\"Like a gun being fired\" — qurol (to'pponcha)."},{"a":["waiter"],"ps":109.02,"en":127.97,"si":9,"ev":"Then in the restaurant car, they ask the first person they meet, who happens to be a waiter, if he also heard the sound. \"No,\" he says, and goes on to tell them that an old lady is in the carriage.","hl":"waiter","uz":"Keyin restoran vagonida duch kelgan birinchi odamdan — u ofitsiant bo'lib chiqadi — tovushni eshitganmi, deb so'rashadi. \"Yo'q\", deydi u va vagonda bir keksa ayol borligini aytadi.","why":"\"Who happens to be a waiter\" — ofitsiant."},{"a":["company"],"ps":160.66,"en":167.45,"si":15,"ev":"In 1995, Peter was a manager in a computer company, but he left that job to go on a world cruise.","hl":"company","uz":"1995-yilda Piter kompyuter kompaniyasida menejer bo'lgan, lekin dunyo bo'ylab kruizga chiqish uchun ishni tashlagan.","why":"\"A manager in a computer company\" — kompaniya."},{"a":["metal"],"ps":173.46,"en":189.05,"si":17,"ev":"Peter claims they will suffer no serious damage even if they hit an iceberg at full speed. It's all in the type of metal you use.","hl":"metal","uz":"Piterning aytishicha, ular to'liq tezlikda aysbergga urilsa ham jiddiy shikastlanmaydi. Gap qanday metall ishlatishingizda.","why":"\"The type of metal you use\" — metall."}],"segs":[{"s":6.36,"e":10.85,"t":"You'll hear an announcement about an evening's programmes on Radio Pearl."},{"s":20.02,"e":37.02,"t":"And now a look at some of this evening's programmes on Radio Pearl. At 7.30 we have Art Review, a programme which has first become a favourite among our listeners with its mix of in-depth reports on artistic events and revealing interviews with the artists who regularly come into the studio."},{"s":37.78,"e":48.67,"t":"Today we'll be going to London to the National Museum, which holds approximately five events a year, and this particular one is always popular because it features work by student artists."},{"s":49.34,"e":58.49,"t":"This year is no exception, as everything is the work of final year art students from a local college. You'll be surprised at the variety of things you can see.","uz":"Bu yil ham istisno emas: hamma narsa mahalliy kollejning bitiruvchi (oxirgi kurs) san'at talabalari ishi."},{"s":59.03,"e":66.21,"t":"Exhibits range from curtains to glasswork, and I understand there are a total of nearly 2,000 works on display."},{"s":66.81,"e":74.37,"t":"There is an excellent use of raw materials and of course many exhibits demonstrate how industrial technology can be employed in art."},{"s":75.19,"e":88.83,"t":"If you want to buy any of the exhibits, it will cost you anything from £25 up to £2,000. So, for more information on what can be seen, where and for how much, tune in to Radio Pearl tonight at 7.30."},{"s":89.91,"e":97.28,"t":"Then at eight there's another in our series of classic plays and tonight it's The Vanishing Lady starring Margaret Loudon."},{"s":98.39,"e":108.57,"t":"Briefly, two young people become caught up in a thrilling adventure when they're walking through a carriage on a train and suddenly hear a noise that sounds to them like a gun being fired."},{"s":109.02,"e":127.97,"t":"Then in the restaurant car, they ask the first person they meet, who happens to be a waiter, if he also heard the sound. \"No,\" he says, and goes on to tell them that an old lady is in the carriage.","uz":"Keyin restoran vagonida duch kelgan birinchi odamdan — u ofitsiant bo'lib chiqadi — tovushni eshitganmi, deb so'rashadi. \"Yo'q\", deydi u va vagonda bir keksa ayol borligini aytadi."},{"s":128.82,"e":130.91,"t":"But when they return, of course, she's gone."},{"s":131.61,"e":135.26,"t":"Some say the lady never existed, but others are sure they saw her."},{"s":135.86,"e":139.2,"t":"Who is telling the truth or is everyone on the train lying?"},{"s":139.67,"e":147.33,"t":"Find out at 8 o'clock tonight. It's a brilliant play by Porton and also his last before he moved on to writing for films."},{"s":148.57,"e":159.81,"t":"Finally, for those of you who like sailing, business scenes at 9.30pm brings you the unsinkable boat and a chance to meet its maker, Canadian businessman Peter Field."},{"s":160.66,"e":167.45,"t":"In 1995, Peter was a manager in a computer company, but he left that job to go on a world cruise.","uz":"1995-yilda Piter kompyuter kompaniyasida menejer bo'lgan, lekin dunyo bo'ylab kruizga chiqish uchun ishni tashlagan."},{"s":168.09,"e":172.93,"t":"He had wanted a stress-free life, but ended up back in the rat race building boats."},{"s":173.46,"e":189.05,"t":"His new company has many products including luxury boats costing from 1 to 2 million dollars which Peter claims will suffer no serious damage even if they hit an iceberg at full speed. It's all in the type of metal you use as he explains tonight."},{"s":189.66,"e":206.27,"t":"And we also hear about Peter's unusual collection. You would think that a man in his line of work would collect model boats and ships, rather than the old maps, which are his real passion. If you tune in this evening, you'll find out how he started his collection and how he hunts for items to add to it."},{"s":207.42,"e":208.83,"t":"to this afternoon's programs."}]},{"n":50,"title":"The Model Maker","dur":480.2,"lines":[{"k":"p","t":"Before becoming a model maker, Peter did a course in woodwork at a college."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter compares his job to the type of work done by a {1}."},{"k":"p","t":"In Peter's hardest job, he was given some {2} of the building to work from."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter's most enjoyable job was making a model of a theatre for an exhibition."},{"k":"p","t":"Most of Peter's work is exported to Japan and Canada."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter says his models look best when they have {3} light directed onto them."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter's model of Marney House measures 140 cm in height."},{"k":"p","t":"The Marney House model took a long time to make because it had so many {4} and roof tiles."},{"k":"p","t":"The roof tiles on the model of Marney House are made of {5}."},{"k":"p","t":"Peter uses watercolour paint to reproduce the effects of the weather and {6}."}],"items":[{"a":["detective"],"ps":63.0,"en":70.14,"si":7,"ev":"Actually, I think there's quite a lot in common between what I do and what a detective does. Tracking down clues, working things out...","hl":"detective","uz":"Aslida mening ishim bilan detektiv ishi o'rtasida ko'p umumiylik bor: izlarni topish, jumboqlarni yechish…","why":"\"What a detective does\" — detektiv."},{"a":["photos"],"ps":76.54,"en":86.3,"si":10,"ev":"They just gave me a few old photos to use, as there was no actual building to copy.","hl":"photos","uz":"Menga faqat bir nechta eski suratlarni berishdi, chunki nusxa ko'chiradigan binoning o'zi yo'q edi.","why":"\"A few old photos\" — suratlar."},{"a":["electric"],"ps":131.1,"en":143.74,"si":18,"ev":"The colours and details come out most clearly if there's electric light directly above them; daylight's too pale.","hl":"electric","uz":"Ranglar va tafsilotlar tepasida to'g'ridan-to'g'ri elektr chirog'i bo'lsa, eng yaxshi ko'rinadi; kunduzgi yorug'lik juda xira.","why":"Daylight — juda xira (tuzoq). Eng yaxshisi — electric light."},{"a":["windows"],"ps":173.05,"en":181.95,"si":22,"ev":"It actually took longer than any model I've ever done before, mainly because I had to do all of the 150 windows, a real test of patience.","hl":"windows","uz":"Bu men qilgan barcha maketlardan ko'proq vaqt oldi — asosan 150 ta derazaning hammasini qilishim kerak bo'lgani uchun. Haqiqiy sabr sinovi.","why":"\"All of the 150 windows\" — derazalar."},{"a":["paper"],"ps":189.3,"en":195.07,"si":24,"ev":"On top of that I had to make every single one of the thousands of roof tiles individually out of paper.","hl":"paper","uz":"Bundan tashqari, minglab tom plitkalarining har birini qog'ozdan alohida yasashim kerak edi.","why":"\"Out of paper\" — qog'ozdan."},{"a":["pollution"],"ps":220.7,"en":232.35,"si":28,"ev":"So I wash the outside of the model with watercolour, so that it looks as if over the years it's been affected by wind and rain, and also pollution of course.","hl":"pollution","uz":"Shuning uchun maketning tashqarisini akvarel bilan yuvaman — go'yo yillar davomida shamol, yomg'ir va, albatta, ifloslanish ta'sir qilgandek ko'rinsin.","why":"Wind and rain — ob-havo. Yana — pollution (ifloslanish)."}],"segs":[{"s":4.98,"e":10.75,"t":"You'll hear a man called Peter Welby, who makes small models of buildings, talking about his work."},{"s":23.51,"e":25.28,"t":"My job is model making."},{"s":25.72,"e":34.33,"t":"I make small copies of large buildings and other structures. It might seem a strange job, but I knew when I was at school that it was what I wanted to do."},{"s":34.84,"e":40.06,"t":"So I did a college course, not in art or architecture as you might expect, but in woodwork."},{"s":40.86,"e":45.82,"t":"Because of the concentration on fine detail it requires, it was ideal for a model maker."},{"s":46.39,"e":50.53,"t":"although later of course I had to adapt my skills to other materials as well."},{"s":51.64,"e":62.53,"t":"When I make a model of an old building, often original parts of the building have been damaged or even completely demolished over the years, so I have to work hard to find out what they must have been like."},{"s":63.0,"e":70.14,"t":"Actually, I think there's quite a lot in common between what I do and what a detective does. Tracking down clues, working things out...","uz":"Aslida mening ishim bilan detektiv ishi o'rtasida ko'p umumiylik bor: izlarni topish, jumboqlarni yechish…"},{"s":71.06,"e":72.93,"t":"I've done quite a few jobs now."},{"s":73.4,"e":75.97,"t":"The toughest commission I've ever had was from Ireland."},{"s":76.54,"e":86.3,"t":"I was asked to do a model of part of a large house which had burnt down years before. They just gave me a few old photos to use, as there was no actual building to copy."},{"s":86.81,"e":92.29,"t":"I've done all sorts of buildings since, everything from grand castles to the most ordinary farmhouse."},{"s":93.08,"e":96.83,"t":"The one I liked most though was where I had to rebuild a theatre."},{"s":97.37,"e":101.89,"t":"The original building was gone, but this time there were detailed drawings to work from."},{"s":102.62,"e":107.36,"t":"My model was then shown in an exhibition called 'All the Worlds are Stage' here in London."},{"s":108.12,"e":113.85,"t":"It was fun because I could go and look at it every day if I wanted to, see how people were reacting to it."},{"s":114.65,"e":124.73,"t":"Generally, though, I don't see my models again after I've delivered them, as 80 percent of them are shipped out to Japan or Canada, with the rest shared between England and France."},{"s":125.5,"e":130.59,"t":"I do try to give pretty careful instructions, however, about how the models should be displayed."},{"s":131.1,"e":143.74,"t":"the height at which they should stand, how large the space around them should be, and also about lighting, because the colours and details come out most clearly if there's electric light directly above them, daylights too pale."},{"s":145.88,"e":157.09,"t":"And that's particularly true of my most recent project, a model of a very interesting old building called Marnie House. The owners decided to open it to the public and wanted a model to display for visitors."},{"s":157.56,"e":168.57,"t":"The detail work was very challenging indeed, as I had to reduce the original to a model just 140 cm high, which is 76 times smaller than the real building."},{"s":169.14,"e":172.35,"t":"that small, yet everything has to be there."},{"s":173.05,"e":181.95,"t":"It actually took longer than any model I've ever done before, mainly because I had to do all of the 150 windows, a real test of patience.","uz":"Bu men qilgan barcha maketlardan ko'proq vaqt oldi — asosan 150 ta derazaning hammasini qilishim kerak bo'lgani uchun. Haqiqiy sabr sinovi."},{"s":182.65,"e":188.61,"t":"There were times, to be honest, when I found myself regretting the fact that I'd ever taken the project on in the first place."},{"s":189.3,"e":195.07,"t":"On top of that I had to make every single one of the thousands of roof tiles individually out of paper.","uz":"Bundan tashqari, minglab tom plitkalarining har birini qog'ozdan alohida yasashim kerak edi."},{"s":195.77,"e":201.44,"t":"Mind you, when I'd finished that process I knew the hardest part was over and that the rest would be quite fun."},{"s":201.98,"e":213.6,"t":"Doing things like the statues along the front was enjoyable because everyone's different. And I spent some happy hours playing around with colours to get the exact reproduction of the original interior walls."},{"s":214.2,"e":220.25,"t":"When I'd finished all that, the only remaining problem was that, of course, the whole thing looked like a model of a new building."},{"s":220.7,"e":232.35,"t":"So I did what I usually do, which is to carefully wash the outside of the model with watercolour, so that it looks as if over the years it's been affected by wind and rain, and also pollution of course."},{"s":233.14,"e":237.63,"t":"But the owners were very pleased with the result, and I'm glad I can go and see it from time to time."},{"s":238.26,"e":243.74,"t":"Model making is a great job and I'd recommend it to anyone with patience and an eye for detail."}]}];
